{"sessions":[{"position":"Barista","status":"In Progress","date":"2026-08-27T02:57:34.658Z","candidateInfo":{"phone":"3059653121","name":"Esther Perea","email":"esthersplatform@gmail.com"},"messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Esther! Welcome, and thank you for your interest in joining our team as a Barista at the brand-new Ellianos Coffee in Lehigh Acres, FL. Weâ€™re excited to get to know you!\n\nBefore we begin, please keep a couple of quick details in mind:\n- This interview consists of a maximum of **25 questions**, asked one at a time.\n- You are free to finish and submit your application at **any time** by pressing the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen, or simply by letting me know in the chat that you'd like to finish.\n\nTo kick things off with our first question: \n\n**What made you interested in applying to be a Barista with Ellianos Coffee?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would love to be a barista because I love making coffee at home and drinks, it is something I enjoy making!"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":33946,"keystrokes":147,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":18814,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":39,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thatâ€™s wonderful to hear, Esther! Having a genuine passion for making drinks is a great starting point. \n\nAt Ellianos, our motto is \"Italian Quality at America's Pace,\" which means pairing delicious coffee with a warm, welcoming smile for every customer who pulls up to our drive-thru. \n\n**How do you naturally go about making someone feel welcome or brightening their day when you meet them?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would greet customers with a smile, be friendly and welcoming, and ask how their day is going. Iâ€™d try to remember regular customerâ€™s orders and have a positive attitude so they leave feeling happier than when they came in!"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":82777,"keystrokes":251,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":63519,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":29,"pasteAttempts":1,"humanConfidence":72}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Remembering regular orders and greeting people with genuine warmth is such a huge part of what makes our guests keep coming backâ€”love that mindset, Esther!\n\nOur store layout is unique: itâ€™s an 800-square-foot double drive-thru kiosk. Because itâ€™s compact and fast-paced, our baristas are on their feet for their entire shift, constantly moving, bending, and occasionally lifting heavy supplies like 30-pound crates of milk or ice bags. \n\n**How comfortable are you with standing and staying physically active for long shifts, and how do you usually keep your energy up throughout the day?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I am comfortable for standing and staying active for long shifts. I"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":34524,"keystrokes":89,"maxInsertChunk":14,"responseDelayMs":37173,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":21,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"It looks like your message might have cut off at the end there! \n\nCould you share a bit more about how you usually maintain your energy and focus when you're working a long, busy shift on your feet?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I usually keep my energy up by staying hydrated, eating enough throughout the day, and keeping up with a positive attitude at work!"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":31574,"keystrokes":41,"maxInsertChunk":15,"responseDelayMs":7232,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":44,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hydration and proper nutrition make all the difference during a fast-paced shiftâ€”smart approach!\n\nBecause of our compact 800-square-foot setup, we operate with very lean teams on shift. That means every single team member is crucial, and an unexpected absence or tardiness directly impacts the entire drive-thru flow.\n\n**Do you have reliable transportation to the Lehigh Acres location, and how do you ensure you consistently arrive on time and ready for scheduled shifts?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes! My mother is able to take me or I can always call an uber."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":33218,"keystrokes":96,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":14089,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":27,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Having a reliable backup plan like Uber is great to know.\n\nNow, working in an 800-square-foot double drive-thru means working very closely with your teammates in a tight space while things move at lightning speed. You might have timers beeping, headsets buzzing, espresso shots pulling, and milk steaming all at once.\n\n**Can you tell me about a timeâ€”whether at school, work, or in your personal lifeâ€”where you had to multitask under time pressure? How did you keep yourself organized and calm?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"iâ€™ve had a time in school when I had multiple assignments needing to be turned in by a certain time frame. I stay organized by making a quick list and deciding what needed to be done and the things that are important the most. I try not to stress and work everything step-by-step!"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":69719,"keystrokes":87,"maxInsertChunk":20,"responseDelayMs":22695,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":46,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Prioritizing step-by-step and keeping a level head is a great strategy, Esther!\n\nIn our drive-thru, customers often have very specific drink modificationsâ€”like extra espresso shots, oat milk instead of whole milk, sugar-free syrups, or varying ice levels. At the same time, speed is essential so cars aren't waiting.\n\n**If youâ€™re making multiple customized drinks during a rush and realize you might have accidentally made one with regular milk instead of oat milk, what would you do?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I will stop and double check that the order is correct and if itâ€™s not then I would remake the drink correctly"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":15298,"keystrokes":21,"maxInsertChunk":16,"responseDelayMs":36669,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":86,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":89}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That demonstrates great integrityâ€”accuracy and food safety are top priorities, so remaking it is definitely the right call!\n\nNow, let's turn up the pressure just a bit. \n\nImagine it's morning peak rush. A customer pulls up to your window clearly irritated, complaining that they've been waiting in line for too long and that they are going to be late for work. \n\n**How would you handle this interaction to de-escalate their frustration, ensure they leave on a positive note, and still keep the drive-thru line moving quickly?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I will stay calm, friendly, I will apologize for the wait. I would keep the interaction, brief or respectful, and thank them for their patience, and take their order with a positive attitude!"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":56032,"keystrokes":159,"maxInsertChunk":14,"responseDelayMs":31653,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":35,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Staying calm, acknowledging their feelings, and moving swiftly is the perfect way to turn that experience around!\n\nNow, I'd like to test your prioritization and multitasking skills with a real-world peak rush scenario:\n\n**You are operating Window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for Window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you at Window A honks, asking for napkins.**\n\n**Walk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks step-by-step.**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would first acknowledge the customer at Window A and get the napkins for they can know that I heard them. I will communicate with the team that Window Bâ€™s order is coming in. I will prioritize tasks based on which needs to be started first and what can be handled by other team members. I will stay organized, communicate clearly, and avoid rushing for I donâ€™t make any mistakes."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":122332,"keystrokes":180,"maxInsertChunk":17,"responseDelayMs":38062,"tabSwitches":3,"wpm":34,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a spot-on approach, Esther! Handling the quick, 5-second napkin request immediately takes care of the customer right in front of you, while communicating over the headset ensures the team can start on items with longer prep times, like the hot grits bowls. Great teamwork and prioritization!\n\nSince Ellianos is open early in the morning through the evening, 7 days a week, having a flexible and reliable team is essential.\n\n**What does your typical weekly availability look like for shifts (e.g., early mornings, afternoons, evenings, weekends)? Are there any specific days or times you are unavailable?**"}]}],"id":"74b4c581-6f3c-4104-91ea-bf7262019fc2"},{"id":"02db5341-a934-4879-94f9-d285b519f675","emailSent":true,"candidateInfo":{"phone":"(239) 333-6198","name":"Emely Alejandre","email":"alejandreemely04@icloud.com"},"secondInterviewGuide":{"interviewerTips":["Profundizar amablemente en cada respuesta pidiendo ejemplos prÃ¡cticos con detalles de acciones y resultados, ya que la candidata tiende al laconismo.","Reconocer su autenticidad (100% de confianza en redacciÃ³n propia sin asistencia) y crear un ambiente de confianza que reduzca los nervios tÃ­picos de un primer empleo.","Evaluar el lenguaje corporal, la energÃ­a y la sonrisa natural mientras simula la interacciÃ³n de ventanilla con clientes de drive-thru."],"decision":{"hire":"Contratar si la candidata confirma disponibilidad semanal compatible para cierres/fines de semana, demuestra soltura y calidez verbal en inglÃ©s (bloque block_ingles >= 3.5/5), y evidencia una actitud coachable, enÃ©rgica y colaborativa en todos los bloques obligatorios (calificaciÃ³n global >= 3.8/5).","decline":"Descartar si presenta incompatibilidad horaria con los turnos operativos de la tienda, timidez extrema o incapacidad de comunicarse en inglÃ©s con clientes, o si muestra resistencia/incomodidad al ritmo fÃ­sico y la retroalimentaciÃ³n en vivo.","thirdConversation":"Considerar una breve conversaciÃ³n de alineaciÃ³n o prueba de turno si demuestra excelente actitud e inglÃ©s pero existen dudas menores sobre el ajuste fino de sus horarios escolares frente al calendario de turnos de la tienda."},"blocks":[{"id":"block_disp","title":"Disponibilidad Horaria y Confiabilidad Operativa","goal":"Determinar si sus restricciones de horario escolar o personal permiten cubrir los turnos clave de cierre y fines de semana sin riesgo de ausentismo.","minutes":10,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q1","q2"]},{"id":"block_presion","title":"Trabajo en Espacio Reducido y Multitarea bajo PresiÃ³n","goal":"Evaluar la capacidad de la candidata para operar a alta velocidad en un kiosco de 800 sq ft manteniendo la calma y el orden.","minutes":15,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q3","q4","q5"]},{"id":"block_ingles","title":"Customer Interaction & Drive-Thru Agility (English)","goal":"Verificar la fluidez verbal en inglÃ©s, dicciÃ³n por auricular y calidez en el trato rÃ¡pido de ventanilla.","minutes":10,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q6","q7"]},{"id":"block_cultura","title":"Coaching, Iniciativa y Cierre","goal":"Validar su receptividad al feedback correctivo en tiempo real y su motivaciÃ³n a largo plazo en la nueva apertura de Lehigh Acres.","minutes":10,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q8","q9"]}],"generatedAt":"2026-08-26T22:14:20.219Z","questions":[{"id":"q1","block":"block_disp","text":"En tu entrevista virtual mencionaste textualmente: 'during the week I am available around the evening and on weekends I am available to work anytime and on holidays it depends'. Â¿A partir de quÃ© hora exacta puedes llegar al kiosco de lunes a viernes y cÃ³mo coordinarÃ­as tus horarios si te asignan turnos de cierre que terminan a las 8:30 PM o dÃ­as festivos con alta afluencia?","language":"es","purpose":"Verificar con precisiÃ³n los rangos horarios reales y el compromiso con los turnos de cierre y feriados.","listenFor":["Horas de llegada claras y realistas compatibles con su rutina diaria o escolar.","DisposiciÃ³n concreta para trabajar turnos completos de cierre y fines de semana.","Plan de transporte sÃ³lido y consistente para llegar y retirarse del local."],"redFlags":["Incertidumbre o contradicciones sobre su horario de llegada entre semana.","Negativa rotunda a trabajar fines de semana o feriados de alta demanda.","Falta de transporte seguro para horarios nocturnos."]},{"id":"q2","block":"block_disp","text":"Durante la entrevista preguntaste sobre la edad mÃ­nima requerida ('is there a certain age i have to be'). Para conocer mejor tu etapa actual: Â¿estÃ¡s actualmente estudiando o combinando alguna otra responsabilidad, y cÃ³mo te organizas para que tus tareas personales nunca afecten tu puntualidad en el trabajo?","language":"es","purpose":"Aclarar su situaciÃ³n acadÃ©mica/personal y verificar sus mÃ©todos de organizaciÃ³n del tiempo.","listenFor":["Transparencia sobre su calendario escolar o compromisos externos.","HÃ¡bitos concretos de planificaciÃ³n (alarmas, agendas, preparaciÃ³n anticipada).","Conciencia de la responsabilidad que implica no fallar a un equipo reducido."],"redFlags":["Falta de claridad en su disponibilidad real o cambios constantes de horario.","Dependencia total de terceros sin plan de respaldo para traslados.","MinimizaciÃ³n del impacto de llegar tarde a un turno con equipo pequeÃ±o."]},{"id":"q3","block":"block_presion","text":"En la entrevista respondiste a un escenario complejo diciendo: 'First I would get window B's order down then give the car the napkins then I would start working on window B's order'. Imagina que mientras preparas esas bebidas complejas, la mÃ¡quina de espresso gotea y tu compaÃ±ero necesita pasar detrÃ¡s de ti en el pasillo estrecho del kiosco de 800 sq ft. Â¿CÃ³mo coordinas fÃ­sicamente tus movimientos y quÃ© le dices a tu compaÃ±ero en ese segundo?","language":"es","purpose":"Evaluar la conciencia espacial, agilidad de movimiento y comunicaciÃ³n de seguridad en pasillos estrechos.","listenFor":["Uso de llamadas de alerta verbal ('detrÃ¡s', 'paso caliente', 'cuidado').","Capacidad de mantener la calma motriz sin bloquear el paso a los compaÃ±eros.","PriorizaciÃ³n de la seguridad fÃ­sica sin detener por completo la producciÃ³n."],"redFlags":["Desconocimiento de la dinÃ¡mica fÃ­sica de una cocina/barra compacta.","Tendencia a paralizarse o frustrarse ante obstÃ¡culos simultÃ¡neos.","Silencio total o falta de comunicaciÃ³n verbal con el equipo."]},{"id":"q4","block":"block_presion","text":"Mencionaste que para resolver desacuerdos en grupo organizaste una votaciÃ³n en un proyecto escolar ('I stepped in and had everyone do a vote on a topic'). En una barra de cafÃ© no siempre hay tiempo de votar: si durante una hora pico hay confusiÃ³n entre dos baristas sobre quiÃ©n debe preparar un pedido y la fila de autos se acumula, Â¿cÃ³mo actuarÃ­as tÃº para destrabar la situaciÃ³n en 5 segundos?","language":"es","purpose":"Medir la capacidad de resoluciÃ³n prÃ¡ctica y rÃ¡pida en entornos donde no aplica el consenso pausado.","listenFor":["Iniciativa para asumir una tarea clara de inmediato ('yo saco las bebidas, tÃº toma la orden').","Enfoque en destrabar el cuello de botella antes de discutir responsabilidades.","Tono positivo, firme y colaborativo sin generar conflicto."],"redFlags":["Esperar a que otra persona resuelva mientras la fila se detiene.","Generar discusiones o culpar a compaÃ±eros en pleno rush.","Actitud pasiva o indiferente ante la acumulaciÃ³n de clientes."]},{"id":"q5","block":"block_presion","text":"Escribiste que tu mÃ©todo para aprender recetas rÃ¡pidas es 'doing it over and over until I get it right or studying it'. En Ellianos preparamos decenas de bebidas personalizadas con diferentes tipos de leche y jarabes. Â¿QuÃ© harÃ­as la noche antes de tu primer turno para asegurarte de dominar las recetas base al dÃ­a siguiente?","language":"es","purpose":"Evaluar el nivel de proactividad, disciplina de estudio y entusiasmo por dominar el menÃº de Ellianos.","listenFor":["DisposiciÃ³n concreta a repasar guÃ­as, tarjetas de memoria o recetarios.","Curiosidad y compromiso con la precisiÃ³n tÃ©cnica ('Italian Quality').","Reconocimiento de la importancia de no cometer errores en recetas."],"redFlags":["Esperar aprender Ãºnicamente por ensayo y error en el turno sin estudiar.","Falta de interÃ©s por los estÃ¡ndares y proporciones de las recetas.","Exceso de confianza no fundamentado."]},{"id":"q6","block":"block_ingles","text":"Let's imagine a car pulls up to Window A at our Lehigh Acres drive-thru. The driver seems rushed and asks: 'Hey, I've never been to Ellianos before, what is your most popular iced drink and can I get it fast?' How would you greet them with energy and guide them through a quick choice in under 15 seconds?","language":"en","purpose":"Verificar la naturalidad, calidez, pronunciaciÃ³n y rapidez de respuesta en inglÃ©s para atenciÃ³n al cliente.","listenFor":["Warm, energetic greeting and confident tone of voice.","Clear recommendation (e.g., signature specialty drink or iced mocha) described simply.","Concise and swift pace appropriate for drive-thru speed expectations."],"redFlags":["Inability to form a coherent sentence in English under conversational pressure.","Flat, hesitant, or barely audible tone of voice.","Taking excessively long to answer or freezing."]},{"id":"q7","block":"block_ingles","text":"In your online interview you mentioned that great customer service is 'greeting everyone with positive manner and with a smile'. If a customer comes back to the drive-thru upset because their drink was made with whole milk instead of almond milk, walk me through how you would handle that conversation directly in English.","language":"en","purpose":"Evaluar el manejo de quejas y la empatÃ­a en inglÃ©s en situaciones de tensiÃ³n.","listenFor":["Immediate and sincere apology acknowledging the mistake.","Proactive solution offering a fast remake right away.","Calm, respectful demeanor without arguing or showing irritation."],"redFlags":["Defensive attitude or blaming another coworker in front of the customer.","Struggling to find basic vocabulary to de-escalate the complaint.","Ignoring the customer's frustration."]},{"id":"q8","block":"block_cultura","text":"Mencionaste que te gusta recibir retroalimentaciÃ³n porque 'I can learn my mistakes and solve them'. CuÃ©ntame sobre alguna ocasiÃ³n reciente en la escuela, en tu casa o en alguna actividad donde alguien te corrigiÃ³ en el momento por hacer algo mal. Â¿QuÃ© sentiste en ese instante y quÃ© hiciste diferente despuÃ©s?","language":"es","purpose":"Comprobar la madurez emocional y la respuesta real ante la crÃ­tica constructiva inmediata.","listenFor":["AceptaciÃ³n madura del error sin resentimiento ni justificaciones defensivas.","AcciÃ³n concreta tomada para corregir el hÃ¡bito o la tÃ©cnica.","Agradecimiento genuino por la oportunidad de mejorar."],"redFlags":["Respuestas evasivas que niegan haber cometido errores.","Reacciones de molestia, orgullo herido o desinterÃ©s ante la correcciÃ³n.","RepeticiÃ³n del mismo error por falta de atenciÃ³n."]},{"id":"q9","block":"block_cultura","text":"Nuestra tienda de Lehigh Acres abre en octubre y buscamos personas comprometidas para construir el equipo fundador. Durante la prueba virtual vimos que respondiste todo con tus propias palabras y ritmo natural. Siendo 100% transparente: Â¿quÃ© es lo que mÃ¡s te motiva de tener este empleo y quÃ© esperas de nosotros como tu equipo de liderazgo?","language":"es","purpose":"Evaluar la honestidad, el compromiso con el proyecto de apertura y las expectativas mutuas de trabajo.","listenFor":["MotivaciÃ³n genuina por aprender, ganar experiencia y aportar al equipo.","Expectativas saludables de liderazgo (claridad en entrenamiento, respeto, apoyo).","Compromiso de permanencia y entusiasmo por la apertura de la tienda."],"redFlags":["Falta de interÃ©s palpable en el puesto o en la marca Ellianos.","Expectativas irreales sobre el esfuerzo que requiere un trabajo de ritmo acelerado.","Incertidumbre sobre su permanencia a corto plazo tras la apertura."]}],"focusPoints":["Verificar la compatibilidad estricta de su disponibilidad horaria (tardes entre semana y fines de semana) con los turnos de cierre y alta demanda del kiosco de Lehigh Acres.","Evaluar su soltura verbal, proyecciÃ³n de voz y dinamismo presencial, dado que sus respuestas escritas fueron sumamente breves y propias de un primer empleo.","Validar su capacidad de trabajo y coordinaciÃ³n motriz en un espacio fÃ­sico compacto de 800 sq ft con 4 a 6 baristas en simultÃ¡neo.","Confirmar su nivel de madurez e iniciativa personal para resolver problemas sin depender constantemente de supervisiÃ³n paso a paso."]},"position":"Barista","evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation Report\n\n**Candidate Name:** Emely Alejandre  \n**Position Applied For:** Barista (Lehigh Acres Location)  \n**Contact Information:** (239) 333-6198 | alejandreemely04@icloud.com  \n\n---\n\n### 1. Final Score: 74 / 100\n\nEmely presents as an earnest, coachable, entry-level candidate with a positive service mindset. While her responses are brief and reflect limited prior industry experience, she demonstrates logical task prioritization, receptive attitude toward coaching, and a willingness to learn. Her score is moderately tempered by limited weekday availability (evenings only) and minimal elaboration in her answers.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Summary of Strengths\n\n* **Coachable & Growth-Oriented:** Emely expressed a healthy, mature attitude toward receiving feedback on the fly, recognizing coaching as an opportunity to fix mistakes and improve.\n* **Sound Prioritization Logic:** When presented with a high-pressure multi-tasking scenario (taking a complex order, handling a customer asking for napkins, and prep), she correctly prioritized logging the order, quickly handling the immediate minor request (napkins), and proceeding with drink preparation.\n* **Customer-Centric Basics:** Understands fundamental service expectationsâ€”emphasizing friendly greetings, smiling, proactive communication, and prompt apologies when mistakes happen.\n* **Team-First & Practical Conflict Resolution:** Provided a practical example of taking initiative to resolve group indecision via a structured vote.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Summary of Weaknesses & Areas of Concern\n\n* **Availability Constraints:** Available primarily during weekday evenings and weekends, with conditional availability on holidays. Because drive-thru coffee operations rely heavily on peak early-morning shifts (starting ~5:30 AM), this restricts her placement to closing/weekend shifts.\n* **Very Brief / Underdeveloped Responses:** Her answers were short and required little detail, suggesting she may need structured guidance and hands-on onboarding to develop confidence and proactive communication on the floor.\n* **Limited Direct Experience:** Her background suggests an entry-level/first-time job seeker (evidenced by referencing school group projects and inquiring about minimum age requirements).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Authenticity Assessment\n\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** 100%\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer:** 100% (All responses scored 100%)\n* **Answers Below 35% Confidence:** None.\n* **Writing-Style Alignment:** The writing-style analysis **strongly agrees** with the typing metrics. Typing speeds ranged naturally between 8 and 30 WPM (with one short burst at 59 WPM), with zero paste attempts, zero tab switches, natural keystroke counts, and appropriate response delays. The conversational, concise, and unpolished tone is entirely consistent with genuine, unassisted human input.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Final Recommendation\n\n**Recommendation:** **Second Interview** (In-Person / Shift Fit Check)\n\n**Justification & Next Steps:**\n* Emely has the raw baseline traits (positivity, teachability, calm logic) to succeed in a Barista role.\n* An in-person interview is recommended to:\n  1. Confirm that her weekday evening and weekend availability aligns with the Lehigh Acres store's open scheduling needs (e.g., closing crew / weekend peak).\n  2. Gauge her energy, verbal communication, and presence in a live, face-to-face setting.","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Emely! Welcome to your interview for the Barista position at our brand-new Ellianos Coffee location in Lehigh Acres, FL. Weâ€™re thrilled to speak with you today!\n\nBefore we jump in, I want to share a few quick details about how our interview process works:\n- The full, expected interview consists of a maximum of **25 questions**.\n- You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by pressing the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know right here in the chat whenever you would like to conclude.\n\nWe take things one step at a time, so let's start with a simple question:\n\n**What excited you about applying to be a Barista with Ellianos Coffee today?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"what has me excited about applying to be a barista is the new experience and new opportunities"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":38643,"keystrokes":112,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":55074,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":26,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is wonderful to hear, Emely! We love welcoming team members who are eager to learn and take on new experiences. \n\nTo help me get to know you a bit better, thinking about your own everyday life or past experiences: **What does great customer service look like to you when you visit a coffee shop or restaurant as a customer?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"great customer service to me looks like greeting everyone with positive manner and with a smile"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":73283,"keystrokes":101,"maxInsertChunk":11,"responseDelayMs":21996,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":13,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"A smile and a warm greeting truly set the tone for someone's entire day! \n\nAs a Barista at Ellianos, our team stays very active. You will be on your feet moving quickly for your entire shift, bending, and occasionally lifting items like milk crates or ice buckets (up to 30 lbs). \n\n**How comfortable are you with a role that is this physically active and fast on your feet?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"yes I am comfortable with that role"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":21607,"keystrokes":47,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":26015,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":19,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is great to know! \n\nOur Ellianos stores operate as an 800-square-foot double drive-thru with very lean teams on shift. Because our team is small and tight-knit, every single team member is vitalâ€”if one person is late or absent, it deeply affects the whole flow. \n\n**Do you have reliable transportation to get to the Lehigh Acres location, and how do you ensure you are always consistently on time for your commitments?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"yes I do have reliable transportation and I am always on time by making sure I leave at a reasonable time from my house"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":91866,"keystrokes":146,"maxInsertChunk":14,"responseDelayMs":34612,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":16,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That planning ahead is so important, Emely!\n\nNow, let's talk a little about the workspace. Our building is a compact 800-square-foot double drive-thru. During peak morning rushes, you'll be working shoulder-to-shoulder with your teammates in a very fast-paced, high-energy environment. \n\n**How do you feel about working in tight, close quarters with others, and how do you keep communication positive and clear when things get super busy?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I feel good about working in tight close quarters with other and I keep communication positive and clear by using friendly tone and solving the problems"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":200585,"keystrokes":172,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":61198,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":8,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Keeping a friendly tone and focusing on solutions is a great mindset to have!\n\nCould you share a specific timeâ€”whether from school, a previous job, or a team activityâ€”where things were getting stressful or hectic, and you had to step in with clear communication to keep things running smoothly? What happened, and what was the outcome?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"when I was doing a group project everyone could not figure out what topic to choose so I stepped in and had everyone do a vote on a topic"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":69433,"keystrokes":184,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":49684,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":25,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Taking initiative to find a fair solution like a vote is a great way to keep a team moving forward!\n\nAt Ellianos, our motto is \"Italian Quality at America's Pace.\" That means baristas are often balancing multiple things at onceâ€”like remembering drink recipes, listening to drink modifications through a headset, and steaming milk simultaneously.\n\n**When you have to learn a lot of detailed information quickly or multitask, what methods or habits help you remember everything accurately?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"the methods that help me remember everything accurately is doing it over and over until I get it right or studying it"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":53785,"keystrokes":130,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":65191,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":25,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Repetition and studying are fantastic ways to build that muscle memory!\n\nIn our drive-thru, speed is essential, but sometimes mistakes can happen. Imagine a customer at your window lets you know their latte was made with regular whole milk instead of the oat milk they requested, and there is already a line of cars waiting behind them. \n\n**How would you handle this situation in the moment with the customer and your team?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would apologize to the costumer for the inconvenience and let my team know"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":28224,"keystrokes":55,"maxInsertChunk":17,"responseDelayMs":18715,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":30,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Apologizing right away and communicating clearly with your team is definitely the best first step to getting that remake started quickly!\n\nNow, let's put your multitasking and prioritization skills to the test with a real rush-hour scenario:\n\n**You are operating window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you honks asking for napkins. Walk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks.**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"First I would get window B's order down then give the car the napkins then I would start working on window B's order"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":88911,"keystrokes":148,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":76077,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":16,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Handling the quick napkin request right away helps resolve the immediate distraction so you can focus on building those drinks accurately!\n\nWe operate seven days a week, often with early morning opening shifts (sometimes starting around 5:30 AM) through the afternoon rush and closing shifts. \n\n**What does your weekly availability look like, and are you available to work early mornings, weekends, or holidays?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"during the week I am available around the evening and on weekends I am available to work anytime and on holidays it depends"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":109168,"keystrokes":137,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":20480,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":13,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you for sharing your availability details, Emely!\n\nDuring busy shifts, shift leaders and teammates often provide quick, real-time coaching or reminders on drink recipes, speed, and technique right on the floor. \n\n**How do you typically like to receive constructive feedback or coaching when you're learning something new on the fly?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I like to receive feedback when im learning something new because I can learn my mistakes and solve them"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":53558,"keystrokes":140,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":18862,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":21,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a fantastic attitude to haveâ€”viewing feedback as an opportunity to grow makes all the difference!\n\nAt Ellianos, keeping our 800-square-foot store spotless and organized is essential for safety and speed. When there is a lull or downtime between rushes, our baristas don't just wait around.\n\n**What kind of tasks or duties would you naturally look for to stay productive and keep the store clean and prepped during those slower moments?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"the task I would look for is always cleaning up after to avoid accidents"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":55387,"keystrokes":82,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":30434,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":15,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Keeping a tidy station definitely prevents slips, spills, and mix-ups, especially in a fast-paced environment!\n\nWe have covered all the key aspects of the Barista role today. Before we wrap up, **is there anything else you would like us to know about you, or do you have any questions for me about working at Ellianos Coffee in Lehigh Acres?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"is there any benefits"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":12966,"keystrokes":43,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":31554,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":19,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Great question! At Ellianos Coffee, typical benefits for our team members include:\n\n- **Free and discounted drinks/food:** Enjoying your favorite beverages during your shift and team discounts on days off.\n- **Tip sharing:** Earning extra hourly income through our shared tip pool from drive-thru customers.\n- **Flexible scheduling:** Working around school, family, or other commitments when possible.\n- **Growth and advancement opportunities:** Opportunities to move up into Shift Lead, Assistant Manager, or Store Manager positions as our brand expands.\n\n*Specific packages (such as any additional health or PTO benefits for full-time roles) will be discussed in full detail with the franchise management team during the offer stage.*\n\nDo you have any other questions for me, or are you ready to submit your application?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"is there a certain age i have to be"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":9079,"keystrokes":36,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":27310,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":59,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"At Ellianos Coffee, team members generally need to be at least **16 years old** to work as a Barista due to equipment safety guidelines and scheduling laws.\n\nDoes that work for you, and do you have any other questions today, or are you ready to submit your application?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"yes that works and im ready to submit my application"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":19763,"keystrokes":48,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":7627,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":30,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you so much for taking the time to interview with us today, Emely! It was a pleasure learning more about you, your positive attitude, and your interest in joining our new Lehigh Acres team.\n\nOur hiring management team will review your interview responses and follow up with you regarding the next steps in the hiring process.\n\nTo finalize and send in your application, please go ahead and click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen now. \n\nWe wish you the very best and hope you have a wonderful rest of your day!"}]}],"date":"2026-08-26T21:48:19.526Z","status":"Completed"},{"position":"Barista","status":"In Progress","id":"c9376f8d-f5d5-4484-9143-9bf18ced33cf","date":"2026-08-26T20:00:06.569Z","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Kianna! Welcome to your interview for the Barista position at our brand-new Ellianos Coffee location in Lehigh Acres, Florida. We are excited to connect with you today!\n\nBefore we get started, I want to share a few quick details about how our interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of 25 questions, taken one at a time.\n- You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the \"Submit\" button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know right here in the chat whenever you would like to conclude.\n\nTo kick things off with a simple question: What made you interested in joining the Ellianos Coffee team here in Lehigh Acres?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I love coffee plus Iâ€™m right next door."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":8207,"keystrokes":46,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":10443,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":58,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Living right next door is fantastic! Being so close certainly helps with keeping a smooth commute. \n\nBecause we operate in a double drive-thru kiosk with lean, tight-knit teams, every single team member's presence is vital to our daily flow. How would you describe your overall track record with punctuality and reliability when it comes to work or school commitments?"}]}],"candidateInfo":{"phone":"2396001090","name":"Kianna ruiz","email":"kianna_ruiz@yahoo.com"}},{"candidateInfo":{"phone":"2396286353","name":"Cordalia campbell","email":"campbellcordalia540@gmail.com"},"emailSent":true,"position":"Barista","status":"Completed","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Cordalia! Welcome, and thank you for your interest in joining our team as a Barista at the brand-new Ellianos Coffee in Lehigh Acres, FL! We're excited to learn more about you today.\n\nBefore we get started, I want to share a few quick details about how this interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a **maximum of 25 questions**, asked one at a time.\n- You are in full control: you can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen, or by simply telling me in the chat that you would like to finish.\n\nLet's begin with something simple to kick things off:\n\n**What excited you about applying to Ellianos Coffee, and what do you enjoy most about working with and serving people?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"What excites me is working with new people and learning to make different drinks that I havenâ€™t made before"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":36343,"keystrokes":111,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":20844,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":31,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thatâ€™s wonderful to hear! We love a strong willingness to learn, and crafting our signature drinks is a big part of the fun here.\n\nMany of our guests are stopping by first thing in the morning to start their day. **How do you make sure you bring a positive, welcoming energy to every customer you interact with, even if youâ€™re having a busy or tiring morning?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Well first I make sure I always have a smile on my face and then I welcome everyone in with a Goodmorning or good afternoon to start they day off great"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":38118,"keystrokes":163,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":13123,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":49,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"A bright smile and a warm greeting make such a big difference in someone's day!\n\nOur baristas are constantly on the move inside our drive-thru kiosks. Shifts involve standing and moving on your feet for several hours at a time, bending, reaching, and occasionally lifting items like milk crates or ice buckets weighing up to 30 lbs. \n\n**How comfortable are you with this level of physical activity during a fast-paced shift?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™m very comfortable"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":10639,"keystrokes":14,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":10394,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":17,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That's great to know! \n\nOur drive-thru model relies on a small, tight-knit team working together on every shift. Because our staffing is lean, every single team member is crucialâ€”if someone is late or absent, it directly impacts the entire team and our speed of service.\n\n**Do you have reliable transportation to get to work consistently, and what steps do you take in your personal routine to ensure you always arrive on time for your scheduled shifts?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes I have reliable transportation and I always make sure I leave home in time so I can make it to work at least 10 or 15 minutes early"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":31526,"keystrokes":133,"maxInsertChunk":12,"responseDelayMs":9147,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":55,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Arriving 10 to 15 minutes early is a fantastic habit and shows great reliability!\n\nOur Ellianos location is an 800-square-foot double drive-thru building. That means itâ€™s a very compact, fast-paced environment where multiple team members are moving around each other quickly with hot espresso, steaming pitchers, and cold drinks.\n\n**How do you handle working in tight quarters with a team, and how do you make sure you communicate clearly and safely with your coworkers when things get busy?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Well first by staying in position and making sure everything runs smooth second by communicating with coworkers about what Iâ€™m doing"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":36868,"keystrokes":121,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":17995,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":34,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Staying in your zone and calling out your movements definitely keeps the flow smooth and safe!\n\nAt Ellianos, our motto is \"Italian Quality at America's Pace,\" meaning speed and accuracy have to go hand-in-hand. You might be memorizing recipe ratios, listening to an order over a headset, and preparing multiple drinks back-to-back.\n\n**Can you share a specific example from your past work, school, or daily life where you had to remember multiple details at once under a tight deadline? How did you keep everything straight?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Working at Dunkinâ€™ Donuts I had to take orders make drinks and also cash the customers out it was a tight deadline because we donâ€™t want are numbers to be high I just stayed focused and contuining doing my job"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":58861,"keystrokes":209,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":14363,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":41,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Having experience at Dunkin' Donuts is a huge plus! You already understand the importance of drive-thru timers and juggling multiple stations.\n\nSometimes, despite our best efforts during a rush, an order might be made incorrectly, or a customer might realize they wanted almond milk instead of whole milk after taking a sip at the window. \n\n**How would you handle a situation where a customer is frustrated about an incorrect drink, balancing making them happy with keeping the drive-thru line moving quickly?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Well first I would apologize and then I would offer to remake there drink or give them a coupon on us to make things right so the customer could come back"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":38006,"keystrokes":169,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":13810,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":49,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a great approachâ€”acknowledging the mistake quickly and making it right keeps trust high and moves things along efficiently!\n\nNow, let's step up the challenge with a fast-paced scenario you might encounter on a busy shift:\n\n**You are operating Window A's espresso station. Through your headset, an order for Window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you honks, asking for napkins. Walk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks.**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Well first I will give the customer the napkins then I would take the order in the headset and while there ordering Iâ€™ll be making drinks so when they come to window they could pay and go"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":41121,"keystrokes":201,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":69468,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":54,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Quickly handing over the napkins resolves the immediate customer right in front of you, while multitasking the headset and drink prep keeps the line flowingâ€”smart thinking!\n\nSince our drive-thru opens very early in the morning and operates seven days a week, scheduling flexibility is key. \n\n**What does your general availability look like throughout the week (including early mornings, afternoons, and weekends), and are there any specific days or times you cannot work?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Open availability"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":4315,"keystrokes":9,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":13811,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":28,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Having completely open availability is fantastic for our team scheduling!\n\nWe have covered all the key topics today regarding the Barista role at our Lehigh Acres location. \n\n**When would you be ready to start if offered the position, and do you have any questions for me about working at Ellianos Coffee?** \n\n*(Remember, whenever you feel ready, you can hit the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen to complete your application!)*"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"As soon as possible"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":5645,"keystrokes":17,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":14686,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":43,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is fantastic, Cordalia! Ready to start as soon as possible is exactly what we like to hear.\n\nThank you so much for taking the time to share your background, drive-thru experience, and positive attitude with us today. You did a wonderful job walking through our questions and scenarios. \n\nOur hiring team will be reviewing your responses for the Lehigh Acres branch. To officially complete and send in your application, please go ahead and click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen now.\n\nHave a wonderful day, and we wish you the best of luck!"}]}],"id":"b4cc372d-37d4-4853-99fe-ce753bbbd635","evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation: Barista â€“ Ellianos Coffee (Lehigh Acres)\n\n**Candidate Name:** Cordalia Campbell  \n**Contact:** campbellcordalia540@gmail.com | (239) 628-6353  \n**Position:** Barista  \n\n---\n\n### 1. Final Score: 88 / 100\n\nCordalia is an ideal fit for the fast-paced drive-thru barista role. She brings prior coffee drive-thru experience from Dunkin' Donuts, understands drive-thru metrics and multi-tasking under pressure, maintains a customer-first mindset, and offers completely open scheduling availability.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Summary of Strengths\n\n* **Directly Relevant Experience:** Possesses hands-on drive-thru coffee experience at Dunkinâ€™ Donuts, demonstrating familiarity with drive-thru timer goals, recipe execution, and operating POS registers concurrently.\n* **Sound Multitasking & Logic Under Pressure:** Correctly prioritized a multi-step scenario (handling the immediate customer at the window first, taking the headset order, and beginning drink preparation simultaneously).\n* **Teamwork & Safety Consciousness:** Understands how to work safely in tight quarters by staying in her designated station (\"staying in position\") and maintaining vocal communication with coworkers.\n* **Reliability & Schedule Flexibility:** Reports having reliable transportation, a habit of arriving 10â€“15 minutes early, completely open availability, and immediate readiness to start.\n* **Positive Customer Service Orientation:** Understands the importance of positive morning greetings, maintaining a welcoming attitude, and de-escalating customer dissatisfaction with apologies and drink remakes.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Summary of Weaknesses & Areas of Concern\n\n* **Brief Responses:** Her answers were short and straightforward. While sufficient for high-volume quick service, she did not elaborate deeply on detailed barista craft skills.\n* **Engagement / Inquisitiveness:** Did not ask any closing questions regarding the store culture, training, or operations when prompted at the end of the interview.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Authenticity Assessment\n\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** **99.2%**\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer:** **Response 9 (92%)** (WPM: 54, 1 tab switch, 69.5s delay).\n* **Answers Below 35% Confidence:** **None**.\n* **Writing-Style & Behavioral Analysis:**  \n  The typing metrics strongly align with human authorship. WPM ranged realistically between 17 and 55 WPM with zero paste attempts across all responses. The conversational tone, natural phrasing, and consistent sentence structure throughout confirm authentic, real-time responses without external assistance or AI generation.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Final Recommendation\n\n**Recommendation:** **Hire** (or Advance to Final In-Person Onboarding Interview)\n\nCordalia meets all core requirements for a fast-paced Ellianos drive-thru barista. Her previous experience at Dunkin' Donuts ensures a minimal learning curve for speed of service, drive-thru headset communication, and basic drink prep. Combined with her 100% open availability and immediate start timeline, she is a high-priority candidate for the Lehigh Acres opening.","date":"2026-08-25T23:57:47.503Z"},{"evaluation":"# Candidate Interview Evaluation\n\n**Candidate Name:** Justyn Cifuentes-Cetina  \n**Position Applied For:** Barista â€“ Lehigh Acres Location  \n**Contact:** 239-850-3178 | cjustyn564@gmail.com  \n\n---\n\n## 1. Overall Score: 90 / 100\n\nJustyn demonstrates strong potential as a Barista at Ellianos Coffee. He exhibited excellent prioritization logic, a customer-first mindset, grounded composure under stress, and coachability. His responses were thoughtful, practical, and aligned with Ellianos' core operating values.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Strengths\n\n* **Exceptional Prioritization & Operational Logic:** In the drive-thru simulation (Response 8), Justyn demonstrated strong instincts: resolving the immediate 5-second customer request (napkins at Window A to de-escalate honking), starting the longest preparation item (grits in the heater), and preparing drinks while the food heated.\n* **Positive, Service-Oriented Attitude:** Understands the importance of morning interactions (eye contact, warm smile, empathy) and handles customer mistakes (remaking drinks without hesitation or defensiveness).\n* **Team-First & Grounded Demeanor:** Values communication and remaining calm under pressure, emphasizing teamwork and supporting struggling peers without compromising overall workflow.\n* **Coachability & Growth Mindset:** Explicitly welcomes constructive floor coaching to optimize efficiency, showing an eagerness to learn food/beverage prep and high-volume operations.\n* **Proximity & Punctuality:** Resides close to the Lehigh Acres store with reliable transportation and can start immediately.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Weaknesses & Areas of Concern\n\n* **Availability Constraints:** Scheduled for college classes Monday through Thursday mornings, which restricts him from working weekday morning rush shifts. However, his full afternoon availability and open Fridayâ€“Sunday schedule fit afternoon and weekend rush coverage.\n* **Entry-Level Food & Beverage Experience:** Lacks prior formal barista or commercial food preparation experience. He will need structured training to build recipe muscle memory and speed on the espresso bar.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Final Recommendation: **HIRE**\n\n**Recommendation:** **Hire** (Part-Time / Shift-Aligned)  \nJustyn is an eager, coachable, and level-headed candidate whose positive attitude and logical thinking make him a great fit for the Lehigh Acres opening team. His availability is well-suited for weekday afternoon/closing shifts and full weekend shifts.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Authenticity Assessment\n\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** **92.0%**\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer(s):** Response 11 and Response 12 (**76%**)\n* **Responses Below 35% Confidence:** None.\n* **Typing & Behavioral Metrics Analysis:**\n  * **Typing Cadence & Keystrokes:** Organic typing speeds ranging from 8 to 35 WPM. High keystroke-to-character ratios (e.g., 687 keystrokes for 365 characters in Response 6) demonstrate active real-time editing and natural composition.\n  * **Paste / Insertion Events:** **0 paste attempts** and small maximum insert chunks throughout the entire session.\n  * **Tab Switches:** Minimal tab switches (1â€“3 on a few responses), typical of normal window management during an interview.\n* **Writing Style Agreement:** The qualitative writing analysis fully **agrees** with the high confidence scores. Justynâ€™s writing features natural phrasing, conversational pacing, minor authentic grammatical quirks, and consistent personal voice throughout. There are no indications of automated, AI-generated, or copied text.","candidateInfo":{"phone":"2398503178","name":"Justyn Cifuentes-Cetina","email":"cjustyn564@gmail.com"},"position":"Barista","date":"2026-08-25T20:03:28.473Z","status":"Completed","emailSent":true,"messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Justyn! Welcome, and thank you for your interest in joining the team at our brand-new Ellianos Coffee location in Lehigh Acres! Weâ€™re thrilled to have you here today.\n\nBefore we get started, I want to share a few quick details about how this interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of **25 questions**, asked one at a time.\n- You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen, or you can simply let me know in the chat whenever you'd like to finish.\n\nTo kick things off simply: **What made you excited to apply to be a Barista with us here at Ellianos Coffee?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Working with coffee is something that I enjoy already doing. The smell of coffee is comforting and it can give people that extra kick. Also, Ellianos Coffee is close by so, commuting their won't be a problem."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":203684,"keystrokes":462,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":32643,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":11,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":84}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That's wonderful to hear, Justyn! Having a genuine love for coffee and living close by are both fantastic pluses. \n\nAt Ellianos, our motto is \"Italian Quality at America's Pace,\" and our customers often look to us to set a positive tone for their entire day. \n\n**What does great customer service look like to you when interacting with someone ordering their morning coffee?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Making eye contact, having a smile on your face, showing genuine compassion to customers by making them feel welcome. A positive interaction early in the morning can have a positive effect on the rest of their day."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":118243,"keystrokes":367,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":15026,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":19,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"I love that mindset, Justynâ€”a friendly smile and genuine warmth truly can make someone's entire day.\n\nOur stores are compact, 800-square-foot double drive-thru kiosks designed for high speed and volume. The job is very active: you'll be on your feet for entire shifts, moving quickly in a small space, and occasionally lifting items like milk crates or ice bags (up to 30 lbs).\n\n**How comfortable are you with being on your feet and staying physically active for an entire shift?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Extremely comfortable for being both being on my feet and staying physically active for my entire shift.  I prefer to be on my feet rather than sitting down for long periods of time."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":240690,"keystrokes":410,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":11830,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":8,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That active energy is exactly what thrives in our drive-thru environment!\n\nBecause our kiosks are compact, we operate with lean, tightly-knit teams. If even one team member is late or absent, it immediately impacts the rest of the crew and slows down our drive-thru times. \n\n**Could you tell me about your typical routine for ensuring you are consistently on time for your commitments, and do you have reliable transportation to get to your shifts regardless of the time of day?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I go to college from Monday to Thursday, but I scheduled my classes to be early in the morning, to be finished early in the morning. I have the entirety of the afternoon and morning's to on Fridays and Saturdays.  Possibly sundays as well. Also, I have access to reliable transportation."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":170202,"keystrokes":394,"maxInsertChunk":14,"responseDelayMs":34113,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":18,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That flexibility and reliable transportation are great to know, Justyn. Thank you for sharing your schedule with me.\n\nSince our drive-thru gets very busyâ€”especially during morning and afternoon rushesâ€”you'll often be listening to orders over a headset, pulling espresso shots, steaming milk, and keeping track of multiple drinks in your head all at once.\n\n**Can you share an example of a time (at school, work, or in daily life) when you had to manage multiple tasks at the same time under a tight deadline? How did you keep everything organized without getting overwhelmed?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"While I was still in High-School I had multiple projects due the same week. I read through the syllabus for each, organized them based on specific deadlines, how lengthy they were, and what they consisted of. By me organizing them into a specific folder, I finished them by priority and knew exactly what had to be done first. That kept me from overwhelming myself."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":255713,"keystrokes":687,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":42285,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":15,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a great example of breaking things down into actionable steps to avoid stress! Prioritization is essential here.\n\nWorking in an 800-square-foot double drive-thru kiosk means you will be working shoulder-to-shoulder with 2 to 4 other baristas during fast, loud rushes. Effective communication and spatial awareness are critical to keep things running smoothly and avoid bumping into each other.\n\n**How do you handle communication with teammates when things get fast-paced and stressful? Can you give an example of how you support a teammate who might be falling behind?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"How I handle communication with teammates when things are starting to get fast-paced and potentially stressful is by using the grounding technique.  Getting overwhelmed could easily happen but we need to remember, where we are. We are not alone but in this together.  An example of how to support a teammate who might be falling behind is by assisting them in ways which I can that won't jeopardize other teammates. So we can both can back on track."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":303436,"keystrokes":690,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":13298,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":15,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That team-first mindset is essential when everyone is sharing such a compact workspace!\n\nNow, letâ€™s put your multitasking and prioritization skills to the test with a real-world drive-thru scenario:\n\n**You are operating Window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for Window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you at Window A honks asking for napkins. Walk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks.**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"First, I would get the napkins and with a smile on my face, quickly give it to the car at window A. It's a quick 5 second and it will make the customer happy while also stopping the honking. Second, I would start with the two hot grits bowls because it'll take a while to heat up and in the mean time, I start making the Lotus Edge energy drinks."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":202066,"keystrokes":539,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":80310,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":21,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is spot-on logic, Justyn. Taking care of the immediate 5-second fix at Window A prevents an escalation, and getting the grits heating immediately allows you to multitask efficiently while preparing the Lotus drinks.\n\nAttention to detail and quality consistency are vital to \"Italian Quality.\" With customers frequently requesting milk alternatives, sugar-free syrups, or specific flavor pumps, accuracy is critical. \n\n**If a customer comes back to the window saying their drink tastes wrong or wasn't made with the oat milk they requested, how would you handle the situation to make sure they leave happy and satisfied?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would happily remake the person's drink and keep in mind for the future to double check the ingredients asked for, and the ingredients quality."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":54176,"keystrokes":202,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":30552,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":28,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That positive attitude and willingness to own the solution right away make a huge difference in guest recovery.\n\nIn our drive-thru, speed is a major focus alongside quality, so shift leaders often provide real-time feedback on the floor (like coaching you to tweak your steaming technique, adjust pump counts, or move a little faster during a rush).\n\n**How do you typically receive constructive feedback or direct coaching in the moment, especially when things are moving fast?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I love receiving constructive feedback because it is called constructive feedback for a reason. If there are ways to help me maximize efficiency, I'm all ears."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":45199,"keystrokes":194,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":18453,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":35,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That coachable attitude is fantastic to have, Justyn!\n\nAs we look toward opening our new Lehigh Acres location, we're building a team that can grow with us. \n\n**What are your personal goals or expectations for this role at Ellianos, and if selected, how soon would you be available to start training?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"My personal goals for my role as a Barista would be to getting an understanding of food and beverage preparation, getting  experience in customer service, and how it's like to work in a fast-paced environment especially working as a collective team."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":129057,"keystrokes":319,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":22058,"tabSwitches":3,"wpm":19,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Those are fantastic goals, Justyn! Ellianos is a great place to build those exact foundational skills in food and beverage prep, teamwork, and fast-paced customer service.\n\nTo finalize our notes: **If selected, what is the earliest date you would be available to start, and do you have any questions for me about the role or the Lehigh Acres store?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I can start early as friday this week for training. To officially start working, the very first day Ellianos Coffee opens up. I have one question. What is the biggest challenge first-time barista's face?"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":224173,"keystrokes":382,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":25392,"tabSwitches":3,"wpm":9,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is an insightful question, Justyn! \n\nFor first-time baristas, the biggest challenge is usually building the **muscle memory and sensory multitasking** needed during peak drive-thru rushes. In the beginning, memorizing all the recipe ratios, pump counts, and milk-steaming temperatures while listening to new orders over a headset and interacting with cars can feel like a lot to juggle at once. \n\nHowever, because we have thorough hands-on training and a supportive team environment, baristas usually find that within a couple of weeks, that coordination becomes second nature!\n\n---\n\nYou have answered all of our core interview questions thoroughly, and your availability to start as early as this Friday is noted.\n\nWhenever you are ready, please click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen to finalize your application. \n\nThank you so much for your time, energy, and thoughtful answers today, Justyn! Our hiring team will review your interview for the Lehigh Acres location and be in touch soon. Have a wonderful rest of your day!"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"12/25 questions remaining? Am I good to go?"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":38579,"keystrokes":85,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":21310,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":12,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Yes, you are all set and good to go, Justyn! \n\nThe 25-question mark is simply the *maximum* limit for the interview. You have covered all of our key topics and scenarios thoroughly and shared everything we need to evaluate your application.\n\nPlease go ahead and press the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen to send everything over to our hiring team. \n\nThank you again for your time, and we wish you the best of luck with the Lehigh Acres store!"}]}],"id":"4facc8f9-49f8-4797-89f4-f9d9f6b9f2e7"},{"position":"Barista","status":"Completed","date":"2026-08-25T19:32:46.897Z","evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation: Barista â€” Ellianos Coffee (Lehigh Acres)\n\n**Candidate Name:** Katherine Perez  \n**Contact:** (239) 823-6507 | perezk2004@icloud.com  \n**Position:** Barista  \n\n---\n\n### 1. Final Score: 85/100\n\nKatherine demonstrates strong foundational alignment for an entry-level barista role. She displays a pleasant, customer-first mindset, practical problem-solving logic during high-pressure rush scenarios, coachability, and wide schedule availability with minimal academic constraints.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Summary of Strengths\n\n* **Practical Prioritization Under Pressure:** In the multi-task drive-thru scenario (handling an espresso station, headset order, and a honking customer), she correctly identified the need to swiftly de-escalate the immediate window need (handing out napkins), lean on team communication, and execute the complex order accurately.\n* **Excellent Schedule Flexibility:** Aside from a brief Tuesday/Thursday morning class (9:00 AM â€“ 10:30 AM), she offers open availability across morning opening shifts (including 5:00 AM), afternoons, and weekends.\n* **Positive Attitude & Coachability:** Expresses a welcoming approach to customer service and explicitly views real-time coaching/feedback as an opportunity to learn and improve.\n* **Task Management Skills:** Articulates clear organizational habits (making lists, breaking tasks down, asking clarifying questions) to avoid getting overwhelmed in fast-paced settings.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Weaknesses & Areas of Concern\n\n* **Lack of Prior Food/Beverage Experience:** Katherine has not worked in a coffee or food-service environment before; she will require standard on-the-job training regarding recipes, POS operations, and speed of service.\n* **Brief/Direct Communication Style:** Several of her answers were quite concise. While efficient, an in-person interview will help gauge her verbal enthusiasm and energy when interacting with drive-thru guests.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Final Recommendation: **Second Interview / In-Person Audition**\n\nKatherine shows solid potential, a great attitude, and the necessary availability for a busy drive-thru kiosk. An in-person interview at the store is recommended to confirm her interpersonal warmth, communication dynamics, and cultural fit with the crew before making an official offer.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Authenticity Assessment\n\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** **91.6%**\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer:** **Response 3 (72%)** *(Note: Response 10 also registered at 75%)*\n* **Answers Below 35%:** **None**\n* **Writing-Style & Behavioral Analysis:** \n  * The writing style analysis **strongly agrees** with the high human-authorship metrics.\n  * Responses consistently reflect natural, spontaneous, and conversational English appropriate for a college student applicant (e.g., minor grammatical quirks such as lowercase \"i\", minor spelling variation \"wheather\").\n  * Response 10 registered a momentary telemetry anomaly (0.0s duration / 0 keystrokes), which is typical of mobile voice-to-text, mobile predictive paste, or browser text autofill rather than AI generation.\n  * There are no signs of external AI generation, unnatural vocabulary shifts, or pre-rehearsed corporate phrasing. Responses are authentic and candidate-generated.","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Katherine! Welcome to your interview for the Barista position at our brand-new Lehigh Acres, FL location. We're thrilled to connect with you today!\n\nBefore we get started, I want to go over a few quick details about how this interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of 25 questions.\n- You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the \"Submit\" button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know in the chat whenever you'd like to finish.\n\nNo prior barista experience is requiredâ€”we are mainly looking for great energy, dedication, and a willingness to learn!\n\nTo kick things off with our first question: **What excited you most about applying to join our team here at Ellianos Coffee?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I saw a flyer saying Ellianos Coffee was hiring. I have always wanted to try out being a barista. I also love the smell of coffee"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":48213,"keystrokes":125,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":30541,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":32,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thatâ€™s wonderful! That fresh coffee aroma is definitely one of the best parts of the job. \n\nAs a barista at Ellianos, you'll be the first smiling face our customers see to start their morning. \n\n**How would you describe your approach to interacting with customers, and what do you do to make sure someone leaves with a smile?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"My approach would be friendly, welcoming and attentive to each customer. I would make sure I listen to what they need, greet them with a positive attitude, and make their experience as smooth as possible."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":75524,"keystrokes":202,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":56008,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":28,"pasteAttempts":1,"humanConfidence":72}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thatâ€™s a great mindset to have! Our customers really appreciate that warm, attentive energy, especially during that early morning rush.\n\nOur Ellianos location is a high-volume, 800-square-foot double drive-thru kiosk. It's a very fast-paced, active environment where baristas are on their feet for their entire shift, moving quickly in a tight space, and occasionally lifting items like milk crates or ice buckets (up to 30 lbs).\n\n**How comfortable are you with being on your feet and physically active during a busy, fast-paced shift?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Very comfortable."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":15543,"keystrokes":35,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":9605,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":8,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is great to hear! \n\nBecause of our compact drive-thru setup, we operate with a lean, close-knit team. That means every single team member is vital to the shift running smoothly, and an unexpected absence or late arrival has a huge impact on the whole team.\n\n**Do you have reliable transportation to the Lehigh Acres location, and how do you ensure you are consistently on time for your scheduled shifts?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes I have reliable transportation. I make sure to plan ahead, check my schedule in advance, and leave with enough time."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":144939,"keystrokes":114,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":21718,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":9,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Planning ahead is the best way to handle itâ€”reliability makes a huge difference for the whole crew!\n\nAt Ellianos, our motto is \"Italian Quality at America's Pace.\" When you start, you'll be learning lots of customized drink recipes, food items, and equipment setups all at once while keeping that quick pace.\n\n**Can you share a specific example from your past work, school, or personal life where you had to learn a lot of new information or juggle several tasks at once under pressure? How did you handle it?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"In school, iâ€™ve had times when i had multiple assignments, tests, and deadlines at the same time . I handled pressure by making a list of everything I needed to complete, prioritizing the most important tasks, and working on them one at a time instead of getting overwhelmed."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":153003,"keystrokes":238,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":24821,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":19,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Breaking things down and prioritizing is an excellent strategy! \n\nIn our double drive-thru kiosk, things get very loud and fast: youâ€™ll hear the espresso grinder running, milk steaming, and orders coming through your headset, all while you're talking directly to a customer at the window.\n\n**How do you stay focused and retain verbal information when there are multiple distractions and noises happening around you all at once?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I stay focused by listening carefully, repeating information to myself, and asking questions if i need clarification. I make sure I understand instructions"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":51887,"keystrokes":112,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":29623,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":27,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"In an 800-square-foot kiosk with 3 to 4 team members moving quickly around each other, clear and positive communication is essentialâ€”especially if a drink order gets mixed up or someone needs immediate help during a rush.\n\n**How do you handle receiving quick feedback or coaching in the moment when the pace is fast and the pressure is on?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I take feedback positively, listening carefully and make the corrections the right way . I see it as an opportunity to learn and improve"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":83920,"keystrokes":170,"maxInsertChunk":13,"responseDelayMs":17166,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":17,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That positive, growth-oriented mindset will take you very far with our team!\n\nNow, let's put your prioritization skills to the test with a real-world scenario you might encounter on a busy morning shift at Ellianos:\n\n**You are operating window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you honks asking for napkins. Walk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks.**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would stay calm and prioritize the tasks based on urgency. Iâ€™d quickly acknowledge the car asking for napkins then focus on completing the window B order while making sure the drinks and grits are made correctly. Iâ€™d communicate with my team if I needed help and then make sure the customer at my window is taken care of promptly"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":151038,"keystrokes":284,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":26186,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":24,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":84}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Handling the immediate, quick customer touchpoint (the napkins) first to de-escalate, while keeping your team in the loop on the larger multi-item order, is a very practical and smart way to prioritize!\n\nOur drive-thru opens bright and early to serve that morning rush, and we operate throughout the day into the evening, seven days a week.\n\n**What does your general availability look like for shifts (mornings, afternoons, weekends), and are you able to work early morning opening shifts (sometimes starting as early as 5:00 AM)?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes i am open availability. I do go to college on Tuesdays and Thursdays from 9-10:30 but any other days I am open to whatever shift is needed wheather its in the morning afternoons or weekends"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":1,"keystrokes":0,"maxInsertChunk":0,"responseDelayMs":2164,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":2160000,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":75}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you for clarifying that, Katherine! That schedule flexibility is very helpful, and accommodating a quick class block on Tuesdays and Thursdays is very manageable with proper planning.\n\nWe have covered all the key topics regarding the Barista role at our Lehigh Acres location. Youâ€™ve done a wonderful job walking through your thought process and sharing your approach to teamwork and customer service.\n\n**Do you have any questions for me about the role, our team, or the next steps in the hiring process?** \n\n*(Whenever you feel ready, you can also go ahead and click the \"Submit\" button on your screen to finalize your application!)*"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"What is the starting rate for a barista"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":14695,"keystrokes":40,"maxInsertChunk":3,"responseDelayMs":9922,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":33,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Starting pay for our Barista position typically begins with a competitive base hourly wage (aligned with Florida standards, usually ranging around $12.00 to $14.00 per hour depending on store scheduling and experience), **plus shared drive-thru tips**, which can significantly boost your total hourly take-home pay! \n\nThe exact base rate will be confirmed in detail by our local hiring manager during the final interview and onboarding stage.\n\nDo you have any other questions for me today, or are you ready to conclude? If you're all set, you can go ahead and press the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen to send in your application!"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"No more questions for me"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":4694,"keystrokes":17,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":15863,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":64,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you so much for your time today, Katherine! It was a pleasure getting to know you and learning more about your background, positive attitude, and enthusiasm for joining Ellianos Coffee. \n\nOur management team will review your interview responses and reach out regarding the next steps for the Lehigh Acres branch. \n\nTo finalize everything, please click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen now. Have a wonderful rest of your day!"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Submit"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":2768,"keystrokes":7,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":22798,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":22,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Your application has been received! Thank you again, Katherine, and have a wonderful day!"}]}],"emailSent":true,"candidateInfo":{"phone":"2398236507","name":"Katherine Perez","email":"perezk2004@icloud.com"},"id":"2d7fa724-b586-4a00-9315-76dc491d9389","secondInterviewGuide":{"interviewerTips":["Pedir siempre ejemplos concretos y situaciones reales en lugar de respuestas teÃ³ricas o hipotÃ©ticas.","No juzgar negativamente la brevedad de sus respuestas previas; evaluar en vivo su ritmo, tono de voz y desenvolvimiento conversacional.","Preguntar sobre el uso de herramientas o dictado de manera neutral y distendida, valorando la autenticidad y honestidad del candidato."],"decision":{"hire":"Aprobar contrataciÃ³n si demuestra energÃ­a verbal positiva, excelente actitud de servicio, calificaciÃ³n >= 4.0 en todos los bloques 'mustPass', nivel de inglÃ©s conversacional fluido (bloque de inglÃ©s >= 3.5) y confirma disponibilidad total para turnos de apertura a las 5:00 AM en Lehigh Acres.","decline":"Descartar si obtiene una calificaciÃ³n <= 2.5 en cualquiera de los bloques 'mustPass', si muestra desgano o apatÃ­a en el roleplay de atenciÃ³n al cliente, si presenta problemas de transporte para aperturas de madrugada, o si se evidencian inconsistencias graves en su comunicaciÃ³n.","thirdConversation":"Considerar llamada de seguimiento con el Gerente de Tienda si cumple con el perfil actitudinal y de disponibilidad, pero muestra dudas menores sobre la compatibilidad de horarios de estudio o requiere una verificaciÃ³n adicional de transporte."},"blocks":[{"id":"block_aprendizaje_experiencia","title":"Curva de Aprendizaje y RetenciÃ³n de Procesos","goal":"Evaluar cÃ³mo asimila procedimientos tÃ©cnicos y recetas complejas sin experiencia previa en el rubro.","minutes":12,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q1","q2"]},{"id":"block_operacion_presion","title":"OperaciÃ³n en Espacio Reducido y Manejo de EstrÃ©s","goal":"Medir agilidad, coordinaciÃ³n fÃ­sica y comunicaciÃ³n en el entorno compacto de un kiosco de 800 sq ft.","minutes":15,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q3","q4"]},{"id":"block_ingles_servicio","title":"InglÃ©s Funcional y Dinamismo en Ventanilla","goal":"Comprobar fluidez conversacional en inglÃ©s, entusiasmo y capacidad de sugerencia rÃ¡pida en drive-thru.","minutes":10,"mustPass":false,"questionIds":["q5","q6"]},{"id":"block_disponibilidad_compromiso","title":"Disponibilidad, Apertura de Tienda y Honestidad","goal":"Validar compromiso con horarios matutinos (5:00 AM), apertura en octubre en Lehigh Acres y verificar autenticidad.","minutes":13,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q7","q8"]}],"generatedAt":"2026-08-25T20:22:26.739Z","questions":[{"id":"q1","block":"block_aprendizaje_experiencia","text":"Por escrito mencionaste: 'In school, iâ€™ve had times when i had multiple assignments, tests, and deadlines at the same time. I handled pressure by making a list...'. En el drive-thru de Ellianos preparamos bebidas en menos de un minuto y no hay tiempo de escribir listas. CuÃ©ntame un caso real donde tuviste que memorizar y ejecutar mÃºltiples instrucciones nuevas sobre la marcha sin anotarlas: Â¿quÃ© hiciste exactamente y cÃ³mo te aseguraste de no cometer errores?","language":"es","purpose":"Evaluar la memoria de trabajo y la capacidad de retener recetas y secuencias operativas rÃ¡pidas sin depender de notas escritas.","listenFor":["TÃ©cnicas activas de memorizaciÃ³n rÃ¡pida (asociaciÃ³n, repeticiÃ³n mental, visualizaciÃ³n).","Humildad para pedir confirmaciÃ³n rÃ¡pida al compaÃ±ero sin frenar el flujo.","OrientaciÃ³n al detalle y precisiÃ³n en la ejecuciÃ³n bajo tiempo lÃ­mite."],"redFlags":["Incapacidad de dar un ejemplo real fuera de la escuela.","Dependencia absoluta de instructivos fÃ­sicos durante momentos de alta velocidad.","FrustraciÃ³n evidente cuando se le exige velocidad mental inmediata."]},{"id":"q2","block":"block_aprendizaje_experiencia","text":"Comentaste que te motivÃ³ la vacante porque siempre quisiste probar ser barista y te encanta el aroma del cafÃ©, aunque no tienes experiencia previa en el sector de alimentos. Cuando entres a Ellianos tendrÃ¡s que aprender mÃ¡s de 30 combinaciones de bebidas calientes, frÃ­as y alimentos en tu primera semana. Â¿CÃ³mo te preparas personalmente para absorber tanta informaciÃ³n tÃ©cnica en tan poco tiempo?","language":"es","purpose":"Verificar la proactividad, disciplina de estudio y entusiasmo real por dominar el menÃº de Ellianos.","listenFor":["DisposiciÃ³n para estudiar guÃ­as y menÃºs en su tiempo libre durante el entrenamiento.","InterÃ©s genuino en los estÃ¡ndares de calidad y preparaciÃ³n de cafÃ©.","Curiosidad por entender las diferencias entre tipos de bebidas (espresso, chai, energizantes Lotus)."],"redFlags":["Actitud pasiva esperando que el entrenador haga todo el esfuerzo.","DesinterÃ©s por la consistencia o recetas exactas.","Minimizar la complejidad del rol de barista asumiendo que 'es solo servir cafÃ©'."]},{"id":"q3","block":"block_operacion_presion","text":"En el ejercicio hipotÃ©tico respondiste: 'Iâ€™d communicate with my team if I needed help and then make sure the customer at my window is taken care of promptly'. En nuestro kiosco de 800 sq ft hay 4 a 6 personas moviÃ©ndose rÃ¡pido con licuadoras, molinos y vaporizadores sonando al mismo tiempo. Describe cÃ³mo proyectas tu voz y cÃ³mo te coordinas con un compaÃ±ero cuando necesitas un ingrediente o ayuda urgente sin chocar ni generar caos.","language":"es","purpose":"Evaluar la comunicaciÃ³n asertiva, uso de llamados claros ('behind you', 'corner') y conciencia espacial en espacios confinados.","listenFor":["ComprensiÃ³n de llamadas de seguridad y comunicaciÃ³n clara y directa.","Capacidad de mantener la calma y el tono positivo sin sonar exasperada.","Sentido de trabajo en equipo y sincronizaciÃ³n fÃ­sica en estaciones de trabajo."],"redFlags":["Tendencia a aislarse o quedarse callada bajo estrÃ©s.","Falta de conciencia del espacio fÃ­sico y del movimiento de otros compaÃ±eros.","Tono de comunicaciÃ³n defensivo o que culpabiliza a otros."]},{"id":"q4","block":"block_operacion_presion","text":"SeÃ±alaste que te sientes 'Very comfortable' estando de pie y fÃ­sicamente activa. En un turno pico de Ellianos estarÃ¡s 6 a 8 horas de pie, agachÃ¡ndote para sacar leches, cargando cubos de hielo de 30 libras y moviÃ©ndote sin parar. CuÃ©ntame sobre la experiencia mÃ¡s demandante fÃ­sicamente que hayas tenido en tu vida y cÃ³mo mantienes tu energÃ­a y sonrisa cuando el cuerpo empieza a cansarse.","language":"es","purpose":"Medir la resistencia fÃ­sica real, tolerancia a la fatiga y capacidad de mantener la actitud de servicio.","listenFor":["Experiencias concretas de esfuerzo fÃ­sico sostenido (deportes, mudanzas, trabajos anteriores, proyectos activos).","HÃ¡bitos saludables de hidrataciÃ³n y manejo de postura fÃ­sica.","Resiliencia mental para no transmitir el cansancio al cliente."],"redFlags":["Muestras de sorpresa o rechazo ante la exigencia fÃ­sica del turno.","Historial de desmotivaciÃ³n inmediata cuando el trabajo requiere esfuerzo fÃ­sico continuo.","Falta de energÃ­a o lenguaje corporal decaÃ­do durante la entrevista."]},{"id":"q5","block":"block_ingles_servicio","text":"Imagine it's 7:15 AM on a Monday rush. A customer at the window says: 'I've been waiting for 5 minutes, I'm late for work, and I need my caramel latte right now!' Show me right now how you would respond to them warmly, de-escalate their frustration, and hand them their drink.","language":"en","purpose":"Evaluar fluidez en inglÃ©s, tono de voz empÃ¡tico y capacidad de resoluciÃ³n y desescalamiento en ventanilla.","listenFor":["Natural English conversational flow with a warm and polite tone.","Immediate empathy and quick acknowledgment ('I completely understand, here is your fresh latte...').","Speed and positive body language without taking the customer's frustration personally."],"redFlags":["Inability to formulate full sentences in English or freezing under roleplay.","Defensive or rude tone towards the customer.","Ignoring the customer's emotions and acting robotic."]},{"id":"q6","block":"block_ingles_servicio","text":"A customer pulls up and asks: 'Hey, I've never been to Ellianos before. What cold drink do you recommend that will keep me awake all morning?' How would you upsell and describe one of our signature drinks in a fast, energetic way?","language":"en","purpose":"Medir capacidad de venta sugestiva, entusiasmo comercial y rapidez descriptiva en inglÃ©s.","listenFor":["High enthusiasm and appetizing descriptions (mentioning flavors, espresso shots, or energy infusions).","Concise recommendation tailored for speed of service.","Friendly call to action inviting the customer to try the recommendation."],"redFlags":["Flat, monotone delivery without excitement.","Hesitant or overly long explanations that would stall the drive-thru line.","Complete lack of product enthusiasm."]},{"id":"q7","block":"block_disponibilidad_compromiso","text":"Mencionaste que tienes disponibilidad completa excepto tus clases universitarias los martes y jueves de 9:00 a 10:30 AM. Para la apertura de Lehigh Acres en octubre, muchos turnos arrancan a las 4:30 AM o 5:00 AM para preparar la estaciÃ³n. Â¿CÃ³mo es tu rutina de transporte y descanso para asegurar llegar siempre 10 minutos antes, especialmente en turnos de madrugada?","language":"es","purpose":"Verificar la confiabilidad del transporte, hÃ¡bitos de descanso y compatibilidad real con los turnos de apertura.","listenFor":["Plan de transporte concreto, independiente y verificado en Lehigh Acres.","Compromiso claro con levantarse temprano sin que interfiera con sus responsabilidades acadÃ©micas.","Entendimiento del impacto crÃ­tico de una llegada tardÃ­a en un equipo de kiosco reducido."],"redFlags":["Dependencia de transporte de terceros poco confiable para horas de madrugada.","Dudas o expresiones de desgano al confirmar turnos a las 4:30/5:00 AM.","Incompatibilidades de horario adicionales que no fueron declaradas previamente."]},{"id":"q8","block":"block_disponibilidad_compromiso","text":"Notamos que en la plataforma virtual respondiste de forma muy fluida y rÃ¡pida, utilizando algunas funciones de texto o dictado mÃ³vil. En Ellianos valoramos al 100% la autenticidad y la honestidad. CuÃ©ntame con total tranquilidad cÃ³mo realizaste la entrevista virtual y si utilizaste algÃºn asistente o dictado: esto suma puntos a tu transparencia.","language":"es","purpose":"Evaluar la honestidad, madurez personal y coherencia del candidato respecto al uso de herramientas digitales.","listenFor":["Respuesta abierta, tranquila y honesta sobre el uso de dictado por voz, telÃ©fono o redacciÃ³n personal.","Coherencia total entre su forma de expresarse oralmente y lo escrito en la evaluaciÃ³n previa.","Madurez al asumir la autorÃ­a de sus respuestas y valores personales de integridad."],"redFlags":["Nerviosismo excesivo, contradicciones evidentes o evasivas al hablar del tema.","Discrepancia abismal entre su nivel de vocabulario hablado y el texto evaluado.","Falta de transparencia al responder preguntas sencillas sobre su mÃ©todo de trabajo."]}],"focusPoints":["Verificar energÃ­a verbal, calidez y carisma presencial frente a las respuestas breves y directas de la prueba virtual.","Evaluar la capacidad de aprendizaje rÃ¡pido y retenciÃ³n de recetas/procesos sin contar con experiencia previa en barismo o alimentos.","Comprobar la agilidad motriz y comunicaciÃ³n en espacios compactos (kiosco de 800 sq ft) bajo el ritmo acelerado de doble carril.","Confirmar la logÃ­stica y puntualidad estricta para turnos de apertura de madrugada (5:00 AM) compatibilizando sus clases universitarias (Mar/Jue 9:00-10:30 AM)."]}},{"candidateInfo":{"phone":"2392700032","name":"Catarina Priscila Ixcotoyac Us","email":"priscilaus2018@gmail.com"},"messages":[],"status":"Incomplete","date":"2026-08-25T19:16:14.149Z","id":"98fd92a9-0999-4bbf-818d-cbdfc7af8edf","position":"Barista"},{"id":"b126cd65-cee3-499d-8776-149aa1b4d875","date":"2026-08-25T12:24:26.575Z","position":"Shift Leader","candidateInfo":{"phone":"7866223599","name":"Anay Martin","email":"anaymartin1977@icloud.com"},"emailSent":true,"evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation: Shift Leader â€” Ellianos Coffee\n\n**Candidate Name:** Anay Martin  \n**Contact:** 786-622-3599 | anaymartin1977@icloud.com  \n**Position Applied For:** Shift Leader (Lehigh Acres Location)  \n\n---\n\n### **1. Final Score: 38 / 100**\n\nWhile Anay brings relevant fast-food management background on paper, the responses demonstrated a significant deficit in operational problem-solving, cash management protocols, equipment contingency planning, and situational leadership. When presented with realistic drive-thru and supervisory scenarios, the answers were either non-responsive, contradictory, or lacked actionable depth required for an 800 sq ft, high-efficiency kiosk.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Strengths**\n* **Relevant Industry Background:** Cites 4 years of managerial and kitchen experience at McDonald's, an environment with high drive-thru volume and speed demands.\n* **Open Morning Availability:** Available 7 days a week for morning shifts, matching peak drive-thru business hours in the drive-thru coffee industry.\n* **Positive Attitude Toward Growth:** Expressed enthusiasm regarding joining a brand-new store location.\n\n---\n\n### **3. Weaknesses & Areas of Concern**\n* **Lack of Loss Prevention & Accountability Procedures:** When asked how to address a recurring cash drawer discrepancy (3rd time in a week), the candidate responded: *\"encorage him her try to get it out as quickly soon as possible.\"* This demonstrates a critical lack of understanding regarding register audits, cash handling procedures, and corrective action.\n* **Inadequate Scenario & Troubleshooting Logic:** \n  * In response to an espresso grinder breakdown during a peak rush, the candidate offered only a generic *\"Encourage and help them at each station\"* without addressing workflow reassignment, menu adjustments, or customer communication.\n  * In the drive-thru multitasking prioritization prompt, the candidate responded with only the number *\"1\"* after giving a generic initial response, failing to sequence or explain how to handle concurrent drink/food orders.\n* **Vague / Evasive Answers:** When prompted repeatedly for specific examples of hands-on coaching and dealing with underperforming team members during a rush, the candidate provided broad platitudes rather than concrete actions or past experiences.\n\n---\n\n### **4. Authenticity Assessment**\n\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** **68.0%** (across 11 recorded responses).\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer:** **Response 7 (12%)**.\n* **Responses Below 35% Confidence:**\n  * **Response 5 (16%):** 294 characters, 511-char max insert chunk, 4 tab switches, 1 paste attempt (*Candidate Warned*).\n  * **Response 6 (16%):** 97 characters, 97-char max insert chunk, 4 tab switches, 1 paste attempt (*Candidate Warned*).\n  * **Response 7 (12%):** 138 characters, 138-char single insertion, 186 WPM recorded over 6.4 seconds with only 1 keystroke (*Candidate Warned*).\n* **Writing-Style Consistency Analysis:** **Agrees strongly with typing metrics.**\n  * There is an abrupt register shift between the candidate's natural typing and Responses 5â€“7. Responses 5 and 7 use formal, polished corporate phrasing (*\"streamlined operations and improved workflow efficiency, ensuring all dishes were prepared...\"* / *\"personal accountability, dedication, and effective collaboration\"*), contrasting sharply with the candidateâ€™s unassisted responses (e.g., *\"encorage him her try to get it out as quickly soon as possible\"* and *\"Meet needs at always keep the costumer happy\"*). \n  * The single-keystroke submissions, high-speed text insertions, and repeated browser tab switching further corroborate external generation/pasting for those specific behavioral questions.\n\n---\n\n### **5. Final Recommendation**\n\n**Recommendation: DO NOT HIRE**\n\n**Rationale:** Independent of the authenticity flags, the candidate's actual operational responses show that they are not currently prepared to independently lead a shift, manage cash reconciliation, or navigate equipment failures under pressure. A Shift Leader at Ellianos must be capable of fast, decisive problem-solving, strict operational accountability, and clear communicationâ€”competencies that were not demonstrated during this interview.","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Shift Leader position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Anay! Welcome, and thank you for your interest in joining the Ellianos Coffee family as a Shift Leader at our brand-new Lehigh Acres location. We're excited to learn more about you!\n\nBefore we get started, I want to go over a couple of quick details about how this interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of 25 questions.\n- You are free to finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen, or simply by letting me know right here in the chat that you'd like to conclude.\n\nLet's start with an easy one: **What drew your interest to Ellianos Coffee, and what excites you about being part of our new team in Lehigh Acres?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I am excited that is a new proyect where i know there will be room for growth"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":81873,"keystrokes":87,"maxInsertChunk":3,"responseDelayMs":295701,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":12,"pasteAttempts":2,"humanConfidence":52}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That's fantastic, Anay! Opening a brand-new store definitely brings great opportunities to grow alongside the business.\n\nTo help me get a better picture of your background, **could you share a little about your previous work experienceâ€”especially any roles involving customer service, food/beverage, or leading a team?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I have been a Mc Donaldâ€™s manager for four years and have kitchen experience"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":97333,"keystrokes":93,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":22383,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":9,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Four years of managerial experience at McDonald's is fantastic background, especially when it comes to understanding fast-paced drive-thru operations! \n\nOur Ellianos model runs with very lean, efficient teams inside an 800-square-foot double drive-thru kiosk, which means reliability is absolutely criticalâ€”a single absence can heavily impact the shift. \n\n**Do you have reliable transportation, and what does your availability look like across different days and shift times (mornings, afternoons, weekends)?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"i Am available in the mornings seven days a week"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":33239,"keystrokes":54,"maxInsertChunk":3,"responseDelayMs":86798,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":18,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":84}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Morning availability is huge in the coffee world, as our peak morning rush is the heartbeat of our business!\n\nGiven your experience as a manager at McDonald's, you know how intense morning rushes can get. In an 800 sq ft building with a lean team, communication is key.\n\n**How do you typically set up and motivate your team right before a heavy morning rush to ensure everyone is aligned, energized, and ready to move fast?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"The most crucial aspect lies in how each individual fulfills their responsibilities in their respective roles to meet the defined objectives. Success depends on personal accountability, dedication, and effective collaboration, ensuring that every action contributes toward the collective goals."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":329918,"keystrokes":222,"maxInsertChunk":511,"responseDelayMs":223390,"tabSwitches":4,"wpm":7,"pasteAttempts":1,"lowConfidenceWarned":true,"humanConfidence":16}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"I completely agreeâ€”accountability and clear roles make all the difference. \n\nSince you've led shifts through busy rushes before, **could you share a specific example of a time when a team member was struggling to keep up with their role during a peak rush, and how you handled the situation in the moment?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Once again, the most important thing is the immediate response to meet the established timeframe."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":99758,"keystrokes":66,"maxInsertChunk":97,"responseDelayMs":309914,"tabSwitches":4,"wpm":9,"pasteAttempts":1,"lowConfidenceWarned":true,"humanConfidence":16}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Speed is definitely essential during a rush! \n\nTo get a clearer sense of your hands-on leadership style, **can you tell me about a specific time at McDonald's when someone on your shift was falling behind on their station? What exact steps did you take in that moment to help them recover without slowing down the line?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"As the kitchen leader, I streamlined operations and improved workflow efficiency, ensuring all dishes were prepared and delivered on time."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":6449,"keystrokes":1,"maxInsertChunk":138,"responseDelayMs":122295,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":186,"pasteAttempts":0,"lowConfidenceWarned":true,"humanConfidence":12}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you for that context, Anay.\n\nLet's step up the difficulty a bit and look at managing unexpected operational issues during a rush. \n\nImagine you are leading a busy morning shift at Ellianos, cars are wrapping around both drive-thru lanes, and one of your main espresso grinders suddenly stops working. \n\n**How would you lead your team through that situation to keep the flow moving and maintain customer satisfaction?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Encourage and help them at each station"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":23942,"keystrokes":44,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":56944,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":18,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you, Anay. \n\nAs a Shift Leader, your responsibilities also include operational accountability and coaching. \n\nImagine you are closing out a shift and discover a significant cash discrepancy in one of the drawers. This is the third time this week that this specific barista's register has been short. \n\n**What exact steps would you take to investigate this discrepancy and address the situation with the employee?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"encorage him her try to get it out as quickly soon as possible"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":49871,"keystrokes":99,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":50129,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":16,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you, Anay.\n\nNow, I'd like to put you in a peak-rush scenario that tests your multitasking, prioritization, and real-time decision-making in our drive-thru model.\n\n**You are operating Window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for Window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you honks asking for napkins. Walk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks.**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Meet needs at always keep the costumer happy"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":48757,"keystrokes":61,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":48339,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":10,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Keeping the customer happy is definitely the ultimate goal! \n\nTo help me understand your operational flow in that moment, **in what exact order would you handle those three actions?**\n\n1. Handing napkins to the car at Window A\n2. Finishing the espresso drink for Window A\n3. Prepping or delegating the Lotus drinks and grits for Window B\n\nPlease walk me through the sequence and why you'd do it in that order."}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"1"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":1486,"keystrokes":1,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":36907,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":40,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Got itâ€”handling the quick request for napkins immediately clears that immediate distraction and takes care of the customer right in front of you. \n\nWe've covered your experience, availability, and how you approach leadership and peak-rush scenarios. \n\nTo wrap up our interview: **Do you have any questions for me about the Shift Leader role, the new Lehigh Acres location, or what it's like to work at Ellianos Coffee?** \n\n*(Whenever you feel you're finished, you can also let me know or click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen to finalize your application.)*"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"No"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":1888,"keystrokes":2,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":12219,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":32,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you so much for your time today, Anay! It was a pleasure speaking with you and learning more about your background. \n\nOur hiring team for the Lehigh Acres location will review your responses and be in touch regarding the next steps.\n\nPlease go ahead and click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen now to finalize your application. \n\nWe wish you the best of luck!