joy up by motivating each other'. En un kiosco de 800 sq ft con 5 personas hombro a hombro, el calor y el ruido pueden generar tensiÃ³n. Describe una situaciÃ³n real en tu trabajo anterior donde un compaÃ±ero perdiÃ³ los estribos o bajÃ³ los brazos y cÃ³mo interveniste tÃº.","language":"es","purpose":"Constatar su capacidad real para mantener la moral alta y la cohesiÃ³n de equipo en espacios ultra-compactos.","listenFor":["Ejemplo concreto de apoyo prÃ¡ctico (asumir una tarea de apoyo, cubrir una estaciÃ³n momentÃ¡neamente).","ComunicaciÃ³n constructiva por headset para aliviar la carga sin generar conflicto.","Madurez emocional para no absorber ni amplificar la negatividad ambiental."],"redFlags":["Ignorar las dificultades de los compaÃ±eros enfocÃ¡ndose Ãºnicamente en su propia tarea.","Engancharse en discusiones o quejas frente al cliente en ventanilla.","Respuestas idealistas sin un respaldo tÃ¡ctico de ayuda real."]},{"id":"q9","block":"block_5","text":"Mostraste interÃ©s en las fechas de apertura de Lehigh Acres, el salario y las propinas. La apertura oficial es en octubre y requerirÃ¡ varias sesiones de capacitaciÃ³n intensiva en equipo. Â¿Tienes total disponibilidad para estas fechas de entrenamiento y cuÃ¡les son tus expectativas salariales por hora?","language":"es","purpose":"Alinear expectativas de compensaciÃ³n y garantizar asistencia a los entrenamientos previos a la inauguraciÃ³n.","listenFor":["Expectativa salarial dentro del rango del mercado para baristas (base + propinas).","Compromiso explÃ­cito de asistencia a todas las jornadas de onboarding y prÃ¡cticas de barra.","Entusiasmo por participar en el lanzamiento de una nueva sucursal."],"redFlags":["Expectativas salariales irreales fuera del tabulador de barista de entrada.","Incompatibilidad de horarios durante las semanas clave de capacitaciÃ³n.","Falta de claridad sobre cÃ³mo encaja este ingreso suplementario con su trabajo de maestra."]},{"id":"q10","block":"block_5","text":"Tus respuestas en el chat inicial fueron muy naturales y dinÃ¡micas. En los procesos de selecciÃ³n valoramos la honestidad ante todo: Â¿te apoyaste en alguna herramienta o asistente para preparar tus respuestas escritas, y quÃ© es lo que mÃ¡s te entusiasma de volver a la energÃ­a del cafÃ© diario?","language":"es","purpose":"Evaluar la honestidad del candidato sobre su proceso previo y confirmar su motivaciÃ³n vocacional genuina.","listenFor":["Transparencia total y tranquilidad al hablar de su proceso de postulaciÃ³n.","PasiÃ³n genuina por el ritmo acelerado del cafÃ© y el contacto humano en drive-thru.","Coherencia entre su estilo verbal actual y las respuestas brindadas por escrito."],"redFlags":["Incomodidad o contradicciones evidentes respecto a su postulaciÃ³n.","DesinterÃ©s por el oficio del barismo tratÃ¡ndolo solo como un relleno horario sin compromiso.","Inconsistencia notable entre su comunicaciÃ³n oral y su registro escrito."]}],"focusPoints":["Confirmar disponibilidad estricta para aperturas desde las 4:30 AM de jueves a sÃ¡bado y validar holgura real con su compromiso eclesiÃ¡stico de las 5:30 PM.","Verificar la profundidad tÃ©cnica real de su experiencia previa en Scooter's Coffee (velocidad en barra, multi-estaciÃ³n, reducciÃ³n de mermas).","Evaluar fluidez verbal y pulimento en atenciÃ³n al cliente en inglÃ©s para evitar respuestas excesivamente breves o informales en ventanilla.","Comprobar disposiciÃ³n para desaprender recetas de Scooter's y acatar los estÃ¡ndares italianos y flujos especÃ­ficos de Ellianos."]},"position":"Barista","id":"8e476bf9-1592-43c1-bb44-3d247d562f57","candidateInfo":{"phone":"2399808360","name":"Joseline Joy Martinez","email":"joselinejm057@gmail.com"},"evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation: Barista Position\n\n**Candidate Name:** Joseline Joy Martinez  \n**Contact:** 239-980-8360 | joselinejm057@gmail.com  \n**Target Location:** Lehigh Acres, FL  \n\n---\n\n### Final Score: 84/100\n\nJoseline presents as a strong, practical candidate who brings direct, highly relevant drive-thru coffee experience from Scooter's Coffee. Her background in high-volume drive-thru environments means she requires minimal operational ramp-up regarding line-busting, headset communication, station multitasking, and drink accuracy. The primary limitation is her scheduling availability, which is restricted to Thursday through Saturday.\n\n---\n\n### Strengths\n* **Direct Drive-Thru Experience:** Prior employment at Scooterâ€™s Coffee provides immediate familiarity with fast-paced drive-thru workflows, line-busting (\"line scooting\"), headset communication, and compact layout operations.\n* **Positive Team-Oriented Attitude:** Demonstrated a clear commitment to peer support, morale maintenance (\"keeping the joy up\"), and step-in teamwork during bottleneck situations.\n* **Practical Prioritization:** Demonstrated common-sense logic under pressure (e.g., handing napkins to an immediate window customer in seconds before addressing complex back-queue drinks).\n* **Trainability & Growth Mindset:** Open to learning Ellianos-specific drink recipes and standards, leveraging her background as a teacher to embrace structured training.\n\n---\n\n### Areas of Concern & Weaknesses\n* **Constrained Availability:** Available only Thursday through Saturday, with a specific request to finish by 4:30 PM on Thursdays and Fridays due to church leadership commitments. Store management must confirm if these specific windows align with shift needs (e.g., morning opening rushes).\n* **Brevity in Communication:** Responses were consistently brief and informal (e.g., typos such as \"what's food\" instead of \"what's good\"). While practical, further evaluation is needed to ensure her customer-facing communication is consistently polished.\n\n---\n\n### Final Recommendation: Second Interview\n**Recommendation:** **Second Interview (Manager Fit & Schedule Confirmation)**\n\nJoselineâ€™s operational background at Scooterâ€™s Coffee makes her an asset for opening-team efficiency. A brief second interview with the store manager should focus on confirming whether her Thursdayâ€“Saturday morning availability matches the schedule matrix for the Lehigh Acres opening.\n\n---\n\n### Authenticity Assessment\n\n* **Average Confidence:** 100%\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer:** 100% (No responses below 100%)\n* **Answers Below 35%:** None\n* **Writing-Style Alignment:** The writing-style analysis **fully agrees** with the typing metrics. All responses showed organic typing speeds (29â€“65 WPM), realistic durations and pauses, 0 paste attempts, 0 tab switches, and single-character insertion sizes. The casual tone, sentence structures, and minor conversational typos are completely consistent with natural human typing.","status":"Completed","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Joseline! Welcome to your interview for the Barista position at our brand-new Ellianos Coffee location in Lehigh Acres, FL. We are excited to get to know you!\n\nBefore we begin, here are a few quick things to keep in mind:\n- You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know right here in the chat whenever you wish to wrap up.\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of **25 questions**, moving one question at a time.\n\nLetâ€™s get started with something simple: \n\n**What made you interested in applying to join the Ellianos Coffee team here in Lehigh Acres?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™ve worked at a coffee shop before it was my favorite job so far, it really felt like a family but i am a part time teacher at a private school so I only work Monday-Wednesday and need something to supplement my income. Iâ€™ve been keeping up with your process and iâ€™m excited for this company to be here locally"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":80529,"keystrokes":337,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":16853,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":45,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Itâ€™s wonderful to hear that you already have a love for coffee and that you're passionate about bringing great energy to our new local branch! \n\nSince we operate with a lean, close-knit team where every shift counts, having a dependable schedule is essential. \n\nGiven your teaching schedule on Monday through Wednesday, **what does your exact availability look like for Thursdays through Sundays (including mornings, afternoons, and weekends), and do you have reliable transportation to get to and from our Lehigh Acres location?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes, I would be able to work Thursdays-Saturdays but would prefer Thursdays and Fridays mornings to about 4:30 pm because I am a leader at my church and iâ€™m usually at church by 5:30 to set up Thursdays and Fridays"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":73173,"keystrokes":246,"maxInsertChunk":3,"responseDelayMs":20299,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":33,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you for clearly outlining your availability, Joseline!\n\nOur Ellianos model is an 800-square-foot double drive-thru kiosk. Because itâ€™s a high-volume, fast-paced environment with a compact footprint, baristas are constantly moving, standing for the duration of their shifts, and handling tasks like lifting milk crates or heavy syrup boxes (up to 30 lbs).\n\n**How comfortable are you with the physical demands of staying on your feet and moving quickly in a fast-paced, compact workspace during a busy rush?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Very comfortable, I worked at scooters which is also a fast paced drive thru"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":29067,"keystrokes":86,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":17668,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":29,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Having that background at Scooter's is great experience, especially with drive-thru speed and efficiency!\n\nSince you're familiar with drive-thru rushes, can you give me a specific example from your time at Scooter's of a moment when the line was wrapped around the building and you had to balance extreme speed while keeping every single drink 100% accurate? How did you manage that?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"We sent someone outside to line scoot which means weâ€™re taking orders outside to have them ahead of time so that we can speed up the process, having clear roles helps too because then you donâ€™t have two people making the same drink"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":59918,"keystrokes":308,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":13626,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":43,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Clear role division and line-busting definitely make a huge difference in keeping things moving!\n\nInside the building, especially on bar, orders can come in fast with lots of specific customizationsâ€”different dairy alternatives, syrup pumps, extra espresso shots, and temperature requests. \n\n**When you have multiple highly customized drink orders coming in at the same time, what personal system or mental trick do you use to remember and execute every detail without mixing up drinks or slowing down the line?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"i always double check if itâ€™s sugar free and what milk needs to be used so i donâ€™t make a mistake that canâ€™t be fixed without having to make a new drink sometimes i would repeat the order in my head over and over so i would remember"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":52721,"keystrokes":255,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":28931,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":55,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Catching those details like milk type and sugar-free preferences upfront is crucial for food safety and preventing remakes!\n\nIn a double drive-thru setup, speed is essential, but warm customer service is just as important. Imagine a scenario where a customer pulls up to the window visibly upset because their wait was a few minutes longer than expected or their drink from a previous visit wasn't made right. \n\n**How do you de-escalate the situation, make them feel valued, and resolve the issue quickly without stalling the flow of cars behind them?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Ask them how theyâ€™re day was or introduce and ice breaker since theyâ€™ve been there before say something along the lines of nice to see you again"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":50285,"keystrokes":184,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":24561,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":32,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"A friendly, welcoming touch definitely helps ease tension right away!\n\nBecause our building is only 800 square feet, during a peak rush you are working shoulder-to-shoulder with your teammates under fast, high-pressure conditions. \n\n**If a bottleneck happensâ€”for instance, one teammate is falling behind on food or a steam wand gets backed upâ€”how do you communicate and coordinate with your team in the moment to keep the vibe positive and get the line flowing again?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"if we have party mode on our headsets give each other a heads up that something is going on, if you see an area where you can help and you have the time do it, keep the joy up by motivating each other and telling each other we can do this"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":60108,"keystrokes":279,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":30356,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":51,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Keeping that positive energy and open communication over the headsets is huge for maintaining morale during a rush. \n\nNow, let's put your multitasking and prioritization skills to the test with a specific scenario:\n\n**You are operating window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you honks asking for napkins. Walk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks.**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Let your partner know you will go help as soon as you pass the napkins to the car"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":24680,"keystrokes":100,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":51366,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":44,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Handling the quick 2-second napkin handoff first keeps the immediate customer happy while using the headset to coordinate support for Window B is a great, practical response.\n\nBecause our drive-thru operates with lean staffing, every single team member is essentialâ€”even one person being 10 minutes late can disrupt an entire morning rush for the whole crew. \n\n**What habits or routines do you use to ensure you are consistently punctual, prepared, and ready to hit the ground running the moment your shift starts?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"arrive early always stock and prep before you hop on shift and where help is needed till your station is ready for you"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":42539,"keystrokes":180,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":24303,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":32,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Arriving early and proactively stocking and prepping sets the entire shift up for success!\n\nEven though you have great coffee drive-thru experience from Scooter's, Ellianos has our own signature recipes, pump counts, and Italian-style espresso standards. \n\n**How do you approach unlearning old habits from previous jobs and embracing new brand standards and feedback from leadership during training?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™m a teacher so learning new ways to do this is my jam"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":12006,"keystrokes":60,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":19683,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":65,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That growth mindset and passion for learning is a fantastic asset to bring to any team!\n\nIn a compact 800-square-foot kiosk, clutter and mess can build up in seconds if not managed actively. Cleanliness directly impacts health standards, drink quality, and speed.\n\n**How do you maintain a \"clean-as-you-go\" habit (like wiping steam wands, rinsing pitchers, and keeping counters clear) while still moving at maximum speed during a heavy rush?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"practice, the more you remember you have to clean it becomes something thatâ€™s natural"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":25043,"keystrokes":128,"maxInsertChunk":3,"responseDelayMs":38838,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":34,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Repetition definitely builds great habits!\n\nSince the Lehigh Acres location is brand new, many customers pulling up to our windows will be trying Ellianos Coffee for the very first time. \n\n**How will you make their first experience memorable so they become loyal daily regulars right from opening week?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"give them recommendations theyâ€™re going to want to know whatâ€™s food"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":10422,"keystrokes":61,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":11374,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":63,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Recommending favorites and guiding first-time guests through the menu is a wonderful way to build trust and make them feel right at home!\n\nWe have covered all the essential details about the Barista position, your background, and what to expect at our new Lehigh Acres double drive-thru. \n\n**Do you have any questions for me about the role, the team, the opening timeline, or anything else youâ€™d like to share before we conclude?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"when would be the opening, do you guys have a salary yet, are tips a thing, how many baristas would be working a shift together?"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":40829,"keystrokes":153,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":15241,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":37,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Those are all great questions, Joseline! Here are the details:\n\n1. **Opening Timeline:** Construction and setup for Lehigh Acres are moving quickly! Selected candidates will begin onboarding and hands-on training very soon ahead of the official grand opening. Exact launch dates will be confirmed during the next stage of the hiring process.\n2. **Pay Rate & Tips:** Barista positions offer a competitive hourly base wage plus tips! Tips are definitely a big part of the earnings at our drive-thru windows and add a great boost to your hourly take-home pay. Specific starting base rates will be discussed in detail during an official offer.\n3. **Team Size per Shift:** Because our space is an efficient 800 sq ft double drive-thru, shift sizes typically range between **3 to 5 team members** during peak morning rushes (covering both windows, espresso, food, and energy drinks) and lean to **2 to 3 baristas** during quieter mid-day and afternoon periods.\n\nYou did a fantastic job throughout this interview. Your drive-thru coffee background, teaching mindset, and positive attitude really shone through.\n\nTo finalize and send your responses to our hiring team, please click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen. Thank you for your time, and we wish you the very best!"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"b"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":8414,"keystrokes":5,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":50021,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":7,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"It looks like that might have been a typo! \n\nWe've completed the interview, and your answers have been recorded. Whenever you're ready, please go ahead and click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen to officially send in your application to our hiring team. \n\nThank you again, Joseline, and have a wonderful day!"}]}]},{"messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Ciara! Welcome, and thank you for your interest in joining our team as a Barista at our brand-new Lehigh Acres location!\n\nBefore we get started, I want to share a few quick details about how this interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of 25 questions.\n- You are free to finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the \"Submit\" button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know right here in the chat whenever you'd like to finish.\n\nTo kick things off with our first question: What made you interested in applying to Ellianos Coffee?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I was interested in applying to Ellianoscoffee because I love coffee."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":42908,"keystrokes":108,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":34673,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":15,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Loving coffee is definitely a great foundation for a barista! \n\nBeyond making great coffee, our brand is really focused on creating a warm, uplifting experience for our guests. How would you describe your natural personality when interacting with people, especially first thing in the morning?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"iâ€™m naturally a morning person, so i love bringing positive energy right from the start! iâ€™m friendly and enjoy making people feel welcome and heard."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":86267,"keystrokes":164,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":79062,"tabSwitches":5,"wpm":17,"pasteAttempts":1,"humanConfidence":56}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That energetic, morning-friendly attitude is exactly what sets the tone for our guests' entire day!\n\nOur drive-thru kiosks operate with a very lean, close-knit crew, meaning every single team member is crucialâ€”especially during those early morning rushes. Do you have reliable transportation, and how do you ensure you are consistently on time for your shifts?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"yes i have reliable transportation, to ensure iâ€™m consistently on time, i always plan to arrive 15 minutes early, which accounts for any unexpected traffic or delays."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":109046,"keystrokes":175,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":17082,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":15,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Planning to arrive 15 minutes early shows great foresight and reliability, which we deeply value.\n\nOur kiosk is a compact, 800-square-foot double drive-thru environment that gets very fast-paced. Baristas are on their feet for their entire shift, constantly moving, bending, and occasionally lifting items like heavy milk crates or bags of ice (up to 30 lbs). How comfortable are you with a role that is this physically active and demanding?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"iâ€™m very comfortable with physically active and demanding role! i actually prefer jobs that keep me moving. iâ€™m used to being on my feet for extended periods and have no issues with lifting. i thrive in fast paced environments and enjoy the challenge."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":103230,"keystrokes":227,"maxInsertChunk":11,"responseDelayMs":17761,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":25,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"It's fantastic that you enjoy staying active on your feet and thrive in that kind of energy!\n\nYou mentioned that you thrive in fast-paced environments. Could you share a specific example from your past work, school, or personal experience where things got super busy or hectic, and how you handled that pressure?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"one time i was volunteering at a local charity event and the number of attendees was way higher than expected. the registration table became swamped and the line was getting really long. i quickly realized we needed to streamline the process. i started by directing people to have their confirmation email ready , then i assigned a few other volunteers to specific tasks: one for checking IDs , one for handling out badges, and another for answering general questions. I also kept a calm and friendly demeanor, even when things were chaotic, which helped keep the attendees relaxed. we managed to clear the line much faster , and everyone eventually got through smoothly."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":314413,"keystrokes":624,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":31471,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":22,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a fantastic example of staying calm, thinking on your feet, and taking the lead to organize a team under pressure.\n\nIn our 800-square-foot drive-thru kiosk, you'll be working shoulder-to-shoulder with 2 to 3 other teammates at top speed. Clear communication is critical to avoid bumping into each other and keeping the flow moving smoothly. \n\nHow do you handle clear, constant communication with your coworkers when you're all moving fast in such a tight space?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"in a tight, face-paced environment, i think clear and concise verbal cues are super important. things like â€œ behind youâ€ â€œ hot coffee coming throughâ€ or â€œ grabbing milkâ€ can prevent collisions and keepeveryone aware of each others movements. i also believe in quick check-ins , like â€œ do you need help with that orderâ€ or â€œiâ€™ve got the next one for youâ€ to make sure weâ€™re always on the same page and supporting each other. itâ€™s all about being proactive and anticipating when your teammates might need."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":284077,"keystrokes":569,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":48649,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":19,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Using call-outs like \"behind you\" and \"hot coffee\" is spot-onâ€”that's standard kitchen safety and keeps everyone safe and moving smoothly!\n\nAt Ellianos, speed has to be balanced with absolute precision. You'll often hear complex drink modifications through your headset (extra shots, alternative milks, specific syrup pumps, sugar-free options) while your hands are already busy making another drink.\n\nHow do you stay organized mentally to ensure you don't miss those small, crucial details when multitasking?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"i use active listening, repeat the order mentally, and break it down into a mental checklist."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":63602,"keystrokes":133,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":45633,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":15,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"A mental checklist is a great way to keep those recipes organized and accurate.\n\nNow, letâ€™s put your multitasking, prioritization, and customer service skills to the test with a real rush-hour scenario:\n\n**You are operating Window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for Window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you at Window A honks, asking for napkins.**\n\nWalk me through your exact thought process to prioritize and handle these tasks."}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"a acknowledge window A , grab napkins , then prioritize starting the complex lotus edge drinks for window B, communicating with the team"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":82862,"keystrokes":155,"maxInsertChunk":13,"responseDelayMs":32353,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":17,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":84}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Quickly handing out the napkins immediately satisfies the customer in front of you without slowing down the lineâ€”great call!\n\nMistakes happen during rush periods, even to the best baristas. Imagine a customer takes a sip of their drink at the window, frowns, and says with frustration: *\"This doesn't taste like what I usually get, and I'm already late for work!\"*\n\nHow would you respond to them in that moment to resolve the issue quickly and leave them with a positive impression?"}]}],"emailSent":true,"status":"Completed","id":"b6ffd863-f5cd-40d2-ad9c-a1f7c1d79ada","candidateInfo":{"phone":"2398340025","name":"ciara christmas","email":"blandonsandra15@gmail.com"},"evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation: Ciara Christmas\n**Position:** Barista â€” Ellianos Coffee (Lehigh Acres)  \n**Candidate Contact:** 239-834-0025 | blandonsandra15@gmail.com  \n\n---\n\n### **1. Final Score: 88 / 100**\nCiara demonstrated strong situational judgment, practical understanding of compact kitchen operations, and an upbeat, customer-ready mindset. Her answers reflected reliability, physical readiness, and calm prioritization under drive-thru pressure.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Summary of Strengths**\n* **Operational & Safety Awareness:** Displayed immediate understanding of working in a small, fast-moving kiosk by proactively mentioning vital call-outs (e.g., *\"behind you,\" \"hot coffee coming through\"*).\n* **Calm Crisis Management & Leadership:** Provided a strong, real-world example from volunteering where she streamlined a bottlenecked registration line by delegating roles and keeping attendees relaxed through a calm demeanor.\n* **Effective Multitasking & Triage:** Accurately prioritized the immediate customer demand (handing napkins to Window A) before coordinating with the team to start the multi-item order for Window B.\n* **Punctuality & Physical Preparedness:** Plans ahead to arrive 15 minutes early to mitigate traffic/delays and expressed genuine enthusiasm for physically active, fast-paced work.\n\n---\n\n### **3. Areas of Concern / Weaknesses**\n* **Brevity in Complex Scenarios:** While her prioritization logic was sound in Response 9, the explanation was very concise and did not fully detail how she would verbally stage or delegate the food/drink preparation.\n* **Incomplete Final Response:** The interview concluded before addressing the last customer de-escalation scenario, leaving conflict resolution skills slightly less explored in depth.\n\n---\n\n### **4. Final Recommendation**\n**Recommendation:** **Hire (or Fast-Track to Brief In-Person Onboarding Interview)**\n\nCiara exhibits the core personality traits and practical instincts needed for a high-volume double drive-thru environment. She understands team communication, stays calm when overwhelmed, and brings a positive, morning-oriented attitude.\n\n---\n\n### **5. Authenticity Assessment**\n\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** **87.5%**\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer:** **Response 3 (56%)**\n* **Answers Below 35%:** **None** (0 responses flagged below 35%).\n* **Style vs. Metrics Agreement:** **Agrees strongly.**\n  * *Metrics Analysis:* Typing speeds remained consistently natural and steady between 15 and 25 WPM. Durations were proportional to answer lengths (e.g., taking over 5 minutes to type the 671-character scenario in Response 6 with 624 keystrokes). Response delays were appropriate (17sâ€“79s), and max insert chunks never exceeded 13 characters.\n  * *Behavioral Details:* Although Response 3 recorded 5 tab switches and 1 paste attempt, the low WPM (17) and proportional keystroke count (164 keystrokes for 149 characters) indicate natural composition rather than external copy-pasting.\n  * *Linguistic Consistency:* The candidate maintained a distinct, highly consistent personal writing style throughout (informal lowercase capitalization for *\"i\"*, spacing before punctuation marks, and authentic conversational phrasing).","position":"Barista","date":"2026-08-25T01:38:57.281Z"},{"position":"Barista","date":"2026-08-24T21:28:08.196Z","status":"Completed","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Yovana! Welcome to your interview for the Barista position at our brand-new Lehigh Acres, FL Ellianos Coffee location. We are thrilled to have you here!\n\nBefore we get started, I want to go over a few quick details about how this interview works:\n* The full interview consists of a maximum of 25 questions, which we will take one at a time.\n* You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n* Alternatively, you can simply let me know right here in the chat whenever you'd like to wrap up.\n\nLetâ€™s start with an easy one: **What made you interested in applying to join the Ellianos Coffee team here in Lehigh Acres?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I love coffee but not also being creative on making drinks and trying new things! I enjoy working with people and making customers feel welcomed to come back! I feel like Ellianosâ€™would be a fun environment to work and learn and to be creative!"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":141348,"keystrokes":316,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":76341,"tabSwitches":3,"wpm":19,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is wonderful to hear, Yovana! We love that energy. Creating a warm, welcoming environment for our customers while crafting great drinks is at the very heart of what we do.\n\nTo help me get to know your customer service style a bit better: **Can you share a quick example of a timeâ€”either in a past job, at school, or in your everyday lifeâ€”where you went out of your way to brighten someoneâ€™s day or make them feel truly welcomed?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"At one of my past jobs, there was a customer who needed help in something I wasnâ€™t sure where to find it but I took my time to help them instead of pointing them to a direction. I made sure they found everything they needed. It reminded me that how small things can make someones day!"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":131462,"keystrokes":295,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":35531,"tabSwitches":3,"wpm":26,"pasteAttempts":1,"humanConfidence":56}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thatâ€™s a fantastic mindset to have, Yovana. Taking ownership instead of just pointing someone away really shows great care for the customer!\n\nOur Ellianos model operates out of a compact 800-square-foot double drive-thru with a lean, tightly knit crew. Because our team is small during each shift, being on time and dependable is absolutely crucialâ€”even one unexpected absence can deeply impact the entire team and our speed.\n\n**Do you have reliable transportation to our Lehigh Acres location, and how do you ensure you consistently arrive on time and ready for your shifts?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes! I always make sure to plan ahead, I always set alarms and always learn early regardless."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":67190,"keystrokes":105,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":5176,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":15,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That proactive planning is exactly what we look for, Yovana! \n\nSpeaking of our 800 sq ft double drive-thru setup, itâ€™s a very fast-paced, physical environment. Our baristas are constantly moving on their feet for entire shifts, stocking supplies (which can include lifting milk crates or ice bags up to 30 lbs), and navigating a compact workspace alongside their teammates.\n\n**How comfortable are you with the physical demands of this role, and how do you keep your energy and focus high during busy, physically active periods?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I feel comfortable! I stay focused on being positive and taking one task at a time. I try not to get overwhelmed and make sure the customer is getting the amazing service. I always stay active and keep a good energy because it helps the shift stay fun!"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":147680,"keystrokes":280,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":6067,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":20,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Staying positive and keeping that high energy really makes a huge difference, especially during our busiest morning rushes!\n\nYou mentioned taking things one task at a time, which is a great way to stay calm. In our double drive-thru, though, things move at lightning speedâ€”you might be pulling espresso shots while simultaneously listening to a customized order through your headset and remembering specific details (like extra pumps, oat milk, or temperature).\n\n**How do you handle remembering detailed instructions or multiple steps when things are moving fast and there are a lot of sounds and inputs happening around you all at once?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I always repeat the instructions back to myself! Even when things get busy or loud I stay calm throughout those situations. So I make sure everything is done correctly"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":85621,"keystrokes":206,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":23452,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":20,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Repeating things back is a great technique to lock in details and prevent mistakes!\n\nBecause our building is only 800 square feet with two active drive-thru windows, you will be working shoulder-to-shoulder with your teammates, moving quickly and sharing equipment like espresso machines, blenders, and food warmers. Constant, clear communication is everything in that space.\n\n**Can you share a specific time when you had to work very closely with a teammate during a busy or stressful moment? How did you communicate with each other to make sure nothing got missed?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"At one of my old jobs, my coworker and i were working by ourselves and our manager was on her lunch. During that time there would be so many customers going through checkout and we had to make sure everyone who needed the help , we had to be available for them! but We communicated to eachother on what we needed to do. my other coworker was overwhelmed so i jumped in the help her out. Communicating make us stay focused and organized"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":138914,"keystrokes":452,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":74470,"tabSwitches":3,"wpm":36,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That kind of teamwork and stepping in to support a teammate when theyâ€™re feeling overwhelmed is vital in our drive-thru environment.\n\nNow, let's put your multitasking, prioritization, and speed to the test with a real-world scenario you might encounter on a busy morning rush:\n\n**You are operating Window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for Window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you at Window A honks asking for napkins. Walk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks.**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would prioritize the task that needs immediate attention! but also being communicated. I would had the napkins to window A and quickly hand them the napkins. Then would focusing on windowâ€™s b order! Since the order is complex. I would ask a teammate to help to comfim order and the order is being made right away! iâ€™d stay focused on the esspreso station, work efficiently so the drinks and food is made correctly."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":213042,"keystrokes":502,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":46331,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":21,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Spot on, Yovana! Handing over those napkins takes two seconds to resolve an immediate concern, and calling out the complex food and drink ticket to your team ensures Window B stays on track without you losing focus on your espresso station. Excellent prioritization!\n\nEven with great focus, in a fast-paced drive-thru mistakes can occasionally happenâ€”for instance, a customer returning to the window saying their drink was made with regular milk instead of oat milk, and they seem frustrated because they're running late for work.\n\n**How would you handle that situation with the customer, and how do you ensure the drink is remade accurately and quickly without disrupting the flow of other orders?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":5213,"keystrokes":14,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":75792,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":23,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Take your time, Yovana! It looks like your message might have cut off. \n\nHow would you handle that situation with the frustrated customer to make it right quickly while keeping the drive-thru moving?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would apologize to the customer and let them know I will make their drink again correctly. I would remake it carefully while keeping up with other orders and let know the team on what i am working on and why. I would double check if the the drink order is correct before handing it back to them"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":95978,"keystrokes":316,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":3131,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":36,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a great approach, Yovana. Sincere ownership, fast correction, and looping in the team makes all the difference when turning a customer's experience around.\n\nOur drive-thru hours start very early in the morning to catch the morning commute, and we are open seven days a week. \n\n**What does your weekly availability look like, and are you fully available for early morning shifts (such as 5:00 AM starts) and weekends?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"i am available Monday-Fri 10am to afternoon"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":33120,"keystrokes":100,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":17577,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":13,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you for sharing that, Yovana. \n\nBecause we operate 7 days a week with heavy morning rushes starting early and peak times extending into the late afternoon/evening and weekends, flexibility is often very helpful for our scheduling.\n\n**Is your availability strictly 10:00 AM to the afternoon Monday through Friday, or do you have any flexibility to take on occasional early morning shifts (like opening at 5:00 AM), evening closes, or weekend hours if needed?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"yes"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":2105,"keystrokes":3,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":6635,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":29,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That flexibility is great to know, Yovana!\n\nAt Ellianos, we pride ourselves on \"Italian Quality at America's Pace,\" meaning our recipes and drink-building standards must be followed precisely so every customer gets the exact same delicious drink every visit. \n\n**How do you typically approach learning and mastering a large menu of recipes and procedures, especially when you need to prepare them quickly from memory?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I tend to remember things when i repeat and break it down to steps. I would learn the common drinks then move on to the rest of the menu! Once im comfortable i would focused s on the speed while making the drinks."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":84251,"keystrokes":205,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":27740,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":31,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Breaking things down into manageable steps and building speed with confidence is the perfect strategy!\n\nIn a fast-paced environment like ours, shift leads and managers often give real-time coaching right on the floor (like tips on steaming milk to the right texture or speeding up your workflow during a rush).\n\n**How do you typically receive constructive feedback or tips on the job, and can you share an example of a time you applied feedback to improve your performance?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I take the feedback positivitybecause theres always room for improvement always. A manager at an old job, gabe me feedback about being more organized whilr handling multiple tasks. I started to make sureWhat i needed to prioritize. Even use the advice on day to day life"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":127883,"keystrokes":279,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":22854,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":22,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a wonderful attitude to have, Yovana. Taking feedback and turning it into a tool for daily growth is a huge asset in a fast-paced environment.\n\nYouâ€™ve done a great job answering our questions today! As we begin wrapping up:\n\n**Do you have any questions for me about the Barista role, our training process, or what itâ€™s like to work at the new Lehigh Acres Ellianos location?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I woukd love to know the training process is like for baristas. and what you looking for the most for someone hoing the lehigh location. What shifts typically look like"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":94447,"keystrokes":189,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":32418,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":19,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":84}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Those are fantastic questions, Yovana! Here is a breakdown of what you can expect:\n\n1. **Training Process:** \nOur training is hands-on and very supportive! Youâ€™ll start with our core drink recipes, espresso calibration, and milk steaming techniques before moving on to specialty drinks (like our Lotus Edge energy infusions) and food items. You'll also practice on the headset and POS systems, and shadow an experienced team member so you can get comfortable with our workflow and speed before handling rushes on your own.\n\n2. **What We Look for Most at the Lehigh Acres Location:** \nSince this is a brand-new store, we are building a strong foundational team culture. We look for **dependability**, a **positive and upbeat attitude**, great **communication**, and an **eagerness to learn**. Speed comes with practice, but bringing great energy and being a supportive teammate every single day is what makes our store successful!\n\n3. **What Shifts Typically Look Like:** \nShifts are generally 5 to 7 hours long and centered around our peak business hours:\n* **Morning Opens (around 5:00 AM â€“ 11:00 AM/Noon):** High volume, fast-paced breakfast rush.\n* **Mid-Day Shifts (around 10:00 AM â€“ 3:00/4:00 PM):** Steady lunch traffic, stocking, and transitioning between rushes.\n* **Afternoon/Closing Shifts (around 1:00 PM/2:00 PM â€“ Close):** Afternoon energy drink/coffee runs, store cleaning, and prep for the next morning.\n\nDo you have any other questions for me, or do you feel ready to submit your application?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes! Submit Application"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":9908,"keystrokes":21,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":34262,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":18,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you so much for your time and thoughtful responses today, Yovana! It was a pleasure speaking with you about the Barista position at our new Lehigh Acres Ellianos Coffee location.\n\nTo officially finalize your interview and send your responses to our hiring team, please go ahead and click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen now.\n\nWe appreciate your interest in joining the Ellianos family and wish you the best of luck! Have a wonderful day!"}]}],"evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation: Barista â€“ Ellianos Coffee (Lehigh Acres)\n\n**Candidate Name:** Yovana Garcia-Ruiz  \n**Phone:** 239-247-0988  \n**Email:** yovanalyalejandra@gmail.com  \n**Position:** Barista  \n\n---\n\n## 1. Overall Score: 85 / 100\n\nYovana demonstrates a very positive, customer-oriented attitude, realistic situational logic for a high-volume drive-thru environment, and an eagerness to learn. Her answers show good teamwork, resilience, and an understanding of operational prioritization during morning rushes.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Summary of Strengths\n\n* **Practical Problem Solving & Prioritization:** Correctly analyzed the rush scenario by resolving an immediate quick need (handing napkins to Window A) while communicating/delegating complex items (Window B drinks/food) to keep the espresso bar moving efficiently.\n* **Team-Oriented Mindset:** Displayed strong proactive teamwork in past roles (stepping in to support an overwhelmed coworker during a rush while their manager was away).\n* **Customer Care & Ownership:** Highlighted personal ownership in customer service by walking customers to items rather than merely pointing them in a direction, and demonstrated proper service recovery steps (apologize, remake accurately, notify team).\n* **Receptiveness to Coaching:** Described a healthy attitude toward on-the-floor feedback, applying manager advice regarding multi-task organization to both work and daily life.\n* **Engagement:** Asked pertinent, practical questions at the conclusion regarding the training process, shift structure, and expectations for the new store.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Areas of Concern / Weaknesses\n\n* **Availability Clarification:** Initially listed availability as Mondayâ€“Friday, 10:00 AM to afternoon. While she confirmed \"yes\" when asked if she had flexibility for 5:00 AM openings, weekends, and closing shifts, her exact weekly availability boundaries need to be locked down in an in-person or phone conversation to ensure schedule alignment.\n* **Brief / Informal Written Style:** Some responses were quite brief (e.g., one-word confirmation on scheduling flexibility), though completely appropriate for an entry-level barista screening.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Authenticity Assessment\n\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** **89.6%**\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer:** **Response 3 (56%)** *(Paste attempts: 1, Tab switches: 3, WPM: 26, Duration: 131.5s)*.\n* **Answers Below 35% Confidence:** **None (0 answers below 35%)**.\n* **Writing-Style Alignment:** **Agrees strongly with metrics.**\n  * The candidate's typing metrics reflect natural, human typing patterns with moderate speeds (13â€“36 WPM), proportional keystroke counts, natural response delays, and realistic organic typos/spelling variations (e.g., *\"positivitybecause\"*, *\"gabe\"*, *\"whilr\"*, *\"woukd\"*). \n  * There are no signs of AI-generated phrasing or automated text generation.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Final Recommendation\n\n**Recommendation: Second Interview (Short In-Person / Phone Screen)**\n\n**Next Steps:**\n1. Invite Yovana in for a brief 10â€“15 minute follow-up interview to meet the store manager.\n2. Specifically confirm her weekly scheduling matrix (confirming early morning 5:00 AM openings and weekend coverage).\n3. If her schedule aligns with the storeâ€™s operational needs, proceed with an offer.","secondInterviewGuide":{"interviewerTips":["Solicitar mÃ©tricas y ejemplos especÃ­ficos de sus empleos previos (volumen de clientes, tiempos de atenciÃ³n, tareas exactas).","Mantener un tono conversacional y de apoyo al explorar incongruencias o la asistencia de herramientas en la prueba escrita sin confrontar.","Observar la energÃ­a corporal, contacto visual y capacidad de sÃ­ntesis verbal mientras responde bajo escenarios simulados de rush."],"decision":{"hire":"Aprobar con calificaciÃ³n >= 4.0 en Bloques must-pass (Disponibilidad, Experiencia, Cierre/Compromiso) y >= 3.0 en InglÃ©s Funcional, con disponibilidad flexible confirmada por escrito para aperturas (5:00 AM) y fines de semana.","decline":"Descartar si se niega a trabajar en turnos de apertura (5:00 AM) o fines de semana, si muestra incapacidad para comunicarse en inglÃ©s bÃ¡sico en ventanilla, o si evidencia actitud defensiva ante la retroalimentaciÃ³n.","thirdConversation":"Si la candidata muestra excelente actitud pero persisten dudas menores sobre la compatibilidad exacta de horarios con la apertura de octubre, realizar llamada final de 10 minutos con el Gerente de Tienda para cuadrar turnos."},"blocks":[{"id":"block_1","title":"Disponibilidad Horaria Real y Puntualidad","goal":"Clarificar la matriz exacta de disponibilidad semanal y garantizar puntualidad estricta para aperturas desde las 4:30/5:00 AM.","minutes":10,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q1","q2"]},{"id":"block_2","title":"Experiencia Operativa y Trabajo en Equipo en Espacios Reducidos","goal":"Verificar la veracidad de su experiencia previa trabajando en equipo bajo momentos de alto volumen y estrÃ©s.","minutes":15,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q3","q4"]},{"id":"block_3","title":"InglÃ©s Funcional y Servicio RÃ¡pido en Drive-Thru","goal":"Evaluar la fluidez, pronunciaciÃ³n y agilidad mental en inglÃ©s al interactuar con clientes en ventanilla.","minutes":10,"mustPass":false,"questionIds":["q5","q6"]},{"id":"block_4","title":"RetenciÃ³n de Recetas y Receptividad al Coaching","goal":"Evaluar su capacidad para memorizar recetas rÃ¡pido y su disposiciÃ³n a recibir correcciones en vivo.","minutes":10,"mustPass":false,"questionIds":["q7","q8"]},{"id":"block_5","title":"Cierre, Honestidad y Compromiso con Lehigh Acres","goal":"Confirmar compromiso fÃ­sico con el rol, despejar dudas del proceso y validar autenticidad de la postulaciÃ³n.","minutes":10,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q9","q10"]}],"generatedAt":"2026-08-24T22:00:36.881Z","questions":[{"id":"q1","block":"block_1","text":"En tu entrevista virtual primero escribiste: 'i am available Monday-Fri 10am to afternoon', pero luego respondiste 'yes' cuando te preguntamos por turnos de 5:00 AM, noches y fines de semana. Si te entregamos tu horario el prÃ³ximo lunes, Â¿cuÃ¡les so