o escolar","Entusiasmo palpable por formar parte de la inauguraciÃ³n de una nueva sucursal"],"redFlags":["Ver el trabajo como algo meramente temporal de pocas semanas","Falta de objetivos de aprendizaje o desinterÃ©s por el producto","Expectativas irreales sobre la carga de trabajo en cafeterÃ­a de autoservicio"]}],"focusPoints":["Evaluar la transiciÃ³n de disciplina deportiva y escolar hacia un entorno laboral formal con estÃ¡ndares comerciales exigentes.","Verificar en vivo la soltura verbal, calidez y capacidad de comunicaciÃ³n proactiva que en la entrevista escrita resultaron muy breves.","Comprobar la receptividad real ante la retroalimentaciÃ³n inmediata y la capacidad de multitarea en un kiosco cerrado de 800 sq ft.","Validar la autenticidad y espontaneidad de sus respuestas tras detectarse patrones de pegado y redacciÃ³n externa en el test virtual."]},"messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Welcome, Nathan! We're thrilled to have you applying for the Barista position at our brand-new Lehigh Acres location.\n\nBefore we get started, I want to share a few quick details about how this interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of 25 questions.\n- You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **Submit** button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know right here in the chat whenever you want to finish.\n\nLet's start with something simple: \n\n**What drew you to apply to Ellianos Coffee, and what excites you most about being in a customer-facing role?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I wanted to apply to Ellianos because I like making drinks. Usually smoothies, and think it would be a good place to get my first work experience. Iâ€™m excited about working with customers, learning how to make coffee and other drinks, and being part of a team. Iâ€™m friendly, willing to learn, and I like helping people."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":39479,"keystrokes":48,"maxInsertChunk":300,"responseDelayMs":132345,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":87,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":40}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thatâ€™s wonderful, Nathan! Making drinks at home is a great starting point, and we love helping people kick off their very first job with us. \n\nSince customer service is a big part of what we do, letâ€™s imagine a common scenario: \n\n**A customer pulls up to your drive-thru window in the morning looking rushed or a bit stressed, and they aren't sure what to order. How would you greet them and help them choose a drink they'll love?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would greet them with a Good morning and ask what kind of drink they usually like.  Iâ€™d ask if they want something hot or cold and if they like their coffee sweet or not too sweet. I would recommend a drink based on what they tell me. I would try to make the experience quick, easy, and friendly since they seem like theyâ€™re in a hurry."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":83824,"keystrokes":56,"maxInsertChunk":372,"responseDelayMs":94048,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":48,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":52}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a great, structured approach! Asking those simple qualifying questionsâ€”hot or cold, sweet or strongâ€”makes it super easy for a rushed customer to decide quickly.\n\nWorking at Ellianos is very active. Our double drive-thru buildings are about 800 square feet, which means you'll be on your feet for shifts lasting 4 to 8 hours, moving continuously in a fast-paced, compact space, and lifting items like milk crates or ice bags up to 30 pounds. \n\n**Have you had experience with activities or routines (like sports, school projects, or chores) that required you to be on your feet and physically active for long stretches? How do you keep your energy up during those times?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes. I've played sports since I was 4. Being on my feet for hours at a time is no problem.  I usually keep my energy up by staying hydrated, and just staying focused on what I need to get done. Iâ€™m pretty good at keeping myself motivated and staying busy."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":119441,"keystrokes":131,"maxInsertChunk":310,"responseDelayMs":82449,"tabSwitches":3,"wpm":25,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":36}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That athletic background is great to hear, Nathan! Playing sports requires real stamina and teamwork, which translates well to our fast-moving drive-thru.\n\nBecause our building is a compact 800-square-foot kiosk, we operate with a lean, tight-knit crew. When one person is late or misses a shift, it immediately impacts the rest of the team and our drive-thru times. \n\n**Do you have reliable transportation to get to the Lehigh Acres location on time for all scheduled shifts, and how do you ensure you are consistently punctual?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes, I have reliable transportation and only live a few miles from the new lehigh location."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":64079,"keystrokes":78,"maxInsertChunk":14,"responseDelayMs":22793,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":15,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":84}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Living so close is a huge plus!\n\nNow, let's step up the pace a bit. In our double drive-thru setup, speed and multitasking memory are essential. You will often be wearing a headset and hearing a new customer's complex order through your ear while your hands are busy steaming milk or blending a smoothie for the car in front of you.\n\n**Can you share an exampleâ€”whether from sports, school, or a projectâ€”where you had to listen to multiple instructions or juggle different tasks at the same exact time without getting confused? How did you handle it?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"One example would be working on a school project with other students. We all had different things we needed to get done. I had to listen to what everyone was saying while also keeping track of my own part. I focused on one thing at a time, and ask questions if I wasn't sure about something. That helped me get everything done without getting confused."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":73694,"keystrokes":58,"maxInsertChunk":378,"responseDelayMs":129078,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":53,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":52}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That method of clarifying details when you're unsure is keyâ€”especially when learning our drink recipes and maintaining \"Italian Quality at America's Pace.\"\n\nWorking closely with a small team in an 800-square-foot space means things move very fast, and sometimes a coworker or manager might need to give you quick, real-time corrections (for example: *\"Catch that espresso shot faster\"* or *\"That needs extra caramel\"*). \n\n**How do you typically handle direct, on-the-spot feedback or constructive criticism when you are right in the middle of a task?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™m okay with being corrected especially if Iâ€™m still learning something. I would listen to what I was told and I would fix it."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":90748,"keystrokes":56,"maxInsertChunk":124,"responseDelayMs":89355,"tabSwitches":4,"wpm":16,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":36}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That teachable attitude is exactly what makes someone thrive here, Nathan.\n\nNow, let's put your critical thinking and multitasking to the ultimate test with a scenario you might encounter during a morning rush.\n\n**You are operating window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you at window A honks asking for napkins.**\n\n**Walk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks.**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would handle the customer in front of me first. Since they are already at my window.  I would quicthem the napkins or let them know Iâ€™ll be right with them. Then I would focus on the order that needs to be made."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":1063,"keystrokes":9,"maxInsertChunk":0,"responseDelayMs":986242,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":2427,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":55}},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":651,"keystrokes":1,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":27384,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":92,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":94}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Handling that quick napkin request right away is spot onâ€”it takes two seconds, keeps the customer happy, and clears your immediate area so you can fully pivot to prep!\n\nTo help us understand how you might fit into the store's schedule, our drive-thru operates early mornings through the evenings, seven days a week.\n\n**What does your typical weekly availability look like (e.g., mornings, afternoons, weekends), and are there any specific days or times you cannot work?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Monday through Friday.  I can work after school 4 to close.  Saturday and Sunday I am available any time."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":158434,"keystrokes":155,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":64222,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":7,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That availability works very well for our afternoon rushes and weekend peak hours!\n\nWe have covered the core areas of the role, and you've done a fantastic job walking through your thought process and sharing your background. \n\n**Do you have any questions for me about the Barista position, our training program, or the new Lehigh Acres location?** \n\n*(Whenever you feel ready, you can also let me know you're finished or click the **Submit** button on your screen to complete your application!)*"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would like to know what the training is like for someone who is new."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":128901,"keystrokes":305,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":141505,"tabSwitches":3,"wpm":7,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Our training program is designed specifically so that anyone, even someone with zero coffee experience, can succeed! \n\nHere is what you can expect:\n1. **Hands-On Pairing:** Youâ€™ll be paired with an experienced Barista Trainer or Manager who walks you through each station step-by-step.\n2. **Recipe & Station Mastery:** Youâ€™ll learn how to pull the perfect espresso shot, steam milk, build specialty drinks (like our signature Freezers and Lotus Edge energy drinks), and prepare hot food items.\n3. **Pacing & Speed:** We start you during calmer shift windows so you can focus on accuracy and drink quality first. As your confidence and muscle memory build, youâ€™ll practice working at our peak drive-thru speeds.\n4. **Team Communication:** You'll get comfortable using the headset, operating the register, and learning how to communicate smoothly with your teammates inside our compact kiosk.\n\nWe don't expect you to know everything on day oneâ€”we focus on your attitude, effort, and willingness to learn!\n\nDo you have any other questions for me, Nathan? If you're all set, you can go ahead and press the **Submit** button on your screen to finalize your application!"}]}],"evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation: Nathan Valentine\n**Position:** Barista â€“ Ellianos Coffee (Lehigh Acres)\n\n---\n\n### **1. Final Score: 85 / 100**\nNathan is a solid entry-level candidate for the Lehigh Acres kiosk. While he lacks formal coffee or retail experience, he demonstrates high coachability, natural customer-oriented logic, physical readiness from his athletic background, and practical common-sense prioritization under pressure. His availability is well-aligned with afternoon and weekend staffing needs.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Summary of Strengths**\n* **Customer Service Mindset & Logic:** Offered structured, practical qualifying questions (e.g., asking hot/cold, sweet/not too sweet) to quickly assist rushed drive-thru customers.\n* **Effective Prioritization:** When presented with competing demands (rush order on headset vs. window customer asking for napkins), correctly prioritized immediately resolving the quick customer touchpoint at the window before turning attention to beverage assembly.\n* **Physical Stamina & Adaptability:** Background in sports since childhood translates well to standing for long shifts and handling active physical work in an 800-square-foot kiosk.\n* **Receptiveness to Coaching:** Stated a healthy, humble attitude toward on-the-spot corrections and direct feedback, which is essential for rapid barista training.\n* **Location & Availability:** Lives just a few miles away; possesses reliable transportation and offers dependable availability for after-school shifts (4 PM to close Mâ€“F) and full availability on weekends.\n\n---\n\n### **3. Summary of Weaknesses / Areas of Concern**\n* **Lack of Prior Work Experience:** This would be his first formal job; he will need onboarding support around workplace standards, commercial pace, and multitasking under sustained rush periods.\n* **Communication Brevity:** Some answers were quite concise, indicating that while his instincts are good, he may need encouragement to proactively communicate and engage in deeper conversations.\n\n---\n\n### **4. Final Recommendation**\n**Recommendation: Second Interview (In-Person)**\n* Nathan shows the right baseline attitude, enthusiasm, and logic for an entry-level barista role. An in-person interview will help confirm his interpersonal warmth, energy, and commitment before extending an official job offer.\n\n---\n\n### **5. Authenticity Assessment**\n* **Average Confidence:** **61.7%**\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer(s):** \n  * **Response 4:** 36%\n  * **Response 7:** 36%\n* **Answers Below 35%:** None recorded (Responses 4 and 7 are the lowest at 36%).\n* **Metric Signals & Writing Style Analysis:**\n  * *Metrics Observations:* Several responses (Responses 2, 3, 4, 6, and 7) showed tab switches, larger chunk insertions (124â€“378 chars), and lower keystroke counts relative to length. Response 8 recorded an abnormally high burst WPM (2,427 WPM) following a long 986-second delay, indicating off-screen drafting or pasting.\n  * *Style Analysis:* The writing style analysis **disagrees** with any suspicion of AI generation or dishonesty. The text consistently reflects authentic, entry-level human speech patterns, complete with minor natural typing artifacts/slips (e.g., *\"I would quicthem the napkins\"*, informal punctuation, and genuine personal anecdotes about youth sports and school projects). The metrics likely reflect a candidate drafting answers in an external notepad or mobile app before pasting. These signals warrant standard verbal confirmation during the in-person interview rather than disqualification.","status":"Completed","emailSent":true,"date":"2026-08-24T18:25:55.728Z","position":"Barista"},{"candidateInfo":{"phone":"2393219657","name":"Jennifer Lopez","email":"jennilopez27@yahoo.com"},"messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Jennifer, welcome! We're excited to learn more about you as we build our team for the brand-new Ellianos Coffee double drive-thru in Lehigh Acres.\n\nBefore we get started, I want to go over a few quick details about how our interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of **25 questions**.\n- You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know here in the chat whenever you would like to conclude.\n\nNo prior coffee experience is necessary to applyâ€”weâ€™re here to learn about your natural disposition and work style!\n\nTo kick things off with our first question: **What made you interested in joining the Ellianos Coffee team here in Lehigh Acres?**"}]}],"date":"2026-08-24T16:10:46.340Z","position":"Barista","status":"Incomplete","id":"f02baaf3-1c00-4b89-9ad2-17db691ee442"},{"deletedAt":"2026-08-25T01:58:46.339Z","position":"Barista","evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation: Barista â€“ Ellianos Coffee\n\n**Candidate Name:** Hailey Myers  \n**Position Applied For:** Barista (Lehigh Acres Location)  \n**Contact Information:** haileymyers012@gmail.com | 239-823-1861  \n\n---\n\n### 1. Final Score: 45 / 100\n\nHailey provides extremely minimal and surface-level responses throughout the interview. While she demonstrates basic customer service instincts (e.g., offering to remake a drink with a calm demeanor), her answers lack depth, detail, and proactive engagement. She struggled to demonstrate multitasking logic, gave vague answers when prompted to expand on past teamwork experiences, and exhibited potential difficulty receiving constructive feedback.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Strengths\n* **Basic Customer Service De-escalation:** Understood the core protocol of remaining calm, apologizing, and remaking an incorrect drink when addressing an upset customer (Response 9).\n* **Punctuality Habits:** Expressed a practical mindset regarding arriving early to ensure reliable attendance (Response 4).\n* **Honest Availability:** Upfront about schooling commitments and scheduling constraints.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Weaknesses & Areas of Concern\n* **Minimal Effort and Communication:** Responses were consistently brief, ranging from one word (\"Good\", \"No\") to fragmented thoughts (\"A medical project\", \"I keep my habits clean\"). Barista roles require strong verbal communication, energy, and outgoing engagement.\n* **Flawed Task Prioritization Under Pressure:** In the drive-thru rush scenario (Window A honking for napkins while Window B has complex drinks), she failed to recognize that completing the quick 2-second task (handing napkins) clears a bottleneck before tackling complex beverage builds.\n* **Receptiveness to Feedback:** When asked how she prefers to receive constructive coaching or corrections, she replied, *\"A congratulations on doing it,\"* which raises concerns about her ability to accept real-time corrective guidance in a fast-paced environment.\n* **Limited Availability:** Enrolled in medical school with availability restricted to evenings and weekends (excluding Monday nights), ruling her out for high-volume morning opening shifts.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Final Recommendation\n**Recommendation:** **Do Not Hire**\n\nHaileyâ€™s minimal engagement during the interview, lack of detail when prompted to elaborate on prior experience, weak prioritization logic, and restricted schedule do not align with the demands of a high-speed, lean-team drive-thru kiosk.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Authenticity Signals\n\n* **Average Confidence:** 97.3%\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer:** Response 9 (64% human-authorship confidence)\n* **Answers Below 35% Confidence:** None\n* **Writing-Style Consistency Analysis:** \n  * The writing-style analysis **agrees** with the high overall confidence metrics. \n  * Response 9 showed a minor drop to 64% due to 2 tab switches and 1 paste attempt over a 127-second delay. However, the resulting text (116 characters, 37 WPM) maintained the same informal tone, minor grammatical errors (\"there drink\", \"need fix\"), and casual structure seen across all other responses. There is no indication of external assistance or AI generation.","emailSent":true,"date":"2026-08-24T13:18:44.249Z","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Hailey! Welcome, and thank you for your interest in joining the Ellianos Coffee team at our brand-new Lehigh Acres location. We're excited to learn more about you today!\n\nBefore we get started, here are a few quick details about how this interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a **maximum of 25 questions**, asked one at a time.\n- You can finish and submit your application at **any time** simply by pressing the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n- You can also just let me know right here in the chat whenever you would like to finish.\n\nTo kick things off with our first question: \n\n**What made you interested in applying to be a Barista with Ellianos Coffee?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I wanted to try a new thing"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":9213,"keystrokes":33,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":18071,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":46,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Trying something new is a great way to grow and learn! \n\nAs a barista at Ellianos, creating a warm, upbeat connection with our customers is a huge part of the daily routine. \n\nHow would you describe your personality when it comes to greeting and interacting with people youâ€™ve never met before?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would like to have a smile on my face when I meet new people"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":17886,"keystrokes":71,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":9772,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":50,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"A friendly smile can truly set a positive tone for a customer's whole day, especially during the morning rush!\n\nOur Ellianos kiosk runs with small, lean teams where every single person counts, so being on time and dependable is essential for the shop to run smoothly. \n\nDo you have reliable transportation to our Lehigh Acres store, and what steps do you take to make sure you're consistently on time for your commitments?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes and leave earlier then my shift"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":11461,"keystrokes":43,"maxInsertChunk":3,"responseDelayMs":26751,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":37,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Leaving early is the best way to avoid unexpected delaysâ€”thatâ€™s a great habit!\n\nOur drive-thru shops are compact (around 800 square feet) and high-energy. The role is very hands-on and physically active, requiring you to be on your feet for your entire shift, move quickly in a tight space, and occasionally lift supplies like milk crates weighing up to 30 pounds.\n\nHow comfortable are you with being on your feet and staying physically active for several hours at a time?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Good"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":2613,"keystrokes":5,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":17806,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":23,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Glad to hear that, Hailey! \n\nAt Ellianos, we pride ourselves on \"Italian Quality at America's Pace.\" That means learning and memorizing dozens of different drink recipes, food items, and customizations so we can make them quickly and accurately.\n\nWhen it comes to learning new routines, recipes, or processes, what methods work best for you to pick things up quickly?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Looking at it and then going straight to it"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":15668,"keystrokes":60,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":20401,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":34,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That hands-on approach is fantastic for a fast-moving environment like ours where you get to practice as you go!\n\nWorking in an 800-square-foot double drive-thru means you and your teammates are sharing a small workspace while moving fast during peak rushes. Communication and teamwork are essential to keep from bumping into each other and keeping the flow smooth.\n\nCould you share an example of a timeâ€”whether at a previous job, in school, or during an activityâ€”where you had to work closely with a team to get things done during a busy or stressful moment?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"In school when I get a busy project"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":13151,"keystrokes":37,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":38528,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":36,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That sounds like a great experience to build on. Could you tell me a little more about a specific project you worked on? \n\nSpecifically, how did you and your group members divide up the tasks and communicate with each other to make sure everything got finished on time?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"A medical project"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":8270,"keystrokes":25,"maxInsertChunk":3,"responseDelayMs":12253,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":22,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"A medical project definitely requires precision and focus!\n\nIn a fast-paced drive-thru, things can sometimes get hectic, and occasionally a mistake happens. \n\nImagine a customer at the window tells you their drink was made completely wrong, and they are visibly upset and in a hurry. How would you handle that situation to make sure the customer leaves happy while keeping the line moving?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would apologize and tell them I would fix there drink and I would stay calm and listen to what they need fix in it"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":41033,"keystrokes":131,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":127311,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":37,"pasteAttempts":1,"humanConfidence":64}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Staying calm, listening, and offering a quick remake is the exact right approach to turn a customer's day around.\n\nNow, let's look at a realistic high-pressure scenario you might experience during a busy morning rush.\n\n**Here is the situation:**\nYou are operating Window A's espresso station. Through your headset, an order for Window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you at Window A honks, asking for extra napkins. \n\nWalk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks and handle everything efficiently."}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would begin to work on the other person order and then would more then welcome help the other person"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":23663,"keystrokes":101,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":83456,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":51,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Handling the immediate needs in front of you while keeping orders moving is always a balancing act! (Pro-tip: Handing out those napkins at Window A takes just two seconds to clear that customer, then you can dive full-speed into making those complex drinks and food for Window B!)\n\nLet's talk about scheduling and availability. Our double drive-thru operates 7 days a week, with opening shifts starting as early as 5:30 AM to catch the morning commute rush.\n\nWhat does your weekly availability look like, and are you available for early morning opening shifts, evenings, and weekends?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Evenings and weekends but I am also in medical school"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":14634,"keystrokes":48,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":24173,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":41,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Balancing medical school alongside a job is very admirable, Hailey! It shows real dedication and drive. \n\nGiven the heavy demands and study load of your classes, how do you manage your time and energy to ensure you stay energized, sharp, and focused during your evening and weekend shifts?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would have to have monday nights off"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":14811,"keystrokes":47,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":16484,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":32,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you for being upfront about needing Monday nights offâ€”that transparency helps us build a schedule that works for everyone.\n\nIn our coffee shop, maintaining strict cleanliness, sanitization, and food safety standards while working at high speeds is vital to keeping our customers safe and the shop running smoothly. \n\nWith your medical school background, how do you see your habits around cleanliness and precision translating into keeping a spotless, safe barista station during a busy rush?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I keep my habits clean"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":9623,"keystrokes":24,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":23224,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":31,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Cleanliness and attention to detail are definitely essential in both healthcare and food service!\n\nAt Ellianos, baristas wear a headset and often listen to a customer placing a new order at the speaker box while simultaneously finishing up a drink or handling cash with their hands. \n\nHave you ever had to listen closely to instructions or information while actively doing a hands-on task, and how do you make sure you don't lose focus or make a mistake?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"By memorizing the ticket that they place"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":19963,"keystrokes":39,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":21829,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":21,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Memorizing the details and keeping an eye on the ticket is a great habit for keeping orders accurate!\n\nIn our high-speed environment, shift leaders and teammates often give immediate, real-time coaching to make sure every drink meets our exact recipe standards. \n\nWhen you're learning a new skill on the fly, how do you prefer to receive feedback or constructive corrections from your team leaders?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"A congratulations on doing it"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":19798,"keystrokes":56,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":19821,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":15,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Positive reinforcement definitely goes a long way in keeping morale high and motivation strong!\n\nOn days when the drive-thru line is non-stop and the pace doesn't slow down for hours, what helps you keep your energy, focus, and enthusiasm high throughout the entire shift?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Moving around and keeping focus"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":7236,"keystrokes":30,"maxInsertChunk":3,"responseDelayMs":10323,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":41,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Staying in motion and maintaining momentum really does help time fly during a rush!\n\nWe have covered a lot of ground today regarding the fast pace, teamwork, and daily life at Ellianos. \n\nDo you have any questions for me about the Barista position, the team culture, or the new Lehigh Acres location?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"No"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":2813,"keystrokes":3,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":10689,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":21,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you so much for taking the time to chat with me today, Hailey! It was a pleasure learning more about you, your availability, and your interest in joining our new Lehigh Acres team.\n\nYou have completed the interview! To finalize and send in your application, please click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen. \n\nOur hiring team will review your application and be in touch regarding the next steps. We wish you the best of luck with both your application and your medical studies! Have a wonderful day!"}]}],"candidateInfo":{"phone":"2398231861","name":"Hailey myers","email":"haileymyers012@gmail.com"},"status":"Completed","id":"984d25ee-714c-43a1-bdab-29740c2afea2"},{"candidateInfo":{"phone":"2392716150","name":"Amariyah","email":"popqueenamariyah@gmail.com"},"position":"Barista","date":"2026-08-24T04:43:48.679Z","id":"4a318459-6107-4f5f-b370-cd6fd483f055","status":"In Progress","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Amariyah! Welcome, and thank you for your interest in joining our brand-new Ellianos Coffee team in Lehigh Acres, Florida! We are thrilled to connect with you today.\n\nBefore we get started, I want to share a few quick details about how this interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of **25 questions**, asked one at a time.\n- You have complete control: you can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know directly here in the chat whenever you'd like to wrap up.\n\nNo prior coffee experience is required to apply, so please just be yourself!\n\nTo kick things off with our first question: **What made you interested in applying for the Barista position at our new Ellianos Coffee location?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™m interested in this position because I like working with and FOR the people so i feel like this would be a great opportunity for me. Iâ€™m also excited about the new location and would love to be apart of the team."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":59402,"keystrokes":212,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":123329,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":42,"pasteAttempts":1,"humanConfidence":64}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That passion for people is wonderful to hear, Amariyah! Connecting with the community is at the heart of what we do.\n\nFor many of our guests, their morning coffee run is the very first interaction they have all day. How do you naturally bring a warm, positive energy to people, especially if they might be in a rush or having a stressful morning?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™d try to be friendly and welcoming without forcing it. A simple â€œI hope you have a great dayâ€ goes a long way. but overall just making the experience calm and smooth for both the customer and myself, and giving them high quality service especially when it comes to their coffee is very effective. Iâ€™d also be patient with them ,greet them with a smile, and have a positive attitude to make the process go by with ease."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":148075,"keystrokes":497,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":63178,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":32,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That genuine, calm approach makes a huge difference, especially during the morning rush.\n\nOur Ellianos model is a compact, 800-square-foot double drive-thru kiosk. That means itâ€™s a high-energy, fast-paced environment where you're on your feet for your entire shift, lifting supplies like milk crates (up to 30 lbs), and working in close quarters alongside your teammates. \n\nHow comfortable are you with a physically active, fast-paced role like this, and how do you usually keep your energy up during a busy day?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Im very comfortable in a physically active, fast paced role especially with much experience from volunteering at the hospital where i was on my feet the whole time i was there running errands and what not. I like staying busy. And I usually keep my energy up on a busy day by being focused , ready for action, and getting a goodnightâ€™s rest."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":105046,"keystrokes":415,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":60455,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":36,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That hospital volunteering background is fantastic experienceâ€”it definitely builds great stamina and a strong service mindset!\n\nBecause our kiosks operate with a lean, tight-knit team on each shift, every single team member is crucial. If one person is late or absent, it directly impacts the entire drive-thru flow.\n\nDo you have reliable transportation to get to our Lehigh Acres location, and how do you ensure you consistently arrive on time and ready to go for scheduled shifts?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes i have a car to get to and from the lehigh acres location. I also live in lehigh so it should never be a problem for me to get there on time. I will definitely ensure iâ€™m at the job at LEAST 15-20 minutes before my shift."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":61720,"keystrokes":244,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":74194,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":47,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":84}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Having your own transportation and living right here in Lehigh is a huge plus, and arriving ahead of time shows great dedication!\n\nAt Ellianos, our promise is \"Italian Quality at America's Pace.\" That means baristas need to learn and memorize dozens of customized drink recipes, syrups, milk types, and temperatures, while making them accurately in just a minute or two.\n\nWhen you have to learn a large amount of detailed information quickly, what methods or study habits work best for you to memorize and master it?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Well iâ€™m in a nursing program which requires a LOT of memorization so trust me I got that down. I tend to use rapid recall, flash cards, or teaching what i learned to someone helps me best to memorize and master."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":67744,"keystrokes":256,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":197110,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":36,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Being in a nursing program is no small featâ€”that level of dedication to rapid recall and active learning is exactly the kind of focus that translates well behind the espresso bar!\n\nIn our 800 sq ft space, you will constantly be crossing paths with your teammates while carrying hot liquids, moving between the blender station, espresso machines, and drive-thru windows. Clear, quick, and respectful communication is essential to keep everyone safe and orders flowing.\n\nCould you share an example of a timeâ€”either in your studies, volunteering, or past workâ€”where you had to communicate quickly and coordinate with others under pressure? How did you handle it?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"During my Nursing studies, Iâ€™ve had to work with classmates during skills check offs where we were under a time limit.  We quickly divided up tasks, communicated what we were doing, and stayed focused so we didnâ€™t miss anything. It taught me to stay calm and communicate clearly when things get busy."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":129548,"keystrokes":331,"maxInsertChunk":2,"responseDelayMs":110371,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":24,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":84}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Skills check-offs under a timer definitely build that calm, precise communication style!\n\nNow, let's step into a high-volume scenario in our drive-thru to see how you prioritize on the fly:\n\n**You are operating Window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for Window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you honks asking for napkins.**\n\nWalk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks."}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"iâ€™d stay focused on the orders first since they involve multiple steps and can take a bit of time. Iâ€™d then quickly communicate with Window B that i heard the order and start on the drinks. Iâ€™d let my other teammate know about the napkins so they can grab them rather than me stopping what iâ€™m doing and slowing down the whole line ."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":86170,"keystrokes":364,"maxInsertChunk":2,"responseDelayMs":82580,"tabSwitches":4,"wpm":45,"pasteAttempts":1,"humanConfidence":56}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"I appreciate how quickly you thought about teamwork and delegating to keep the line moving!\n\nIn a fast-paced drive-thru, occasional mistakes happenâ€”for example, a customer at the window realizes their latte was made with whole milk instead of oat milk, and they are visibly frustrated because they're already running late for work.\n\nHow would you handle this situation at the window to de-escalate their frustration, fix the mistake accurately, and still keep the drive-thru line from backing up?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™d apologize , stay calm, and let them know iâ€™ll get it fixed right away. Iâ€™d quickly remake the latte correctly while keeping the customer updated . then thank them for their patience and make sure they leave happy."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":64562,"keystrokes":254,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":45740,"tabSwitches":3,"wpm":36,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Taking accountability and remaking it swiftly with a calm demeanor is exactly the right approach!\n\nSince you mentioned you are in a nursing program, having a clear and reliable schedule is especially important for our lean-staffed team. \n\nWhat does your general weekly availability look like (mornings, afternoons, weekends), and how do you plan to balance your school commitments with scheduled shifts at Ellianos?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Well although I have school,my schedule is still pretty free. I am free especially on weekends including mornings and afternooons"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":41831,"keystrokes":151,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":47026,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":29,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Weekend availability is always a huge asset in our business!\n\nAt Ellianos, maintaining both high speed and strict Italian quality standards means our shift leads and managers often give quick, direct coaching right in the momentâ€”like adjusting milk steaming temperatures, espresso grind timing, or drink sequencing during a rush.\n\nHow do you typically handle receiving real-time, constructive feedback on the fly while staying focused and positive on your tasks?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I take feedback well and effectively and i do not take it personally . Iâ€™d simply listen , make the adjustment and keep moving while staying positive and calm. Iâ€™d rather get corrected and learn than keep making the same mistake and jeopardizing business."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":61901,"keystrokes":285,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":81983,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":43,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is an exceptional mindset to have, Amariyah. A willingness to learn, adapt quickly, and view feedback as a tool for growth is what turns a good barista into a great one!\n\nLooking ahead, what are you most excited to contribute or learn as part of the founding team launching this brand-new Lehigh Acres Ellianos location? (And please feel free to share any questions you might have for me as well!)"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™m most excited to create a good and positive atmosphere making Lehigh acres feel welcomed at Ellianos. Also I want to build great bonds with my teammates all while learning more and more everyday about coffee. And i canâ€™t wait to grow this place!"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":137886,"keystrokes":360,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":65531,"tabSwitches":3,"wpm":19,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That enthusiasm, community-first heart, and desire to grow alongside your team is exactly the spirit we are looking for to open our Lehigh Acres store! \n\nThank you so much for taking the time to share your background, experiences, and mindset with me today, Amariyah. You did a fantastic job throughout our conversation.\n\nOur hiring team will be reviewing your responses as we assemble the opening crew. We will be in touch regarding the next steps in the hiring process.\n\nTo officially complete and finalize your application, please go ahead and click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen now. \n\nHave a wonderful rest of your day, and thank you again for your interest in Ellianos Coffee!"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Submit"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":8604,"keystrokes":6,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":36073,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":7,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you, Amariyah! Your application has been successfully submitted. \n\nOur management team for the Lehigh Acres branch will review your responses and reach out soon regarding next steps. \n\nWe appreciate your time, energy, and interest in Ellianos Coffee. Best of luck with your nursing program, and have a great rest of your day!"}]}]},{"messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Shift Leader position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Ashley! Welcome, and thank you for applying for the Shift Leader position at our brand-new Ellianos Coffee location in Lehigh Acres! We are excited to get to know you.\n\nBefore we begin, I want to go over a few quick details about our interview process:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of **25 questions**, asked one at a time.\n- You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by pressing the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know here in the chat whenever you would like to wrap up.\n\nTo kick things off with a simple question: What drew you to Ellianos Coffee, and what excites you most about the idea of working at a brand-new location?"}]}],"date":"2026-08-24T02:41:28.422Z","status":"Incomplete","id":"1710a18f-90c1-443e-99dc-1bc5712fb2bc","followUpSentAt":"2026-08-28T01:19:36.562Z","position":"Shift Leader","candidateInfo":{"phone":"2392378573","name":"Ashley Zavala-Govea","email":"ashleymarcela.2006@gmail.com"}},{"position":"Barista","emailSent":true,"candidateInfo":{"phone":"2393099030","name":"Giselle Solorio Gonzalez","email":"gsolo169@icloud.com"},"date":"2026-08-24T02:08:11.415Z","status":"Completed","evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation: Barista â€“ Ellianos Coffee (Lehigh Acres, FL)\n\n**Candidate Name:** Giselle Solorio Gonzalez  \n**Contact:** 239-309-9030 | gsolo169@icloud.com  \n**Target Position:** Barista (Part-Time)  \n\n---\n\n## 1. Final Score: 87 / 100\n\nGiselle is an excellent fit for the fast-paced drive-thru barista role. She brings direct fast-casual order assembly and customer service experience from Panera Bread, displays sound operational logic when handling order rushes, maintains a teachable attitude, and holds reliable transportation. Her limited weekday availability due to school is easily offset by full weekend availability and alignment with a ~20 hour/week part-time schedule.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Summary of Strengths\n\n* **Directly Transferable Experience:** Currently works at Panera Bread in food expo and order hand-off, demonstrating familiarity with speed-of-service metrics, accuracy under rush conditions, and close team coordination.\n* **Sound Prioritization & Operational Logic:** When given a multi-task rush scenario (Window B complex drink/food order vs. Window A customer requesting napkins), she correctly chose to clear the immediate bottleneck (napkins) first, then sequenced the specialty drinks and hot food to preserve product temperature and quality.\n* **Positive Attitude Toward Coaching:** Expressed a clear appreciation for real-time, on-the-spot visual feedback, which is crucial in a fast-paced 800 sq. ft. double drive-thru kiosk.\n* **Proactive Cleanliness & Maintenance:** Understands the necessity of resetting and restocking stations immediately after peak rush periods to prepare for the next surge.\n* **Reliability & Professionalism:** Owns a reliable vehicle, factors in traffic buffers to prevent tardiness, and demonstrated professional integrity by committing to give one week's notice to her current employer.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Areas of Concern / Weaknesses\n\n* **Schedule Constraints:** Giselle is unavailable on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays due to school. While she is fully available on Tuesdays, Thursdays, Saturdays, and Sundays (which covers peak weekend shifts), this limits mid-week scheduling flexibility.\n* **POS / Order-Taking Inexperience:** She noted she has less direct experience on the register/taking orders compared to food prep/expo; however, she demonstrated strong learning methods (pattern recognition for drink builds) and standard training will bridge this gap quickly.\n* **Brief Communication Style:** Some answers were somewhat concise, though they remained directly relevant, honest, and practical.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Authenticity Assessment\n\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** **99.1%** across 18 measured responses.\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer(s):** \n  * **Response 2:** 92% confidence (WPM: 27, Delay: 119.8s, Keystrokes: 167)\n  * **Response 10:** 92% confidence (WPM: 38, Delay: 89.2s, Keystrokes: 220)\n* **Answers Below 35% Confidence:** **None (0)**.\n* **Behavioral & Writing Style Analysis:** \n  * The writing-style analysis **strongly agrees** with the high confidence scores. \n  * Keystrokes and character counts match naturally across all answers, with zero paste attempts recorded.\n  * Typing speeds remained steady and organic (ranging from 13 to 50 WPM for standard answers, with natural burst speed of 76 WPM on an 8-character confirmation).\n  * Tab switches were minimal (1 on R2, 1 on R10) and accompanied by normal typing rhythms and organic delays, representing natural browsing pauses rather than external text insertion or AI generation.\n  * Register and tone remained consistent, authentic, and human throughout.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Final Recommendation\n\n### **Recommendation: HIRE**\n\n**Next Steps:**\n1. Extend an offer for a part-time position (approx. 20â€“25 hours/week) focusing shifts on Tuesdays, Thursdays, and weekend peak morning rushes (Saturday/Sunday).\n2. Pair her with an experienced trainer on the POS/register during onboarding to quickly build her confidence in order taking to complement her already strong expo and beverage prep foundations.","id":"298b09bf-a849-422c-9692-b5d4e9d0e8b1","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Giselle! Welcome to your interview for the Barista position at our brand-new Ellianos Coffee location in Lehigh Acres, FL. We are excited to learn more about you!\n\nBefore we get started, I want to share a few quick details about how this interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of **25 questions**, asked one at a time.\n- You are free to conclude and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen, or by simply letting me know in the chat that you would like to finish.\n\nTo kick things off with our first question: **What made you interested in joining the Ellianos Coffee team here in Lehigh Acres?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I was interested in applying because its definitely closer to my house compared to my current job, and Iâ€™ve heard that the drinks here are really good!"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":58957,"keystrokes":167,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":119832,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":27,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"A shorter commute and great coffee are definitely huge pluses! \n\nSince you mentioned you currently have a job, **what kind of experience do you have with customer service or working in a team environment?** *(No worries if it's not in coffeeâ€”we're just curious about your general background!)*"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I work at Panera. Currently, Iâ€™m one of the main employees who put together the orders and hand them out to customers, so I have a ton of experience when it comes to customer service! Iâ€™m very used to working together with my coworkers to make sure we get the orders done efficiently and as fast as we possibly can."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":146015,"keystrokes":354,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":18441,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":25,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That experience at Panera is fantasticâ€”order assembly and expo definitely require sharp attention to detail and great speed!\n\nSince you handle direct customer interactions daily, could you share a specific example of a time when an order went wrong or a customer was upset, and how you personally handled the situation?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Last week, we had run out of a pastry for an order. So, I decided to offer the customer to either get a refund or get two different pastries to make up for the one they wanted"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":88890,"keystrokes":232,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":30557,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":25,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That was a great, proactive way to turn a potentially frustrating moment into a positive experience for the guest!\n\nAt Ellianos, our store model is unique: we operate out of a compact, 800-square-foot double drive-thru kiosk. It's fast-paced, space is tight, and our baristas are on their feet moving quickly for entire shifts, often lifting things like milk crates or syrup boxes weighing up to 30 lbs. \n\n**How comfortable are you with this kind of close-quarters, physically demanding, and high-energy environment?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™m comfortable with that type of environment"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":31399,"keystrokes":51,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":17965,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":13,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Because we operate with a lean, close-knit team in our double drive-thru, attendance and punctuality are criticalâ€”if one person is late or absent, it immediately impacts the entire flow of the store.\n\nDo you have reliable transportation to and from our Lehigh Acres location, and how do you ensure you are consistently on time for your shifts?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I have my own car, so my transportation is reliable. I usually leave about 5 minutes earlier than I need to just in case thereâ€™s ever traffic"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":58001,"keystrokes":190,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":11276,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":28,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Having your own vehicle and planning ahead for traffic is great to hear!\n\nAt Ellianos, our motto is \"Italian Quality at America's Pace.\" During peak morning rushes, you'll be memorizing multiple custom drink modifications (like alternative milks, syrup pumps, or extra espresso shots) while greeting guests and keeping drive-thru times fast.\n\n**How is your multitasking memory when you have to balance listening to customizations, preparing items quickly, and keeping a warm, friendly conversation going at the window?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would say Iâ€™m capable of multitasking and preparing items quickly. Iâ€™m just not as experienced when it comes to taking orders"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":45500,"keystrokes":141,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":35375,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":29,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is completely okay! We provide thorough hands-on training for our register system and menu. \n\nWhen you are learning a new menu with lots of specific recipes, drink builds, and customizations, **what strategies or methods work best for you to learn and retain that information quickly?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I like to look for patterns when im trying to retain information quickly. I know that drinks that are in the same category (ex: frozen drinks) they have the same base but different syrups and add-ons, at least where I currently work"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":87235,"keystrokes":291,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":32151,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":29,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Spotting patterns across drink bases and builds is actually one of the fastest and smartest ways to master a coffee menu!\n\nNow, let's put your multitasking and prioritization skills to the test with a real-world rush scenario:\n\n**You are operating Window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for Window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you honks asking for napkins. Walk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks.**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would prioritize whatever I can do faster first. So in this scenario, Iâ€™d get the car napkins to move the line ahead. Then, Iâ€™d start on the order for Window B"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":84139,"keystrokes":192,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":70733,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":23,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Handing the napkins right away is a smart moveâ€”it immediately resolves the customer's need at your window and keeps that car moving!\n\nTo take that scenario one step further: **When you turn your attention to that Window B order (the 3 complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and the 2 hot grits bowls), how would you organize the preparation of those specific items to get everything out as quickly and fresh as possible?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™m not sure how exactly the bowls or energy drinks are prepared, but Iâ€™d start on the drinks first, to make sure theyâ€™re made correctly. Then, Iâ€™d move onto the bowls, that way theyre still hot when given to the customer"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":65248,"keystrokes":220,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":89223,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":38,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Keeping the food hot for the guest is a great instinct! \n\nIn that same high-pressure rush, operating in a tight 800 sq ft space with a small team means verbal communication is everything. \n\n**If you ever found yourself falling behind on orders or feeling overwhelmed at your station, how would you communicate with your teammates to ask for help while keeping the energy positive and calm?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™d ask if anyone would be able to help me out after theyâ€™re free from preparing orders in their stations"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":32382,"keystrokes":119,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":15046,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":37,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Clear and respectful communication makes a huge difference in keeping the drive-thru running smoothly!\n\nOur double drive-thru operates early mornings through the evening, seven days a week, with peak rushes often starting as early as 5:30 AM or 6:00 AM. \n\n**What does your general weekly availability look like (e.g., mornings, afternoons, weekends), and are there any specific days or hours you are unavailable?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™d be able to work any hours. But, Iâ€™m unavailable mondays, wednesdays, and fridays due to school."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":41115,"keystrokes":132,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":13610,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":25,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you for letting me know! That means you'd be available on Tuesdays, Thursdays, Saturdays, and Sundays.\n\nGiven your school schedule on those other days, **how many total hours per week are you ideally looking to work at Ellianos?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"at least 20 hours"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":5191,"keystrokes":17,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":8580,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":46,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Got it! That fits well with our part-time scheduling needs across those available days.\n\nIn our drive-thru model, speed metrics (like window times) and quality standards are monitored closely, so shift leads often give quick, real-time coaching while working side-by-side with you. \n\n**How do you typically receive and implement constructive feedback or on-the-spot coaching while working in a fast-paced setting?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I appreciate constructive feedback, especially because it helps me retain the information better. And on the spot coaching is ideal, since I learn better visually"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":95661,"keystrokes":240,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":13456,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":16,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That receptive attitude towards hands-on coaching is essential for quick growth here!\n\nEven though we focus heavily on speed and efficiency at our drive-thrus, our brand identity is built on genuine connectionâ€”many of our guests visit daily, and that 30-to-45-second window interaction might be the brightest part of their morning.\n\n**How do you build a warm, memorable connection with a customer when you only have less than a minute with them at the window?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would ask them how theyâ€™re doing and if they would like anything else. I would also tell them to have a good day as I hand them their order"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":57940,"keystrokes":179,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":16052,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":31,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That friendly, attentive demeanor leaves a lasting impression!\n\nIn our 800 sq ft kiosk, cleanliness and staying stocked are critical so the next rush runs smoothly. When drive-thru traffic slows down between peak rushes, **what kind of tasks do you naturally take the initiative to do to keep your workspace clean and prepped?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"After rushes, I usually wipe down any messes made and put everything back to the way is was to make sure everything is organized and easy to find for the next rush of customers"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":64773,"keystrokes":204,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":14572,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":31,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Wiping down and resetting stations so everything is organized and ready to grab is key to keeping those rush times low!\n\nIf you are selected to join our opening team at the Lehigh Acres location, **how soon would you be available to start training with us?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™d want to give my current job a heads up, so about a week"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":33566,"keystrokes":83,"maxInsertChunk":3,"responseDelayMs":9590,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":25,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Giving your current employer proper notice shows great professionalism and responsibility!\n\nWe have covered all of our key questions today. Do you have any questions for me about the Barista position, our training process, or the new Lehigh Acres location?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"How many people are usually on the line at a time?"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":13143,"keystrokes":56,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":10244,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":50,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Great question! Because our double drive-thru is a compact 800-square-foot kiosk, we typically operate with a lean, highly efficient team. \n\nDuring our peak morning rushes, youâ€™ll usually see **3 to 4 team members** working togetherâ€”typically dedicated roles like Window A/Espresso Barista, Window B/Specialty Drink Barista, a Food & Prep Float, and a Shift Lead/Order Taker. During slower mid-afternoon or evening shifts, that usually scales down to **2 to 3 team members**. Everyone works closely together and communicates constantly!\n\nDid you have any other questions, or do you feel ready to submit your application?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Im ready"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":1577,"keystrokes":8,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":15228,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":76,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you so much for your time today, Giselle! It was a pleasure getting to know you, your background at Panera, and how you handle fast-paced environments.\n\nYou can now click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen to finalize your application. \n\nOur hiring team for the new Lehigh Acres location will review your interview responses and reach out to you with the next steps. We wish you the best of luck and hope you have a wonderful rest of your day!"}]}]},{"date":"2026-08-24T02:07:16.960Z","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Shift Leader position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Giselle! Welcome to the interview for the Shift Leader position at our new Ellianos Coffee location in Lehigh Acres, FL. We are excited to get to know you today!\n\nBefore we begin, I want to share a few quick details about how this interview works:\n* The full interview consists of a maximum of 25 questions.\n* You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by pressing the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n* Alternatively, you can simply let me know in the chat if you wish to finish early.\n\nLetâ€™s start with an easy first question:\n\nWhat sparked your interest in joining the Ellianos Coffee team as a Shift Leader here in Lehigh Acres?"}]}],"candidateInfo":{"phone":"2393099030","name":"Giselle Solorio Gonzalez","email":"gsolo169@icloud.com"},"id":"8027b4c2-3b85-48c9-aaaa-9916dcbe1cc4","followUpSentAt":"2026-08-28T01:19:47.284Z","position":"Shift Leader","status":"Incomplete"},{"candidateInfo":{"phone":"2394107309","name":"Jessy Blanco","email":"scarlethblanco52@gmail.com"},"date":"2026-08-24T01:50:59.796Z","status":"Completed","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Jessy, welcome! It is great to meet you, and thank you for your interest in joining our new Ellianos Coffee team in Lehigh Acres, FL.\n\nBefore we jump in, I want to share a couple of quick details about how this interview works:\n* You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n* You can also simply let me know directly in our chat whenever you'd like to wrap things up.\n* The full interview consists of a **maximum of 25 questions**, and we will go through them one at a time.\n\nTo start off nice and simple: **What made you interested in applying to be a Barista with Ellianos Coffee?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™ve passed where the store is being built as well as seen it on TikTok. Itâ€™s very close to me and I love learning new things"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":26074,"keystrokes":143,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":8424,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":60,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is awesome! Our community on TikTok is definitely growing, and living close by is a huge plus.\n\nOur coffee shops kick off bright and earlyâ€”often before sunriseâ€”to serve that morning rush. \n\n**How do you feel about working early morning shifts, and do you have reliable transportation to get you to the store consistently on time?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I prefer morning shifts and yes I have transportation"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":15806,"keystrokes":61,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":6761,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":34,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is fantastic to hear. Mornings are where the real energy is at!\n\nAt Ellianos, our slogan is \"Italian Quality at America's Pace,\" meaning every guest gets a warm, energetic experience in just a few short moments at the window.\n\n**How do you typically greet someone or make them feel welcomed, even if you only have 30 seconds with them?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Greeting them, making small conversation and always maintaining a positive attitude"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":24344,"keystrokes":85,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":12031,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":27,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"A positive attitude truly goes a long way, especially during a quick drive-thru interaction!\n\nNow, working in our 800-square-foot double drive-thru is very active. You will be on your feet for several hours at a time, moving quickly, bending, reaching, and occasionally lifting supply boxes up to 30 lbs (like milk crates or syrup cases).\n\n**How comfortable are you with a fast-paced, physically demanding environment like this?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Very comfortable, Iâ€™ve worked in similar environments"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":9950,"keystrokes":46,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":7896,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":42,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That's great! Since you've worked in similar settings before, could you share a specific example of a past job or situation where you had to manage a fast-paced, high-energy shift? What were your daily responsibilities there?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™ve worked in fast food, Iâ€™m currently working in the deli at Publix which requires a lot of lifting and standing for long periods of time. I assess customer and serve them as well as do the closing shift cleaning"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":60871,"keystrokes":270,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":4738,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":39,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Publix Deli is known for high standards and a fast pace, so that background is fantastic preparation for our environment!\n\nOur store layout is quite unique: itâ€™s an 800-square-foot double drive-thru. With equipment and several team members moving quickly in a small footprint, constant communication (like calling out \"behind you\" or \"corner\") is essential to keep everyone safe and efficient.\n\n**How do you handle working closely in tight quarters with a team when everyone is moving fast during a rush?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I donâ€™t mind it at all, as long as weâ€™re all working together"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":9901,"keystrokes":59,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":6448,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":79,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Because our kiosk operates with a lean crew of just a few team members at a time, every single personâ€™s presence and punctuality directly impact the entire shift. If one person is late or absent, it immediately puts pressure on the rest of the team.\n\n**How do you ensure you consistently maintain reliable attendance, and how would you handle it if an unexpected emergency ever came up?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"If calling out try to call out in advance so they arenâ€™t caught at the last moment, waking up earlier can also help. If an unexpected emergency came up let the manager know as soon as possible."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":46977,"keystrokes":224,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":9609,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":47,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Clear and prompt communication with leadership is key, especially with a lean team.\n\nLet's dive a bit into the mental side of the job. At Ellianos, customers frequently customize their drinksâ€”such as asking for oat milk, extra espresso shots, specific syrup pumps, or temperature changes. At the same time, you'll be listening to new orders coming in through your headset.\n\n**How do you keep complex orders and recipe details organized in your mind during a rush so you don't mix up ingredients or lose your place?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Memorizing each name and recipe individually, looking at the different types of recipes as well"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":24981,"keystrokes":93,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":27798,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":36,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Memorization and attention to detail are definitely essential skills when crafting our signature drinks!\n\nNow, let's step up the challenge with a real-world scenario you might encounter during a peak rush:\n\n**You are operating window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you honks asking for napkins. Walk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks.**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would try to memorize as much as the customer orders while handing the napkins to window A and quickly take down order B if I canâ€™t keep up I would nicely apologize and ask for the customer to repeat their order"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":67052,"keystrokes":284,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":41791,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":38,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a great approach. Handing over the napkins takes just two seconds to satisfy the guest right in front of you, and asking the headset guest to repeat an item is always better than serving an incorrect order!\n\nIn a fast-paced environment, mistakes can occasionally happenâ€”like a drink made with whole milk instead of oat milk, or an incorrect flavor pump. If a guest brings this to your attention and is visibly frustrated during a peak rush, **how would you handle the situation to make it right while keeping the drive-thru moving smoothly?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Quickly apologize and offer to make their order as quick as possible or having them park aside as we quickly remake the drink."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":39341,"keystrokes":159,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":14368,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":35,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Apologizing genuinely and remaking it right away is the perfect way to turn that guest's day around.\n\nDuring our grand opening training, you'll be learning dozens of recipes, drink builds, and speed-of-service techniques very quickly, and trainers will often give real-time coaching while you're on the line.\n\n**How do you typically receive constructive feedback or on-the-spot corrections during a shift?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Either being told or show is a good way to receive feedback rather than doing it incorrectly multiple times"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":34531,"keystrokes":141,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":42941,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":33,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That openness to learning by being shown and coached is so important, especially as we launch this brand new store.\n\nIn a drive-thru kiosk, there will occasionally be brief lulls between rushes. Cleanliness, restocking, and prep work keep the store running smoothly when the next rush hits.\n\n**When things slow down and there are no immediate orders on screen, what do you naturally look to do to keep yourself productive and help the team?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Anything that can be cleaned or if a teammate needs help making a drink or taking an order I can step up"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":22649,"keystrokes":108,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":10756,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":58,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Taking the initiative to restock and support your teammates during downtime makes all the difference!\n\nLooking at scheduling for the Lehigh Acres store, we are open seven days a week from early morning to evening.\n\n**What is your general weekly availability (days of the week and times of day you are available to work), and are you looking for part-time or full-time hours?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™m looking for full time hours preferably mornings"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":14363,"keystrokes":55,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":4263,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":33,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Full-time morning availability fits our schedule needs very well, especially for the high-volume morning rushes!\n\nSince weekends are typically our busiest days of the week, **are you available to work Saturday and Sunday mornings, and if offered the position, how soon would you be able to start?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes as soon as possible"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":9985,"keystrokes":46,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":6355,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":30,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you for sharing that, Jessy. Weekend morning availability and being ready to start right away is a huge asset as we gear up for opening.\n\nWe've covered all the key areas regarding the Barista role, your experience, and the fast-paced drive-thru environment at our new Lehigh Acres store.\n\nBefore we conclude, **do you have any questions for me about Ellianos Coffee, the role, or the next steps in our hiring process?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"What are the next steps?"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":5823,"keystrokes":25,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":5387,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":52,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Great question! Here are the next steps:\n\n1. **Review:** Our hiring and store management team for the new Lehigh Acres location will review your responses and qualifications from this interview.\n2. **Follow-Up:** If your profile is a strong match for the team, we will reach out via phone or email within the next few business days to discuss the next stage, which typically includes an in-person meeting and details regarding training dates for the grand opening.\n\nTo finalize and officially send your application over to our team, please go ahead and click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen now.\n\nThank you so much for your time today, Jessy. It was a pleasure speaking with you, and we wish you the best of luck!"}]}],"position":"Barista","emailSent":true,"id":"c87d0617-b711-4a92-a42d-b4f8f3bcb14f","secondInterviewGuide":{"interviewerTips":["Jessy escribe de forma muy resumida pero con lÃ³gica operativa impecable; en la entrevista presencial empÃºjala a desarrollar respuestas con anÃ©cdotas detalladas, nombres de herramientas y mÃ©tricas de tiempo.","Realiza simulaciones dinÃ¡micas de pie (roleplay en ventanilla y toma de Ã³rdenes) para medir su lenguaje corporal, sonrisa y ritmo vocal natural.","Reconoce su autenticidad comprobada (100% confianza humana en telemetrÃ­a) y enfÃ³cate en verificar si su disposiciÃ³n para aprender rÃ¡pido encaja con el ritmo del Grand Opening en octubre."],"decision":{"hire":"CalificaciÃ³n promedio >= 4.0/5.0 en bloques must-pass, demostrando excelente proyecciÃ³n de energÃ­a en ventanilla, solidez fÃ­sica verificable en Publix Deli, total disponibilidad para aperturas 4:30 AM y actitud receptiva al entrenamiento acelerado de barismo.","decline":"CalificaciÃ³n <= 2.5 en cualquiera de los bloques must-pass, tono apagado o antipÃ¡tico en ventanilla, dudas sobre transporte seguro a las 4:30 AM, o falta de resistencia para el trabajo continuo de pie en 800 sq ft.","thirdConversation":"Dudas en la velocidad de memorizaciÃ³n de recetas o timidez inicial en los roleplays que pueda subsanarse con un segundo filtro con el Store Manager para evaluar coaching directo en barra."},"blocks":[{"id":"block_1","title":"Experiencia Operativa y Resistencia en Publix Deli / Fast Food","goal":"Verificar la solidez de sus hÃ¡bitos de trabajo fÃ­sico, manejo de herramientas de cocina/deli y protocolos de ritmo continuo.","minutes":12,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q1","q2"]},{"id":"block_2","title":"EnergÃ­a en Ventanilla y Calidez de Servicio al Cliente","goal":"Evaluar si Jessy proyecta la chispa, extroversiÃ³n y empatÃ­a requeridas para crear conexiones memorables de 30 segundos en drive-thru.","minutes":12,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q3","q4"]},{"id":"block_3","title":"Curva de Aprendizaje en Recetas, Multitarea y Coachability","goal":"Determinar su mÃ©todo real para retener combinaciones complejas de bebidas y su respuesta a la correcciÃ³n inmediata en barra.","minutes":12,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q5","q6"]},{"id":"block_4","title":"English Functional Drive-Thru Interaction & Speed Roleplay","goal":"Confirm natural English fluency, energetic tone, and active listening when taking complex drive-thru orders.","minutes":10,"mustPass":false,"questionIds":["q7","q8"]},{"id":"block_5","title":"AdaptaciÃ³n al Modelo Kiosco 800 sq ft, Madrugadas y Lehigh Acres","goal":"Validar su compromiso con turnos desde 4:30 AM, trabajo en espacios estrechos y su motivaciÃ³n para la apertura de octubre.","minutes":9,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q9","q10","q11"]}],"generatedAt":"2026-08-24T02:02:55.216Z","questions":[{"id":"q1","block":"block_1","text":"En tu entrevista virtual mencionaste: 'Iâ€™m currently working in the deli at Publix which requires a lot of lifting and standing for long periods of time. I assess customer and serve them as well as do the closing shift cleaning'. CuÃ©ntame un turno especÃ­fico de mÃ¡ximo volumen en Publix: Â¿cuÃ¡ntos clientes atendÃ­as por hora, quÃ© cargas pesadas manejabas y cÃ³mo mantuviste el ritmo durante 6 u 8 horas continuas sin bajar la calidad?","language":"es","purpose":"Verifica si su experiencia fÃ­sica y de servicio en Publix Deli respalda la demanda fÃ­sica de 8 horas de pie en Ellianos.","listenFor":["Detalles especÃ­ficos de tareas pesadas (freidoras, cajas de pollo/embutidos, limpieza profunda)","HÃ¡bitos concretos para mantener la resistencia y energÃ­a constante","Conciencia de tiempos de atenciÃ³n y estÃ¡ndares de servicio al cliente"],"redFlags":["Respuestas monosilÃ¡bicas o incapacidad de detallar su rutina diaria en Publix","Quejas sobre el esfuerzo fÃ­sico o la fatiga en turnos largos","Desconocimiento de mÃ©tricas de servicio o flujo de clientes"]},{"id":"q2","block":"block_1","text":"El deli de Publix y los kioscos de Ellianos comparten altos estÃ¡ndares de inocuidad y sanitizaciÃ³n. Cuando te tocaba el cierre o cambio de estaciÃ³n en Publix, Â¿cuÃ¡l era tu checklist mental para dejar el Ã¡rea impecable y lista para el siguiente turno?","language":"es","purpose":"EvalÃºa el rigor higiÃ©nico y la proactividad en el mantenimiento de estaciones de trabajo limpias.","listenFor":["MenciÃ³n de protocolos de sanitizaciÃ³n, control de contaminaciÃ³n cruzada y fechas/temperaturas","Enfoque en dejar la estaciÃ³n lista para el turno entrante sin dejar pendientes","Orgullo por mantener Ã¡reas de trabajo limpias y ordenadas"],"redFlags":["Ver la limpieza como un castigo o tarea secundaria","Falta de estructura en pasos higiÃ©nicos bÃ¡sicos","Dependencia total de que un supervisor le diga quÃ© limpiar"]},{"id":"q3","block":"block_2","text":"Por escrito seÃ±alaste que tu forma de conectar en 30 segundos es 'Greeting them, making small conversation and always maintaining a positive attitude'. En la prÃ¡ctica de Ellianos buscamos 'Italian Quality at America's Pace'. Hazme una demostraciÃ³n en vivo aquÃ­ mismo: yo soy un cliente que llega apurado a las 6:30 AM en ventanilla A. Â¿CÃ³mo me saludas, me entregas mi bebida y me sacas una sonrisa en 15 segundos?","language":"es","purpose":"EvalÃºa en tiempo real su energÃ­a vocal, contacto visual, calidez y carisma en ventanilla rÃ¡pida.","listenFor":["Sonrisa genuina, contacto visual directo y tono de voz alegre y seguro","InteracciÃ³n fluida sin sonar robotizada o forzada","Manejo natural de la entrega rÃ¡pida combinada con un saludo cÃ¡lido"],"redFlags":["Lenguaje corporal tÃ­mido, retraÃ­do o con la mirada hacia abajo","Tono plano, apagado o apÃ¡tico","Incapacidad de improvisar una interacciÃ³n cordial y rÃ¡pida"]},{"id":"q4","block":"block_2","text":"En el cuestionario indicaste que ante una orden errÃ³nea tu soluciÃ³n es 'Quickly apologize and offer to make their order as quick as possible or having them park aside as we quickly remake the drink'. CuÃ©ntame de una ocasiÃ³n real en tu trabajo anterior donde un cliente te gritÃ³ o se mostrÃ³ sumamente frustrado: Â¿cuÃ¡les fueron tus palabras exactas y cÃ³mo controlaste tus emociones?","language":"es","purpose":"Comprueba su temple, desescalamiento emocional y madurez frente a clientes conflictivos bajo presiÃ³n.","listenFor":["Capacidad de mantener la calma y no tomar la agresiÃ³n de manera personal","Uso de empatÃ­a y enfoque inmediato en la soluciÃ³n prÃ¡ctica","ResoluciÃ³n sin generar cuellos de botella en la operaciÃ³n"],"redFlags":["Ponerse a la defensiva o discutir con el cliente","Bloquearse o entrar en pÃ¡nico ante reclamos enÃ©rgicos","Culpar a otros compaÃ±eros de turno frente al cliente"]},{"id":"q5","block":"block_3","text":"Mencionaste que para aprender recetas complejas tu mÃ©todo es 'Memorizing each name and recipe individually, looking at the different types of recipes as well'. Dado que no tienes experiencia previa como barista en espresso bars, Â¿cuÃ¡l es tu tÃ©cnica de estudio para memorizar en menos de 1 semana mÃ¡s de 30 combinaciones de shots, leches alternativas, siropes y temperaturas?","language":"es","purpose":"Identifica si tiene un sistema de retenciÃ³n efectivo para superar la curva tÃ©cnica del barismo.","listenFor":["MÃ©todos concretos de memorizaciÃ³n (tarjetas nemotÃ©cnicas, repeticiÃ³n activa, esquemas de ingredientes)","Compromiso de estudiar guÃ­as de recetas en su tiempo de inducciÃ³n","ComprensiÃ³n de que cada segundo y cada onza cuenta en la consistencia de la marca"],"redFlags":["Confiar Ãºnicamente en la memoria visual sin mÃ©todo de estudio","Subestimar la complejidad de las recetas de cafÃ© y bebidas energÃ©ticas","DesinterÃ©s por aprender la tÃ©cnica detrÃ¡s de la extracciÃ³n y texturizado de leche"]},{"id":"q6","block":"block_3","text":"Escribiste que 'Either being told or show is a good way to receive feedback rather than doing it incorrectly multiple times'. CuÃ©ntame de un momento en que un lÃ­der te llamÃ³ la atenciÃ³n enfrente de otros o corrigiÃ³ tu tÃ©cnica en medio de un rush. Â¿CÃ³mo reaccionaste en ese instante y quÃ© ajuste hiciste en tu forma de trabajar a partir de ese dÃ­a?","language":"es","purpose":"Verifica su receptividad al coaching en tiempo real sin resentimientos ni frustraciones.","listenFor":["AceptaciÃ³n madura y agradecimiento por la retroalimentaciÃ³n inmediata","Capacidad de aplicar el ajuste tÃ©cnico al siguiente pedido sin perder el ritmo","Foco en la mejora continua y el Ã©xito del equipo"],"redFlags":["FrustraciÃ³n visible o quejas de sentirse expuesta por los lÃ­deres","Justificar el error en lugar de asumir la correcciÃ³n","Repetir el error por no prestar atenciÃ³n a la demostraciÃ³n"]},{"id":"q7","block":"block_4","text":"Let's do a quick roleplay in English: You are wearing the headset at Window A. A guest drives up and orders: 'A large iced Caramel High 5 with oat milk, extra caramel drizzle, and a sausage and cheese biscuit.' But our oven is currently reheating and the biscuit will take 4 minutes. How do you respond to the guest clearly, warmly, and offer a great fast alternative?","language":"en","purpose":"Evaluates speed of thought, English customer service tone, and upselling/alternative offering abilities.","listenFor":["Polite, clear, and proactive communication in English","Offering an immediate alternative (e.g., muffins, breakfast bagel, or pulling forward politely)","Keeping high energy and cheerful hospitality tone"],"redFlags":["Freezing up or struggling with basic conversational English","Simply saying 'we don't have it' without offering a substitute or solution","Unclear pronunciation that could confuse drive-thru guests"]},{"id":"q8","block":"block_4","text":"Ellianos is famous for 'Italian Quality at America's Pace'. When you have cars queued in both Lane A and Lane B during the morning rush, what key phrases do you use over the headset to acknowledge both cars promptly so no guest feels ignored?","language":"en","purpose":"Tests dual-lane drive-thru awareness and customer reassurance skills in English.","listenFor":["Prompt acknowledgement phrases (e.g., 'Good morning, welcome to Ellianos! I will be right with you in just one moment!')","Friendly, energetic vocal projection","Calm tone despite double-headset pressure"],"redFlags":["Leaving a lane in complete silence for over 15 seconds","Rushed, irritated, or aggressive tone of voice","Confusion between managing headset cues and physical window tasks"]},{"id":"q9","block":"block_5","text":"Mencionaste vivir muy cerca de la nueva ubicaciÃ³n de Lehigh Acres y preferir turnos matutinos ('I prefer morning shifts and yes I have transportation'). Nuestras aperturas implican estar en tienda a las 4:30 AM con las luces encendidas y las mÃ¡quinas calibradas. Â¿CuÃ¡l es tu rutina exacta para levantarte a las 3:30 AM y garantizar que nunca llegarÃ¡s tarde?","language":"es","purpose":"Asegura la viabilidad real de su transporte y disciplina para turnos de apertura ultra tempranos.","listenFor":["Rutina de sueÃ±o planificada y alarmas redundantes","Medio de transporte propio y confiable confirmado","Entendimiento del impacto crÃ­tico de la impuntualidad en una cuadrilla pequeÃ±a de 4 personas"],"redFlags":["Depender de terceros o transporte pÃºblico incierto a las 4:00 AM","Minimizar la dificultad de levantarse de madrugada de forma consistente","Historial previo de tardanzas en trabajos matutinos"]},{"id":"q10","block":"block_5","text":"Sobre el espacio de 800 sq ft respondiste: 'I donâ€™t mind it at all, as long as weâ€™re all working together'. En un espacio tan compacto, chocar o derramar cafÃ© caliente es un riesgo constante. Â¿CÃ³mo manejas la comunicaciÃ³n preventiva con tus compaÃ±eros ('behind you', 'hot water', 'corner') cuando el ritmo es frenÃ©tico?","language":"es","purpose":"EvalÃºa hÃ¡bitos de seguridad fÃ­sica, espacialidad y trabajo en equipo sincronizado en kioscos reducidos.","listenFor":["Uso natural y constante de comandos verbales de seguridad","Conciencia espacial y cuidado por la integridad de los compaÃ±eros","DisposiciÃ³n para adaptarse a movimientos coordinados tipo 'baile en cocina'"],"redFlags":["Incomodidad o claustrofobia en espacios con 4-6 personas en movimiento","Omitir llamadas verbales por timidez o descuido","Actitud individualista en lugar de sincronizada"]},{"id":"q11","block":"block_5","text":"Tu prueba virtual demostrÃ³ una redacciÃ³n 100% natural, fluida y transparente, lo cual valoramos enormemente en Ellianos. De cara a la gran apertura de Lehigh Acres en octubre, Â¿quÃ© te entusiasma mÃ¡s de ser parte del equipo fundacional y quÃ© podemos esperar de tu compromiso en los primeros 90 dÃ­as?","language":"es","purpose":"EvalÃºa honestidad, motivaciÃ³n intrÃ­nseca y lealtad con el proyecto de apertura de la nueva tienda.","listenFor":["Orgullo por participar en un Grand Opening desde cero","Deseo de crecer dentro de Ellianos Coffee y dominar la estaciÃ³n de Barista","Disponibilidad total para las semanas intensivas de entrenamiento previas a octubre"],"redFlags":["Ver el trabajo como algo pasajero sin compromiso a mediano plazo","Falta de entusiasmo o desinterÃ©s por la cultura de la marca","Conflictos imprevistos de horario en las fechas clave de apertura"]}],"focusPoints":["Evaluar el nivel de calidez, extroversiÃ³n y proyecciÃ³n de energÃ­a presencial, contrastando su estilo de comunicaciÃ³n escrito muy conciso con las exigencias de ventanilla rÃ¡pida en Ellianos.","Comprobar la capacidad real de absorciÃ³n rÃ¡pida de recetas de barismo y cafÃ© de especialidad, dado que no cuenta con experiencia previa en preparaciÃ³n de espresso.","Validar la resistencia fÃ­sica, ritmo operativo y hÃ¡bitos de puntualidad para aperturas a las 4:30 AM en un kiosco de 800 sq ft, derivado de su experiencia en Publix Deli.","Verificar la comunicaciÃ³n en equipo y manejo de espacio reducido bajo alta presiÃ³n de doble carril drive-thru."]},"evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation Report\n\n**Candidate Name:** Jessy Blanco  \n**Position Applied For:** Barista (Lehigh Acres Location)  \n**Email:** scarlethblanco52@gmail.com | **Phone:** 239-410-7309  \n\n---\n\n## 1. Overall Score: 88 / 100\n\nJessy demonstrates strong operational suitability for the Barista role at Ellianos Coffee. Her relevant background in customer-facing food prep, ideal availability, proximity to the store, and practical problem-solving during fast-paced scenarios make her a well-qualified candidate for the grand opening team.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Summary of Strengths\n\n* **Relevant Fast-Paced Experience:** Currently works at Publix Deli and has fast-food experience, environments known for heavy lifting, prolonged standing, sanitation protocols, and high customer interaction.\n* **Ideal Schedule & Proximity:** Lives very close to the new store, prefers early morning shifts, is available for high-volume weekends (Saturday/Sunday), and is ready to start immediately on a full-time basis.\n* **Practical Drive-Thru Problem Solving:** Demonstrated sound instincts in drive-thru pacing scenariosâ€”such as quickly handing out napkins while taking headset orders, and offering to pull a car aside during drink remakes to keep the drive-thru line moving.\n* **Team-First & Coachable Attitude:** Expressed a strong willingness to learn, receptive attitude toward direct coaching/demonstration, and initiative to clean and assist coworkers during downtime.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Summary of Weaknesses & Areas of Concern\n\n* **Brief Communication Style:** Answers were concise and to the point. While clear and practical, in-person communication should be evaluated to ensure she brings warm, outgoing energy to window interactions.\n* **Coffee Recipe Learning Curve:** Lacks prior specialty coffee/barista-specific experience, meaning she will need hands-on training during the grand opening ramp-up to master recipe builds and speed of execution.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Final Recommendation\n\n**Recommendation:** **Second Interview (In-Person)**\n\nJessy meets all core requirements: ideal availability, relevant food service experience, practical thinking under pressure, and geographic convenience. An in-person interview with the Store Manager is recommended to confirm cultural fit, energetic customer presence, and finalize shift scheduling.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Authenticity Signals\n\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** **100%** (across all 15 recorded responses; Response 1 had no metrics recorded).\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer:** None (all recorded responses scored **100%**).\n* **Answers Below 35% Confidence:** **None**.\n* **Typing Metrics & Behavioral Analysis:**\n  * **Typing Speeds:** Natural typing cadence ranging between **27 WPM and 79 WPM**.\n  * **Paste / Insertion Events:** **0 paste attempts**; maximum text insertion chunks ranged from 1 to 10 characters, consistent with organic single-character and auto-correct typing.\n  * **Navigation & Delays:** **0 tab switches** throughout the entire assessment. Response delays (4.3s to 42.9s) and typing durations reflect organic reading, thinking, and drafting.\n  * **Writing Style Alignment:** The qualitative writing analysis **fully agrees** with the 100% metric. Jessy's register is consistently natural, conversational, and direct with no signs of external AI generation or copied material."},{"id":"f8a558ee-e6da-4672-868f-c665f449a71d","evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation: Barista Position\n\n**Candidate Name:** Sierra Maldonado  \n**Position:** Barista (Lehigh Acres Location)  \n**Phone:** 239-691-3848  \n**Email:** slmaldonado239@icloud.com  \n\n---\n\n## Final Score: 85/100\n\nSierra presents as a polite, earnest, and highly coachable entry-level candidate. While she is currently in high school and lacks direct prior barista experience, she displays strong personal accountability, positive interpersonal skills, and an eagerness to learn. Her availability aligns well with operational needs for high-volume morning weekend shifts and weekday evening coverage.\n\n---\n\n## Strengths\n* **Reliability & Attendance:** Demonstrates strong discipline, citing a perfect school attendance record, reliable transportation, and proactive personal time-management strategies (calendars, alarms, adequate rest).\n* **Customer Service & Positivity:** Shows a naturally warm and service-oriented demeanor. She understands the importance of small gestures (compliments, de-escalating customer complaints with a no-fuss remake and apology).\n* **Coachability:** Highly receptive to direct feedback and real-time coaching, viewing it as an opportunity to improve rather than personal criticism.\n* **Operational Habits:** Understands fundamental kitchen and beverage station practices, notably the \"clean as you go\" approach to avoid clutter and stress.\n* **Targeted Availability:** Weekday evenings and weekend mornings provide coverage across high-demand retail and peak drive-thru periods.\n\n---\n\n## Weaknesses & Areas for Growth\n* **Lack of Direct Fast-Paced Experience:** Some operational scenario responses were slightly simplistic (e.g., suggesting making \"small talk\" with an overwhelmed coworker during a peak rush rather than stepping in to assist with physical prep/station support).\n* **Multitasking/High-Stress Execution:** Will require structured training on managing simultaneous auditory inputs (headset), order queue pacing, and physical beverage crafting.\n\n---\n\n## Authenticity Assessment\n\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** **100%**\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer:** None (All recorded responses scored 100%).\n* **Responses Below 35% Confidence:** None.\n* **Behavioral & Typing Analysis:** The candidate's typing data shows completely natural human cadence, with typing speeds averaging between 14 and 50 WPM, appropriate keystroke counts, zero paste attempts, zero tab switches, and standard input durations.\n* **Style Consistency:** The writing style is consistent, conversational, and authentic to an entry-level applicant across all responses. The writing-style analysis is in full agreement with the high-confidence telemetry data.\n\n---\n\n## Final Recommendation: Hire / Proceed to In-Person Store Interview\n\n**Recommendation:** **Hire (or proceed to final brief in-person interview with Store Manager)**  \nSierra possesses the baseline enthusiasm, coachability, and reliability needed to succeed in an entry-level Barista role at Ellianos. Her positive demeanor and availability make her a strong fit for the team at the new Lehigh Acres location.","position":"Barista","status":"Completed","candidateInfo":{"phone":"2396913848","name":"Sierra Maldonado","email":"slmaldonado239@icloud.com"},"messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Welcome to Ellianos Coffee, Sierra! We are thrilled to consider you for our team at the brand-new Lehigh Acres location. \n\nBefore we jump in, here are a few quick notes on how our interview works:\n- The full, expected interview consists of a maximum of **25 questions**, asked one at a time.\n- You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by pressing the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n- You can also simply tell me right here in the chat whenever you'd like to finish.\n\nTo kick things off with our very first question: \n\n**What got you interested in joining Ellianos Coffee as a Barista?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"What got me interested is that itâ€™s a family owned coffee shop. I thought it was really neat idea since we donâ€™t have a lot of family owned stores around. Iâ€™m also interested in working as a barista because I want to meet new people, and connect with them. I also would love to learn how to make coffees. I think this job would suit me because iâ€™m really looking for something hands on, and that will keep me going and busy."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":202973,"keystrokes":502,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":22427,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":24,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That family-oriented feel and community connection is truly at the heart of what we do at Ellianos, and we definitely have a fast, hands-on environment to keep you energized! \n\nSince you mentioned wanting to connect with new people, could you tell me about a timeâ€”either at a previous job, school, or in your everyday lifeâ€”when you went out of your way to brighten someone's day or make them feel welcome?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I love to compliment people, I feel like itâ€™s such a small gesture that makes a big difference. I like to see people smile and have a good time."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":50199,"keystrokes":167,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":15194,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":35,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"A genuine compliment can completely turn someone's day around, and our drive-thru guests will love that positive energy!\n\nAt Ellianos, our building is a compact, 800-square-foot double drive-thru. Itâ€™s very fast-paced, and youâ€™ll be on your feet for entire shifts, moving quickly around your coworkers, and occasionally lifting supplies like milk crates or ice buckets (up to 30 lbs). \n\nHow do you feel about working in a physically demanding, tight space like that for several hours at a time?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I feel like it could be a good fit for me. I am definitely quick learning and I like to ask for help so iâ€™m clear on what iâ€™m doing and not making mistakes."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":48908,"keystrokes":170,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":22801,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":42,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Asking questions and communicating with your team is a huge strength in our fast-paced setup!\n\nBecause our double drive-thru kiosk runs on lean, tight-knit staffing, every single team member's presence is essentialâ€”an unexpected absence or tardiness can really impact the whole team and slow down service. \n\nDo you have reliable transportation to the Lehigh Acres location, and how do you ensure you are consistently on time and ready for your scheduled shifts?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I do in fact have reliable transportation. How I ensure myself that I am on time and ready for my shift is setting alarms, getting a good nights rest, and thinking positively. I am really good with time management"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":72449,"keystrokes":220,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":24599,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":32,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Setting alarms and coming in well-rested makes a huge difference, Sierra! \n\nYou mentioned you're really good with time management. Could you share a specific example from work, school, or personal life where you had multiple tasks competing for your attention at the exact same time, and how you managed to get everything done?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"At school I am very busy with work assignments and tasks. I am at school everyday, I do not skip school and iâ€™ve never been absent. I also plan out my tasks by putting the dates or times in a calendar so iâ€™m better prepared."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":86677,"keystrokes":266,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":14567,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":31,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Having a perfect attendance record and keeping yourself organized with a calendar shows great discipline!\n\nIn a high-volume drive-thru, things move very fast, and sometimes a customer might receive a drink that wasn't made quite how they like itâ€”or they might simply be in a rush and frustrated. \n\nIf a customer at your window handed a drink back and said it tasted completely wrong, how would you respond to them in that moment while keeping the line moving?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would simply apologize for the inconvenience and remake their drink how they wanted it with no complaints. Iâ€™m very understanding with other people and I get where they come from, so iâ€™d rather keep the misunderstanding positive with customers."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":69478,"keystrokes":268,"maxInsertChunk":11,"responseDelayMs":27059,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":35,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That calm, gracious attitude is exactly what diffuses tense moments and keeps customers coming back!\n\nNow, let's step up the pace a bit. In our drive-thru, you'll be wearing a headset. That means you might be steaming milk or wiping down a counter while simultaneously listening to a new order coming through your ear, all while keeping an eye on the order screen.\n\nHow do you stay focused and remember the details of what you're hearing while your hands are busy doing something completely different?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"How I stay focused is not letting anyone or anything distract me while I work. Serving customers and making a positive impact is my main goal when working."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":58014,"keystrokes":181,"maxInsertChunk":2,"responseDelayMs":42363,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":29,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Staying focused on the customer is definitely the right mindset!\n\nNow, let's put your multitasking and prioritization to the test with a real-world scenario you might encounter on a busy morning rush:\n\n**You are operating Window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for Window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you at Window A honks asking for napkins.**\n\nWalk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks step-by-step."}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I think I would quickly serve them their napkins because itâ€™s a quick and easy simple task. Once iâ€™m done with that customer I would quickly get the other customers drinks prepared and ready while also apologizing to them for the long wait."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":65734,"keystrokes":244,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":38990,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":39,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Taking care of the quick, immediate need right in front of you so that car can be on their way is a great call!\n\nIn that same tight space, teamwork and communication are everything. During a major rush, shift leads or coworkers might need to give you quick, direct coaching or redirect tasks in the heat of the moment to keep the drive-thru moving smoothly. \n\nHow do you typically handle fast, direct feedback while working under pressure?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I typically handle it in a positive way because employee feedback is what I want. If an employee can redirect me in a positive manner iâ€™m all for it because it can improve my skills in the future. I take the feedback and process it and do better with the next customer."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":98468,"keystrokes":287,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":27884,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":32,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That coachable mindset is fantastic, Sierra. Being able to adapt on the fly makes our team so much stronger.\n\nEllianos serves our communities early in the morning and throughout the afternoon and evenings, 7 days a week. \n\nWhat does your weekly availability look like for shifts (including early mornings, evenings, or weekends), and roughly how many hours per week are you looking to work while balancing school?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"For shifts, since iâ€™m still in school, iâ€™d prefer doing evenings during the week, and mornings on the weekends. During the week it allows me to get done with any homework I have. During the weekends it allows me to get a fresh start of my day working in the morning."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":79559,"keystrokes":296,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":30962,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":38,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That schedule fits really nicely with our peak hours, especially on weekend mornings! \n\nAt Ellianos, our promise is \"Italian Quality at America's Pace,\" which means our baristas need to learn and memorize quite a few recipesâ€”syrup pump counts, espresso shot timings, milk temperatures, and custom drink buildsâ€”so we can craft them with precision and speed.\n\nWhen you're faced with having to memorize a lot of new information or steps quickly, what study or learning techniques work best for you?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I like to write and take notes with new information and study them at home. It makes for a peaceful study and ensures I have memorized everything."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":50571,"keystrokes":181,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":14868,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":32,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Taking the initiative to review notes at home shows wonderful dedication, and that will definitely give you a head start with our menu recipes!\n\nBeyond crafting drinks, maintaining a clean and sanitized workspace is vital in our 800-square-foot kioskâ€”especially during peak rushes when milk, syrups, and ice are moving fast. \n\nHow do you approach keeping your station clean, organized, and stocked when orders are constantly coming in?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I like to clean up as I go. I donâ€™t like to do something and clean it later because it creates a big mess and stress."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":41434,"keystrokes":130,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":15098,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":38,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"\"Clean as you go\" is the absolute golden rule in our drive-thruâ€”it keeps everything running safely and smoothly!\n\nWorking in close quarters with a small crew means your energy directly impacts the whole team. If you noticed a coworker was feeling overwhelmed or falling behind on their station during a big morning rush, how would you step in to support them while keeping up with your own duties?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would give them a positive boost by telling them they are doing great and keep up the good work. I would also have small talk with them to make sure their ok and to understand what their feeling."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":66431,"keystrokes":211,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":20777,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":35,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That emotional support and encouragement can really lift the team's spirits!\n\nAt Ellianos, our standard of \"Italian Quality\" means that whether it's the 5th drink of your shift or the 100th, every single cup needs to be made accurately and taste delicious. \n\nWhen you're doing repetitive, hands-on tasks for several hours, how do you keep yourself alert and ensure your attention to detail doesn't slip?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Getting good sleep and eating a balanced breakfast is important to me to keep my brain awake and running. I donâ€™t like to be tired when iâ€™m working because I think that just causes me to not work at my full potential."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":70607,"keystrokes":235,"maxInsertChunk":2,"responseDelayMs":21535,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":36,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Taking care of yourself before a shift is so key to staying consistent and energized throughout the day!\n\nLooking ahead, what are you most excited to learn or achieve during your first few months as a Barista on our team?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™m very excited to learn how to make coffee and make new friends."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":54979,"keystrokes":73,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":30795,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":14,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Making great coffee and building strong bonds with your team are two of the best parts of the job!\n\nAs we wrap up our conversation today, do you have any questions for me about the Barista role, our training process, or the new Lehigh Acres location?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"No I donâ€™t have any questions. Thank you so much though."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":28459,"keystrokes":76,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":11990,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":23,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"You're very welcome, Sierra! It was such a pleasure speaking with you and learning more about your positive attitude, strong work ethic, and dedication. \n\nThat concludes all of my questions for today. Please go ahead and click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen to finalize your application. \n\nOur management team for the Lehigh Acres location will review your responses and be in touch regarding next steps. Have a wonderful rest of your day!"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Thank you, you as well!"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":6058,"keystrokes":24,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":20967,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":50,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you, Sierra! Don't forget to press that **\"Submit\"** button on your screen. Take care, and have a great day!"}]}],"date":"2026-08-24T01:37:13.827Z","emailSent":true},{"date":"2026-08-24T01:00:29.649Z","id":"3295db2b-f5b4-468e-905d-51662b612a00","candidateInfo":{"phone":"2394785817","name":"Amy Joseph","email":"amyjoseph0909@gmail.com"},"position":"Barista","status":"Incomplete","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Amy! Welcome to your interview for the Barista position at our brand-new Ellianos Coffee in Lehigh Acres, FL. We are excited to connect with you!\n\nBefore we get started, here are a few quick details about how our interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of 25 questions, taken one at a time.\n- You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know directly in the chat whenever you'd like to finish.\n\nTo kick things off with a simple question: What made you interested in joining the Ellianos team, and what is your absolute favorite drink to start your day?"}]}]},{"id":"d528ed24-ea48-4456-950e-0aaef8d78dd6","secondInterviewGuide":{"interviewerTips":["Exige ejemplos reales con detalles concretos (quÃ© hizo, cÃ³mo reaccionÃ³ la otra persona y tiempos exactos) en lugar de respuestas hipotÃ©ticas sobre lo que 'harÃ­a'.","EvalÃºa la energÃ­a fÃ­sica, tono de voz y desenvolvimiento natural en persona para confirmar la agilidad que exige el ritmo 'Italian Quality at America's Pace'.","Aborda el tema de la telemetrÃ­a y uso de herramientas externas de man