ctado directamente por ti en el momento?","language":"es","purpose":"EvalÃºa la honestidad, transparencia y autoconciencia del candidato en un entorno de confianza sin emitir juicios.","listenFor":["Respuesta transparente, tranquila y sin titubeos","ExplicaciÃ³n lÃ³gica de su proceso de reflexiÃ³n al responder","Coherencia entre su forma de expresarse oralmente y lo escrito"],"redFlags":["Nerviosismo extremo o contradicciones evidentes frente a las mÃ©tricas de tecleo","Respuestas evasivas que busquen ocultar la realidad en lugar de ser honesta","Discrepancia abismal entre su nivel de anÃ¡lisis oral y el contenido virtual"]},{"id":"q11","block":"block_5","text":"Lehigh Acres es una apertura desde cero donde buscamos formar un equipo sÃ³lido y duradero. Â¿QuÃ© metas personales o profesionales buscas cumplir en Ellianos Coffee y quÃ© te motivarÃ­a a quedarte a largo plazo como parte del equipo?","language":"es","purpose":"EvalÃºa la estabilidad, proyecciÃ³n y alineaciÃ³n del candidato con el crecimiento de la nueva sucursal.","listenFor":["Deseo de estabilidad laboral y desarrollo de habilidades operativas","AlineaciÃ³n con el ambiente y ritmo de la marca","Compromiso de permanencia durante el periodo de apertura y estabilizaciÃ³n"],"redFlags":["Ver el puesto Ãºnicamente como un empleo pasajero de muy corto plazo (semanas)","Falta de interÃ©s en el crecimiento o en la cultura de Ellianos","Expectativas salariales o de rol desalineadas con la posiciÃ³n de barista"]}],"focusPoints":["Verificar la compatibilidad y consistencia de su disponibilidad restringida (tardes de Lunes a Jueves desde 2:00 PM, Viernes desde 12:00 PM y fines de semana completos) con la cobertura de turnos de cierre y alta demanda.","Evaluar a fondo su protocolo de atenciÃ³n y resoluciÃ³n de quejas en ventanilla (remakes rÃ¡pidos y desescalamiento), Ã¡rea que respondiÃ³ de forma muy escueta en la fase virtual.","Comprobar su capacidad de comunicaciÃ³n en tiempo real y recepciÃ³n de feedback directo en un entorno fÃ­sico de 800 sq ft, contrastando la respuesta de menor confianza de autorÃ­a (Respuesta 6).","Validar su mÃ©todo de aprendizaje visual y memoria procedimental para dominar el recetario de alta velocidad de Ellianos previo a la apertura de Lehigh Acres."]},"evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation: Emily Roda\n**Position Applied For:** Barista (Ellianos Coffee â€“ Lehigh Acres)  \n**Contact:** emilyroda.21@gmail.com | (239) 324-6431  \n\n---\n\n## 1. Final Score: 88 / 100\n\nEmily demonstrates a warm, customer-focused attitude, strong self-awareness regarding multitasking and communication, and a clear, logical thought process when handling peak drive-thru rushes. Her score reflects strong operational alignment, with minor points deducted due to weekday morning availability limitations for a high-volume morning coffee concept.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Strengths\n* **Customer-Centric Mindset:** Shows a natural enthusiasm for uplifting customer moods and delivering positive hospitality during morning routines.\n* **Logic Under Pressure:** Handled the complex multi-tasking rush scenario (Response 8) exceptionally wellâ€”prioritizing immediate customer acknowledgment, clear headset delegation to teammates, and station accuracy.\n* **Proximity & Reliability Buffer:** Lives 5 minutes away and proactively plans a 20â€“30 minute buffer to prevent tardiness.\n* **Communication & Receptiveness:** Expresses a clear appreciation for direct feedback, real-time kiosk communication, and resolving issues without conflict or grudges.\n* **Continuous Learning:** Self-identifies as a visual learner who takes initiative to review notes at home to master recipes.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Weaknesses & Areas of Concern\n* **Weekday Morning Availability:** Available starting at 2:00 PM Mondayâ€“Thursday and 12:00 PM Friday. Given that Ellianos experiences peak volume during early morning opening hours, her availability is restricted to afternoon/closing shifts and weekends.\n* **Succinct Conflict Resolution:** Response to handling drink remakes (Response 9) was somewhat brief; she would benefit from training on customer recovery protocols and speed-of-service de-escalation.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Final Recommendation\n**Recommendation:** **Second Interview** (In-Person / Shift Verification)\n\n*Rationale:* Emily has the right disposition, physical stamina, and prioritization skills for an Ellianos drive-thru kiosk. The hiring manager should conduct an in-person follow-up primarily to verify that her afternoon/closing and weekend availability aligns with store staffing needs.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Authenticity Assessment\n\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** **93.0%**\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer:** **Response 6 (56%)** (Second lowest: Response 8 at 76%)\n* **Answers Below 35% Confidence:** None.\n\n### Behavioral & Writing Style Analysis\n* **Typing Metrics vs. Tone:** The writing-style analysis **strongly agrees** with human authorship. The candidate's typing speeds were steady and natural (averaging between 18 and 30 WPM), with normal response delays and proportional keystroke counts.\n* **Tab Switches & Paste Attempts:** \n  * Response 6 recorded 1 paste attempt and 3 tab switches over a 154-second duration.\n  * Response 8 recorded 4 tab switches over a 351-second duration.\n  * *Context:* The extended durations, low WPM (21 WPM), and natural conversational language (including informal grammar/spelling like *\"tho\"*, *\"right it down\"*, *\"with cautions\"*) indicate the candidate was drafting manually and thinking through their answers rather than using AI generation or copying external text.","emailSent":true,"messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Emily! Welcome to your interview with Ellianos Coffee for our brand-new Lehigh Acres location. We're excited to learn more about you today!\n\nBefore we get started, here are a few quick guidelines for our conversation:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of 25 questions.\n- You are free to finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know right here in the chat whenever you'd like to finish.\n\nTo kick things off with our first question: \n\nWhat excited you most about applying to join our team as a Barista here at Ellianos Coffee?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"being able to put a smile on peoples faces with an amazing coffee"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":25956,"keystrokes":55,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":46124,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":30,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thatâ€™s a wonderful attitude to have! Brightening someone's morning with great energy and a delicious drink is truly at the heart of what we do.\n\nSince morning coffee runs are often the first interaction someone has during their day, how do you typically handle or connect with a customer who might be arriving in a rush or having a rough morning?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"always try to have a great attitude because sometimes all it takes is someone being nice to you to brighten your mood or day"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":32661,"keystrokes":97,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":59229,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":44,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is so true, a little genuine kindness goes a long way!\n\nAt Ellianos, we run a double drive-thru model that often starts very early in the morning and operates with lean, tight-knit teams where every single team member is essential. \n\nDo you have reliable transportation to ensure you can consistently make scheduled shiftsâ€”including early morning openersâ€”and how do you keep yourself organized and punctual?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"yes i have reliable transportation, even tho i live 5 minutes away i would always try to starting getting ready way ahead of time and leave my house 20-30 mins early cause you never know what can happen on the way"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":111131,"keystrokes":203,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":17394,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":22,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Living close by and giving yourself that 20â€“30 minute buffer is fantastic practice!\n\nOur drive-thru kiosks are uniqueâ€”they're about 800 square feet, which means space is compact, movement is constant, and our baristas are on their feet for entire shifts, often bending, reaching, and lifting items like 30-pound boxes of milk or ice buckets. \n\nHow comfortable are you with being on your feet and staying physically active for several hours at a time during a busy shift?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"yes im comfortable with that, im a very active person so i enjoy keeping myself busy"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":42689,"keystrokes":76,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":19486,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":22,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That active energy will definitely serve you well in our fast-paced setup!\n\nBecause our double drive-thru moves so quickly, baristas often need to listen to an incoming order through a headset while simultaneously preparing another drink or ringing up a customer at the window. \n\nCan you share an experienceâ€”whether from work, school, or daily lifeâ€”where you had to juggle multiple fast-moving tasks at the same time, and how you managed to keep everything straight?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"one experience iâ€™ve had would be in school when i had multiple assignments with the same deadline and also having to come home and help take care of my baby siblings but i decided to give each task a certain amount of time so i can get it done and not overwhelm myself"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":154274,"keystrokes":301,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":142864,"tabSwitches":3,"wpm":21,"pasteAttempts":1,"humanConfidence":56}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Time-blocking and staying calm under pressure is a great strategy for keeping yourself grounded!\n\nWorking in an 800-square-foot kiosk means you'll be working shoulder-to-shoulder with 2â€“4 other team members during peak rushes, constantly sharing equipment and moving around each other quickly.\n\nHow do you feel about communicating constantly in real-time with teammates (like calling out your movements or asking for a quick hand), and how do you handle quick, direct feedback in the heat of a busy moment?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"communicating is a very important skill especially in such a small space , i also feel like direct feedback is good. let someone know how you feel instead of trying to throw hints or even hold grudges"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":125632,"keystrokes":224,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":75253,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":18,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Spot onâ€”clear, direct communication keeps the whole team running smoothly and prevents misunderstandings.\n\nNow, let's put you into a real peak-rush scenario to see how you think on your feet:\n\nYou are operating window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you honks asking for napkins. \n\nWalk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks."}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"i would prioritize the tasks based on urgency and what helps my team and our line moving as quickly as possible. First i would acknowledge the customer who asked for napkins and let them know iâ€™ll help them with their napkins as soon as possible Then ill communicate with my team through the headset and let them know the order from window b is coming in . I would start working on the espresso orders quickly but with cautions because i want everyone to get the exact drink and enjoy it to the max then iâ€™d make sure the grits is being worked one by the appropriate team member . Most importantly ill always communicate with team so everything runs smoothly"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":351763,"keystrokes":680,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":120266,"tabSwitches":4,"wpm":21,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a great breakdownâ€”acknowledging the customer right in front of you, delegating via headset, and keeping your station moving accurately are exactly the keys to success in that situation.\n\nCoffee recipes at Ellianos have specific syrup pumps, espresso shot timings, and milk proportions. If a customer tastes their drink at the window and mentions it doesn't taste quite right, how would you handle the situation to ensure they leave happy without holding up the drive-thru line?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"i would ask them what they think the drink is lacking on and try to fix it from there"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":51586,"keystrokes":120,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":23304,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":22,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That's a very practical approachâ€”finding out the specific issue quickly so you can make it right!\n\nOur menu has quite a variety of offeringsâ€”from signature espresso drinks and freezers to Lotus energy drinks, smoothies, and breakfast itemsâ€”all with precise recipes that need to be prepared in seconds.\n\nHow do you typically approach learning and memorizing a lot of new information or recipes when starting in a new environment?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"im a visual learner so seeing other making items or someone teaching it to me really makes it stick and i would try to right it down and memorize it when i get home so i donâ€™t mess up no ones order in the future"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":90736,"keystrokes":253,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":22009,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":30,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Writing things down and reviewing them is an excellent habit, and that dedication to getting orders right shows great pride in your work!\n\nBecause our store is open seven days a week from early mornings into the evening, schedules often include weekends, early opening shifts, and occasionally helping cover a teammate's shift on short notice. \n\nWhat does your general weekly availability look like, and how flexible are you when it comes to working weekends or varying shift times?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Mondays - Thursday im available from 2pm til closing and Fridays im available 12 til closing and Saturday and Sundays i have open availability"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":79564,"keystrokes":138,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":18650,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":18,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you for sharing your availability details, Emily! That afternoon, evening, and full weekend flexibility is very helpful.\n\nYouâ€™ve done a wonderful job answering all of our questions and giving us a clear picture of your energy, communication skills, and how well you'd fit into our fast-paced drive-thru environment.\n\nDo you have any questions for me about the role, the team, or the new Lehigh Acres location? \n\n*(Whenever you feel you are ready to conclude and submit your application, you can go ahead and press the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen!)*"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"what skills would i develop working with your team?"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":78649,"keystrokes":57,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":68312,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":7,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Working as a Barista at Ellianos Coffee will help you build a strong and versatile skillset that will benefit you throughout your career! Here are a few key areas youâ€™ll really develop:\n\n1. **Mastery of Specialty Coffee & Beverages:** Youâ€™ll learn the art and science of espresso extraction, milk steaming/texturing, syrup ratios, and crafting high-volume specialty drinks quickly and consistently.\n2. **High-Speed Multitasking & Prioritization:** Working in our fast-paced, double drive-thru environment will sharpen your mental agility, helping you make quick decisions under pressure without sacrificing quality.\n3. **Advanced Communication & Team Collaboration:** Operating closely with your team in an 800 sq ft kiosk will turn you into an exceptional communicator, teaching you how to coordinate movements, give and receive feedback, and support your teammates seamlessly.\n4. **Customer Connection & Conflict Resolution:** Youâ€™ll gain experience in turning around tough situations, reading customer needs in seconds, and delivering memorable hospitality that keeps regulars coming back.\n5. **Efficiency & Spatial Awareness:** Youâ€™ll master lean speed of service, clean-as-you-go habits, and time management skills.\n\nIs there anything else you'd like to ask, or are you ready to finalize your interview? \n\n*(Whenever you are ready, you can simply click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen to complete your application!)*"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"what are the next steps in the hiring process"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":27018,"keystrokes":60,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":14872,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":20,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Great question! Here are the next steps in our hiring process:\n\n1. **Application Review:** Our management team for the new Lehigh Acres location will review your full interview transcript and application details.\n2. **Follow-Up Contact:** If your profile is a strong match, a manager will reach out to you via phone or email (usually within a few business days to a week) to schedule an in-person interview or meet-and-greet.\n3. **Onboarding & Training:** From there, selected candidates will receive formal offers, followed by orientation and hands-on training to get you fully prepped for opening day!\n\nTo make sure your responses are sent directly to the hiring team, please go ahead and click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen now. \n\nThank you so much for your time and enthusiasm today, Emily! We wish you the best of luck!"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"thank you"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":3994,"keystrokes":9,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":18795,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":30,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"You're very welcome, Emily! \n\nIt was a pleasure speaking with you today. Whenever you're ready, please make sure to click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen to complete your application. \n\nHave a wonderful rest of your day, and take care!"}]}],"status":"Completed","position":"Barista","date":"2026-08-23T23:50:07.072Z","candidateInfo":{"phone":"2393246431","name":"Emily Roda","email":"emilyroda.21@gmail.com"}},{"status":"Completed","id":"7bea92fe-29e7-43b7-9e50-2f2570f3da10","position":"Barista","evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation: Yuseli Perez\n**Position:** Barista  \n**Location:** Lehigh Acres â€“ Ellianos Coffee  \n**Contact:** 239-738-8225 | yuseli_aiyana@icloud.com  \n\n---\n\n### **1. Final Score: 74 / 100**\nYuseli demonstrates practical problem-solving logic, a calm customer-first demeanor, and basic kitchen safety awareness suitable for a fast-paced drive-thru coffee environment. However, significant weekday availability constraints and brief communication on physical demands slightly temper her overall score.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Summary of Strengths**\n* **Practical Prioritization & Multi-tasking:** When presented with a high-pressure scenario (Window A honking vs. Window B large drink/food order), Yuseli showed excellent instinct by quickly handing napkins to resolve the immediate distraction before focusing methodically on the complex drink tickets.\n* **Kitchen Communication & Safety Awareness:** Demonstrated understanding of kitchen callouts (*\"behind you\"*, *\"coming through\"*) to maintain team safety within a compact 800 sq. ft. kiosk.\n* **Customer Service & Recovery Mindset:** Handled the incorrect order scenario appropriately with a polite apology and an immediate remake.\n* **Receptiveness to Feedback:** Open to hands-on coaching and demonstrated the ability to apply constructive feedback to improve accuracy under pressure.\n\n---\n\n### **3. Summary of Weaknesses & Areas of Concern**\n* **Restricted Availability:** Unavailable all day on Tuesdays, Thursdays, and Fridays; only available after 5:00 PM on Mondays and Wednesdays. While she has open weekend availability, reaching her target of 15â€“29 hours per week may be difficult depending on store operating hours and evening shift volume.\n* **Terse Communication on Physical/Logistical Demands:** Provided minimal one-to-three word responses (*\"i feel good\"*, *\"yes\"*) regarding physical standing/lifting and transportation reliability.\n* **Written Communication Nuance:** Minor grammatical and phrasing slips (e.g., *\"fast paste\"* instead of fast-paced, *\"hot grip bowls\"* instead of hot grits bowls), though these do not hinder her suitability for a frontline barista position.\n\n---\n\n### **4. Final Recommendation**\n**Recommendation: Second Interview (Phone / In-Person Screen)**\n\n* **Rationale:** Yuseliâ€™s service attitude, prioritization logic, and willingness to learn make her a strong cultural fit. A brief follow-up conversation is recommended to confirm whether her restricted weekday evening and weekend availability aligns with the Lehigh Acres store's current scheduling requirements.\n\n---\n\n### **5. Authenticity Assessment**\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** **98.7%**\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer(s):** Response 2 (**92%**) and Response 8 (**92%**).\n* **Answers Below 35%:** None.\n* **Typing Signals & Writing Style Analysis:**\n  * **Consistency:** The writing-style analysis strongly **agrees** with the high confidence scores. \n  * **Typing Mechanics:** Typing metrics display natural human keystroke patterns, realistic durations, normal response delays, and zero paste attempts.\n  * **Stylistic Continuity:** Language style, tone, and organic phonetic spelling variations (e.g., *\"fast paste business\"*, *\"hot grip bowls\"*) are consistent and fully authentic throughout the interview transcript. There are no signs of automated text generation or outside assistance.","date":"2026-08-23T22:44:10.680Z","candidateInfo":{"phone":"2397388225","name":"Yuseli Perez","email":"yuseli_aiyana@icloud.com"},"emailSent":true,"messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Yuseli! Welcome, and thank you for your interest in joining our team at the brand-new Ellianos Coffee in Lehigh Acres!\n\nBefore we jump in, I want to share a few quick details about how this interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of 25 questions.\n- You have the freedom to finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the \"Submit\" button on your screen, or you can simply let me know right here in the chat whenever you're ready to conclude.\n\nWe are excited to learn more about you! To kick things off with our first question: \n\nWhat made you interested in applying for a Barista role with Ellianos Coffee?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"iâ€™m interested in being a barista at Ellianos coffee because it looks like a friendly environment fast paste business"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":67844,"keystrokes":76,"maxInsertChunk":12,"responseDelayMs":123796,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":17,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"A friendly attitude and a love for a fast-paced environment are both fantastic qualities for a barista! \n\nSince creating a welcoming environment for our guests is so important to us, how do you personally make sure a customer feels warmly welcomed, even when you only have a minute or two to interact with them?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would make them feel welcoming by being friendly, speaking kindly and having patience"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":48460,"keystrokes":53,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":52331,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":17,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Patience is definitely a valuable quality to have, especially in customer service! \n\nCould you share an example of a timeâ€”whether at work, school, or in your personal lifeâ€”when you had to stay patient with someone who was stressed, upset, or in a rush? How did you handle that situation?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"A classmate of mine was stressed and upset because they lost something valuable to them how I handled that I was trying to stay calm while they were panicking I was speaking gently to them and helping them look for their valuable item that they lost"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":32748,"keystrokes":39,"maxInsertChunk":16,"responseDelayMs":78798,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":84,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":98}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That was very kind of you. Keeping a calm and reassuring attitude when someone else is panicking makes a big difference!\n\nOur Ellianos location is an 800-square-foot double drive-thru, which means the space is compact, busy, and physically active. Baristas are on their feet moving quickly for entire shifts and occasionally lifting items like 30-pound milk crates or syrup boxes. \n\nHow do you feel about working in a physically active role that requires standing, moving, and lifting for several hours at a time?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"i feel good"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":3464,"keystrokes":11,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":26483,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":52,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Glad to hear that, Yuseli!\n\nBecause our double drive-thru operates with a tight-knit, lean team, every single person on shift plays a crucial role. If someone is late or absent, it directly impacts the speed and flow of the entire store. \n\nDo you have reliable transportation to ensure you can consistently arrive on time for your scheduled shifts, including early mornings or weekends?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"yes"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":2311,"keystrokes":3,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":30543,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":26,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thatâ€™s great to know. Reliability is key to keeping the drive-thru running smoothly!\n\nIn an 800-square-foot shop, youâ€™ll be working shoulder-to-shoulder with 2 to 3 teammates during rush hours, moving fast to get drinks and food out the windows. \n\nHow do you communicate with your teammates in a small, crowded space to keep things safe and make sure everyone stays on the same page without running into each other?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would use quick phrases like behind you are coming through to communicate with my team members so it can be a safe environment with no mistakes"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":33648,"keystrokes":29,"maxInsertChunk":12,"responseDelayMs":63316,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":48,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Using call-outs like \"behind you\" and \"coming through\" is spot on for a compact kitchen environment! \n\nAt Ellianos, we pride ourselves on \"Italian Quality at America's Pace,\" meaning our speed is just as important as the quality of our drinks. During a morning rush, you might hear three different drink orders through your headset while you're in the middle of pulling espresso shots and steaming milk.\n\nHow do you keep track of multiple tasks or order details in your head so you don't forget anything when things start moving very quickly?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would repeat the order in my head or I can write it down on a sticky note"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":61996,"keystrokes":58,"maxInsertChunk":14,"responseDelayMs":82206,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":17,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Writing things down or repeating them are great ways to keep details straight!\n\nHere is a common scenario in coffee: Imagine it's the middle of a huge morning rush with lines wrapped around both drive-thru lanes. You hand a customer their specialty latte, and they take a sip and say, *\"This doesn't taste right, I asked for oat milk, not whole milk!\"*\n\nHow would you handle this interaction with the customer, and what steps would you take to resolve it quickly?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"in this situation I had apologize for the mistake and remake the latte with oat milk hand it"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":17650,"keystrokes":28,"maxInsertChunk":15,"responseDelayMs":108228,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":61,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"A quick, polite apology and an immediate remake is exactly the right approach to make sure the customer leaves happy!\n\nNow, let's step up the challenge with a high-pressure scenario that can happen during peak rush:\n\n**You are operating Window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for Window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you at Window A honks asking for napkins.**\n\nWalk me through your exact thought process to prioritize and handle these tasks."}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would quickly hand napkins to the honking car first then I would focus on finishing the complex drinks and the hot grip bowls one order at a time repeating each item in my head to stay organized and make sure nothing is missed"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":37784,"keystrokes":50,"maxInsertChunk":14,"responseDelayMs":99197,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":70,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That's a very practical way to prioritizeâ€”knocking out the quick, 2-second task immediately keeps the customer right in front of you happy and eliminates the distraction, letting you focus on the larger order!\n\nTo help us understand how you might fit into our schedule at the Lehigh Acres branch, what does your general availability look like throughout the week (mornings, afternoons, weekends), and how many hours per week are you ideally looking to work?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I am available on Mondays in the afternoon at 5pm,"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":98098,"keystrokes":43,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":39224,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":6,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thanks for sharing that, Yuseli! \n\nWhat does the rest of your availability look like throughout the week (Tuesday through Sunday), and how many total hours per week are you hoping to work?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"On Tuesdays, Thursdays and Fridays I am unavailable. Wednesdays I am available in the afternoon at 5 PM then on the weekend Iâ€™m available anytime. I am looking for at least 15 to 29 hours, part time job"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":122395,"keystrokes":155,"maxInsertChunk":17,"responseDelayMs":8753,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":19,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Got it, thank you for clarifying your availability and target hours! Open weekends and evening shifts are very helpful for scheduling.\n\nLearning our menuâ€”from signature espresso drinks to Lotus energy mixes and hot breakfast itemsâ€”is a big part of training for new baristas. \n\nWhen it comes to picking up new recipes and routines quickly, how do you personally learn best (such as hands-on practice, studying flashcards/notes, or watching someone demonstrate it first)?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I am more of a hands-on practice or watching someone demonstrate to me"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":26252,"keystrokes":39,"maxInsertChunk":14,"responseDelayMs":17702,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":30,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hands-on training and watching live demonstrations work really well in our fast-paced setup!\n\nDuring your training, your shift lead or manager will frequently give you real-time tips, corrections, or feedback on how to make drinks faster or more accurately. \n\nHow do you typically handle receiving constructive feedback or coaching on the spot while you're working?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I am normally good at receiving constructive feedback and coaching on the spot while Iâ€™m working"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":14528,"keystrokes":12,"maxInsertChunk":18,"responseDelayMs":30475,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":66,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thatâ€™s a great mindset to have, as continuous improvement helps the whole team succeed!\n\nCould you share a specific example of a time when someone (like a teacher, supervisor, or coach) gave you constructive feedback or suggested a different way of doing things? How did you apply that advice?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"well study with only 25 minutes my teacher once told me to slow down and check my work so I started pausing to review each step which helped me stay confident"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":31230,"keystrokes":85,"maxInsertChunk":12,"responseDelayMs":68774,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":60,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a wonderful example. Learning to balance accuracy with pacing is essential, especially when preparing handcrafted drinks under a timer!\n\nWe have covered the core areas of the Barista role today. As we reach the final part of our interview, do you have any questions for me about working at Ellianos Coffee or the Lehigh Acres location, or is there anything else you'd like our hiring team to know about you?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"are you guys taking part-time workers"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":4445,"keystrokes":9,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":29235,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":81,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":99}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Yes, absolutely! We definitely hire part-time team members at Ellianos Coffee. Part-time baristas are essential to our team, especially for covering busy weekend shifts and evening routines like the ones you mentioned.\n\nThank you so much for your time and thoughtful answers today, Yuseli! It was a pleasure getting to know more about you and your interest in our new Lehigh Acres location.\n\nTo officially finish and send your interview responses to our hiring team, please go ahead and click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen. We appreciate your interest, and our management team will be in touch with next steps! Have a wonderful day!"}]}],"secondInterviewGuide":{"interviewerTips":["No te quedes con respuestas monosilÃ¡bicas; solicita ejemplos con situaciones concretas, tiempos y acciones exactas ejecutadas por ella.","MantÃ©n una postura abierta y no acusatoria al preguntar sobre su proceso de redacciÃ³n o disponibilidad horaria.","Realiza simulaciones de rol cortas (30-45 segundos) para comprobar su manejo de la presiÃ³n y su tono de voz en ventanilla."],"decision":{"hire":"Aprobar los 3 bloques mustPass con calificaciÃ³n sobresaliente (demuestra soluciÃ³n real a su horario con disponibilidad absoluta en fines de semana/cierres, resistencia fÃ­sica comprobada y lÃ³gica de drive-thru) mÃ¡s un desempeÃ±o fluido y cÃ¡lido en el bloque de inglÃ©s funcional.","decline":"Cualquier bloque mustPass reprobado (incompatibilidad absoluta de horarios para alcanzar el mÃ­nimo de horas, dudas sobre transporte o poca resistencia fÃ­sica) o incapacidad de comunicarse en inglÃ©s con los clientes en ventanilla.","thirdConversation":"Si demuestra excelente actitud operativa, destreza y buen inglÃ©s, pero el Store Manager necesita cuadrar con exactitud la matriz de horarios de apertura para verificar si sus turnos de fin de semana y tardes cubren la necesidad del kiosco."},"blocks":[{"id":"block_schedule_transport","title":"Disponibilidad Horaria y Confiabilidad LogÃ­stica","goal":"Verificar la compatibilidad del horario restringido de la candidata con los turnos de cierre y fines de semana, asÃ­ como su puntualidad.","minutes":10,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q1","q2"]},{"id":"block_physical_pace","title":"Resistencia FÃ­sica y Ritmo en Espacio Reducido (800 sq ft)","goal":"Indagar a profundidad sobre su capacidad de soportar la exigencia fÃ­sica del kiosco tras sus respuestas escuetas.","minutes":10,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q3","q4"]},{"id":"block_drive_thru_prioritization","title":"PriorizaciÃ³n Operativa y Manejo de Crisis en Ventanilla","goal":"Evaluar la lÃ³gica prÃ¡ctica para resolver cuellos de botella simultÃ¡neos en el modelo de doble carril.","minutes":15,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q5","q6","q7"]},{"id":"block_english_service","title":"Functional Customer Service & Drive-Thru Communication (English)","goal":"Evaluar la fluidez, calidez y rapidez de respuesta en inglÃ©s durante la interacciÃ³n directa con clientes en ventanilla.","minutes":10,"mustPass":false,"questionIds":["q8","q9"]},{"id":"block_culture_coachability","title":"Adaptabilidad al Coaching, Cultura y Cierre","goal":"Medir su receptividad a la retroalimentaciÃ³n inmediata en turno pico y validar la honestidad general de su postulaciÃ³n.","minutes":10,"mustPass":false,"questionIds":["q10","q11"]}],"generatedAt":"2026-08-23T23:10:13.428Z","questions":[{"id":"q1","block":"block_schedule_transport","text":"Por escrito mencionaste: 'On Tuesdays, Thursdays and Fridays I am unavailable. Wednesdays I am available in the afternoon at 5 PM then on the weekend Iâ€™m available anytime' y que buscas entre 15 y 29 horas. ExplÃ­canos con exactitud a quÃ© se debe este esquema y cÃ³mo te asegurarÃ­as de cumplir tu meta de horas trabajando exclusivamente en cierres y fines de semana sin faltar.","language":"es","purpose":"Verificar si sus restricciones de horario permiten cubrir la operaciÃ³n de la nueva tienda y si su compromiso con los fines de semana es real.","listenFor":["ExplicaciÃ³n lÃ³gica de sus compromisos (estudios, responsabilidades familiares)","DisposiciÃ³n absoluta y confirmada para turnos completos de sÃ¡bado y domingo","Claridad en que sus 15-20 horas dependerÃ¡n fuertemente de los fines de semana y cierres"],"redFlags":["Inconsistencias con lo reportado por escrito","Dudas o restricciones ocultas para trabajar sÃ¡bados y domingos completos","Expectativa poco realista de tener turnos diurnos de lunes a viernes"]},{"id":"q2","block":"block_schedule_transport","text":"Cuando te preguntamos sobre transporte confiable para llegar a tiempo a turnos de madrugada o fines de semana respondiste simplemente 'yes'. Â¿CuÃ¡l es tu mÃ©todo exacto de traslado a la tienda de Lehigh Acres y cuÃ¡l es tu plan de contingencia si surge un imprevisto?","language":"es","purpose":"Comprobar que cuenta con medios de transporte independientes y seguros para garantizar cero retardos.","listenFor":["VehÃ­culo propio o sistema de transporte familiar especÃ­fico y predecible","Conocimiento del tiempo real de trayecto a la tienda de Lehigh Acres","Plan B estructurado (conductor alternativo, servicio de ride-share)"],"redFlags":["Dependencia de terceros sin horario fijo","Desconocimiento de la ubicaciÃ³n o tiempos de traslado","Falta de plan alternativo ante emergencias"]},{"id":"q3","block":"block_physical_pace","text":"Al preguntarte por escrito sobre estar de pie, moverte rÃ¡pi