 Â¿cuÃ¡l es tu secuencia exacta de acciÃ³n?","language":"es","purpose":"Validar su criterio de priorizaciÃ³n y seguridad operativa ante imprevistos en tiempo real.","listenFor":["Asegurar primero la seguridad (limpiar rÃ¡pido el derrame o avisar al equipo)","Mantener la calma y registrar el pedido del headset","Comunicar verbalmente a sus compaÃ±eros para recibir apoyo rÃ¡pido"],"redFlags":["Ignorar el derrame creando riesgo de resbalÃ³n","Bloquearse o desatender por completo al cliente por entrar en pÃ¡nico","No pedir ayuda ni coordinar con sus compaÃ±eros"]},{"id":"q6","block":"block_drive_thru_prioritization","text":"Mencionaste que usarÃ­as frases como 'behind you' o 'coming through' para evitar accidentes. En un kiosco de 800 sq ft con 4 personas en hora pico, Â¿cÃ³mo te coordinas cuando dos personas necesitan usar la misma mÃ¡quina de espresso o la estaciÃ³n de hielo al mismo tiempo?","language":"es","purpose":"Comprobar su visiÃ³n espacial y trabajo en equipo en espacios sumamente compactos.","listenFor":["ComunicaciÃ³n verbal constante y en voz alta","Ceder el paso fluidamente segÃºn la urgencia del ticket","Mantener siempre las manos y objetos calientes a la vista"],"redFlags":["Falta de conciencia del espacio compartido","Tendencia al silencio o timidez excesiva en cocina","Molestia o roces al chocar o compartir herramientas de trabajo"]},{"id":"q7","block":"block_drive_thru_prioritization","text":"Ante un error de bebida dijiste: 'apologize for the mistake and remake the latte with oat milk'. Â¿CÃ³mo equilibras rehacer esa bebida de inmediato sin detener el flujo de los pedidos de los autos que vienen detrÃ¡s en el carril?","language":"es","purpose":"Evaluar la capacidad de recuperaciÃ³n de servicio manteniendo la velocidad general de la lÃ­nea.","listenFor":["Pedir apoyo al compaÃ±ero de apoyo o preparar la leche de inmediato","Mantener informado al cliente con cortesÃ­a sobre el tiempo exacto de espera","Continuar operando con las manos mientras dialoga amablemente"],"redFlags":["Detener la producciÃ³n completa de la tienda para un solo vaso","Mostrar fastidio o discutir con el cliente por el reclamo","Desatender a los siguientes autos de la fila"]},{"id":"q8","block":"block_english_service","text":"Let's do a quick roleplay in English: A guest at Window B says, 'Excuse me, my iced Lotus energy drink tastes too weak and has no flavor.' Walk me through how you address them with high energy and fix their drink in under 45 seconds.","language":"en","purpose":"Verificar la fluidez conversacional en inglÃ©s y la calidez en la recuperaciÃ³n de servicio.","listenFor":["Natural, polite English communication ('I am so sorry about that, let me fix that right up for you!')","Friendly and confident customer service tone","Clear and positive body language"],"redFlags":["Inability to formulate basic customer service phrases in English","Defensive tone or arguing with the customer","Long freezes or extreme nervousness speaking English"]},{"id":"q9","block":"block_english_service","text":"In a busy drive-thru, you only have about 30 seconds at the window with each customer. In English, tell me how you build a genuine, friendly connection with regulars in that short window of time.","language":"en","purpose":"Evaluar la habilidad de generar lealtad y conexiÃ³n rÃ¡pida con clientes en inglÃ©s.","listenFor":["Mention of eye contact, smiling, using customer names, or greeting warmth","Proactive attitude ('Have an amazing day!')","Ability to speak clearly while handing out items"],"redFlags":["Treating interactions as strictly robotic or transactional","Dificultad evidente para articular ideas sencillas en inglÃ©s","Falta de calidez o desinterÃ©s en el trato humano"]},{"id":"q10","block":"block_culture_coachability","text":"Mencionaste que tu profesora te recomendÃ³ 'slow down and check my work' para tener mÃ¡s confianza. En Ellianos, tu Shift Lead te darÃ¡ correcciones en vivo para aumentar tu velocidad y precisiÃ³n. Â¿CÃ³mo manejas que te den retroalimentaciÃ³n directa y continua en medio de un turno lleno de clientes?","language":"es","purpose":"Determinar si asimila el coaching inmediato sin frustrarse ni tomarlo como algo personal.","listenFor":["Agradecimiento y recepciÃ³n positiva de la crÃ­tica constructiva","Capacidad de aplicar el cambio de inmediato en la siguiente bebida","Compromiso con el estÃ¡ndar de calidad de la marca"],"redFlags":["Actitud defensiva o justificaciones excesivas ante errores","DesmotivaciÃ³n o enojo cuando se le seÃ±alan fallas","Resistencia a cambiar mÃ©todos personales por los estÃ¡ndares de Ellianos"]},{"id":"q11","block":"block_culture_coachability","text":"Para cerrar: Notamos en tu entrevista virtual que tus respuestas fueron muy directas y con lenguaje natural. Valoramos enormemente la honestidad en Ellianos: Â¿tuviste oportunidad de investigar previamente sobre nuestro menÃº o recibiste apoyo de alguien al responder las preguntas escritas?","language":"es","purpose":"Evaluar su transparencia, nivel de iniciativa y honestidad personal.","listenFor":["Respuesta honesta, transparente y sin titubeos","InterÃ©s genuino demostrado por conocer la marca y el menÃº de Lehigh Acres","Congruencia total con su estilo de comunicaciÃ³n mostrado en la entrevista presencial"],"redFlags":["Incongruencias notorias entre su expresiÃ³n oral y sus respuestas previas","Falta de autenticidad o respuestas evasivas","DesinterÃ©s total por la apertura de la nueva tienda"]}],"focusPoints":["Validar la viabilidad real de su horario restringido (no disponible mar/jue/vie, disponible lun/mie despuÃ©s de las 5 PM y fines de semana completos) frente a las necesidades operativas de la tienda de Lehigh Acres.","Profundizar en su resistencia fÃ­sica, movilidad en 800 sq ft y transporte confiable tras sus respuestas de una sola palabra ('i feel good', 'yes').","Evaluar en vivo su agilidad para balancear velocidad ('Italian Quality at America's Pace') y precisiÃ³n tÃ©cnica sin perder la calma.","Comprobar su fluidez comunicativa y servicio al cliente en inglÃ©s funcional para la operaciÃ³n de ventanilla drive-thru."]}},{"position":"Barista","status":"Completed","emailSent":true,"messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Maylin! Welcome, and thank you for your interest in joining our team at the brand-new Ellianos Coffee in Lehigh Acres! We're thrilled to connect with you today.\n\nBefore we get started, I want to share a few quick details about how this interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of 25 questions.\n- You are free to finish and submit your application at **any time** by pressing the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know right here in the chat whenever you would like to conclude.\n\nTo kick things off with our first question: **What made you interested in applying for a Barista position with us at Ellianos Coffee?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"i was interested in applauding because."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":8587,"keystrokes":45,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":46665,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":42,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"It looks like your message may have cut off at the end! \n\nPlease feel free to finish your thoughtâ€”what specifically drew you to Ellianos and the Barista role?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"i was intrested in applying because i really like the fast paced, friendly environment of coffee shops, i also enjoy working with people. Iâ€™m also excited for this brand new coffee shop along with the location. Iâ€™d love the opportunity to grow with the team and learn to be a barrista."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":118632,"keystrokes":359,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":3165,"tabSwitches":9,"wpm":26,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That enthusiasm is wonderful to hear, Maylin! Being part of a brand-new opening team is definitely an exciting journey, and having a passion for learning is the best foundation for a barista.\n\nAt Ellianos, creating a warm, friendly connection at the windowâ€”even in just a few secondsâ€”is a huge part of what we do. \n\nCan you share an example from your past experience (whether from work, school, or daily life) where you went out of your way to make someoneâ€™s day brighter or provide great service?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Since i havenâ€™t had the chance to get a job i use the exepeicne from every day life. I always try to be helpful and kind to people, weather that means helping someone who is confused or upset or just being friendly me. i think the small things can really make someoneâ€™s day better."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":116749,"keystrokes":304,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":34853,"tabSwitches":12,"wpm":28,"pasteAttempts":1,"humanConfidence":56}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a great mindset to bring to the table, Maylin. Small, genuine gestures really do make a huge difference to our guests!\n\nOur Ellianos location operates out of an 800 sq ft double drive-thru kiosk with a small, tight-knit crew on each shift. Because our team is lean, every single team member is vitalâ€”if one person is late or absent, it impacts the entire drive-thru flow.\n\nDo you have reliable transportation to get to and from shifts consistently, and how do you make sure you stay organized and punctual for your commitments?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Indeed i do, I stay consistently organized by having a planner. I like to make things down so i donâ€™t forget iâ€™m also big on cleaning and organization a good day starts with an organized life."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":57955,"keystrokes":228,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":6349,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":37,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Having a planner and valuing cleanliness will serve you very well hereâ€”especially in an 800 sq ft kiosk where keeping things tidy and organized is essential for speed!\n\nBeing a barista is also very active and physically demanding. You'll be on your feet moving quickly for long stretches, and occasionally lifting items like 30 lb milk crates or boxes of syrups. \n\nHow comfortable are you with being on your feet and handling physical tasks throughout an entire shift?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Im actually very comfortable with staying on my feet and moving around for long periods of times. I donâ€™t mind lifting heavy or doing physical task. Iâ€™d be able to keep up and stay on my feet during a busy shift."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":243284,"keystrokes":303,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":38840,"tabSwitches":11,"wpm":10,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That's great to hear! Physical stamina makes a huge difference during a morning rush.\n\nLet's talk about learning and multitasking. Making specialty drinks involves memorizing unique recipe builds, milk choices, syrup pumps, and temperaturesâ€”all while listening to new orders coming in through your headset and communicating with your teammates in a compact space.\n\nHow do you usually approach memorizing detailed new information, and how do you keep yourself focused when multiple things are happening around you at once?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I try to memorize by practicing and repeating it until it sticks. when a lot  is going on i stay calm  and focus on what need to be done first and work through each task without letting myself get overwhelmed."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":147580,"keystrokes":348,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":22490,"tabSwitches":13,"wpm":16,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Staying calm and working through tasks step-by-step is exactly the right mentality to have.\n\nSince that can be easier said than done when things get hectic, could you share a specific timeâ€”maybe during a busy school project, an event, or a chaotic moment at homeâ€”where several things were demanding your attention at once? \n\nHow did you decide what to do first, and how did you handle it?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"One example would be when i hsve multiple things to get done at home at the same time. I figured out whatâ€™s most important needed to be done first, then worked through everything else one at a time. I stayed organized and calm instead of trying to do everything at once  and overwhelming myself."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":209164,"keystrokes":458,"maxInsertChunk":2,"responseDelayMs":37650,"tabSwitches":17,"wpm":15,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Prioritizing by urgency and staying composed is a great habit. \n\nNow, letâ€™s put that prioritization into action with a real-world rush scenario in our drive-thru:\n\n**You are operating Window A's espresso station. Through your headset, an order for Window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you honks asking for napkins. Walk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks.**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Id quickly give the customer a napkin since that only takes a few seconds and then iâ€™d go right back to the drink order and focus on making everything correctly and in order. if needed help   with grits or another part of order iâ€™d asked my team so we could keep things moving"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":113030,"keystrokes":388,"maxInsertChunk":4,"responseDelayMs":39196,"tabSwitches":12,"wpm":28,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Handling the immediate customer in front of you with a quick smile and napkins, while immediately calling out to your team to start the hot food, shows great instincts for drive-thru flow and teamwork!\n\nWorking in an 800 sq ft kiosk means you and your teammates are in very close quarters, moving fast and bumping elbows during a rush. When things get busy, communication has to be very direct, and sometimes a shift lead might give you quick, on-the-spot corrections (like fixing a milk texture or remaking a drink).\n\nHow do you handle receiving fast, direct feedback in the moment, and how do you maintain a positive, supportive attitude with your teammates even when the shift gets stressful?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I take feedback well and use it to improve we all need feedback. I stay calm and respectful and positive even when things get busy of course"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":45205,"keystrokes":162,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":76242,"tabSwitches":5,"wpm":36,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":76}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"A growth mindset regarding feedback is crucial in a fast-paced environment, so that's wonderful to hear.\n\nOur drive-thru opens very early in the morning to serve our community their daily fuel, and we operate seven days a week, including weekends and holidays.\n\nWhat does your current weekly availability look like, and are you comfortable working early morning shifts, weekends, or flexible hours as needed?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"im available any time during the weekends and and any time during the holidays during the weekdays i do have school going on so during the afternoon"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":41766,"keystrokes":196,"maxInsertChunk":1,"responseDelayMs":27388,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":39,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you for clarifying your schedule, Maylin! Having open weekend and holiday availability paired with weekday afternoons is very helpful for our scheduling team.\n\nYou have done a great job answering all of our core questions today, covering everything from customer service and handling drive-thru rushes to teamwork and availability. \n\nDo you have any questions for me about the role, our training program, or working at the new Lehigh Acres Ellianos? Or, if you feel good about everything we've covered, please let me know or feel free to press the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen to complete your interview!"}]}],"evaluation":"# Candidate Interview Evaluation\n\n**Candidate Name:** Maylin Perez  \n**Position Applied For:** Barista (Lehigh Acres Location)  \n**Contact Information:** 239-839-9941 | maylinperez2008@icloud.com  \n\n---\n\n### 1. Final Score: 78 / 100\n\nMaylin presents as an eager, positive, and coachable entry-level candidate. While she lacks formal work experience and has limited weekday morning availability due to school, she demonstrated solid practical instincts for drive-thru prioritization, an appreciation for team communication, and an adaptable mindset suitable for a fast-paced kiosk environment.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Summary of Strengths\n\n* **Sound Practical Instincts & Prioritization:** When presented with a multi-task drive-thru rush scenario (handling a quick customer request vs. complex drink builds vs. hot food), she correctly prioritized resolving the quick immediate need (napkins), returning immediately to drink builds, and delegating the food order to teammates.\n* **Positive, Coachable Attitude:** Expressed a strong willingness to learn, openly embraced receiving feedback and corrections, and displayed enthusiasm for being part of a brand-new store opening.\n* **Customer-Centric Mindset:** Shows a natural grasp that small gestures and friendly interactions create positive customer experiences.\n* **Physical Preparedness & Organization:** Confirmed she is comfortable on her feet for long shifts, willing to handle physical lifting, and utilizes tools like planners to maintain personal organization and punctuality.\n* **Strong Weekend & Holiday Availability:** Full availability on weekends, holidays, and weekday afternoons aligns well with high-volume peak periods outside of school hours.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Summary of Weaknesses & Areas of Concern\n\n* **No Prior Work Experience:** Maylin has not held a formal job yet; her responses drew exclusively from daily personal life and school. She will require initial coaching on workplace standards and fast-paced operational workflows.\n* **Restricted Weekday Morning Availability:** As a current student, she cannot cover early weekday morning shifts (the primary rush period for drive-thru coffee). Her scheduling utility is restricted to afternoon, weekend, and holiday shifts.\n* **Surface-Level Examples:** Some behavioral responses (e.g., handling chaos or multitasking) were somewhat generic and brief, reflecting her limited professional background.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Final Recommendation\n\n**Recommendation:** **Second Interview** (or **Hire** specifically for a Part-Time Afternoon/Weekend Shift)\n\n*Maylin is well-suited for a part-time entry-level barista position. A brief in-person follow-up interview with the store manager is recommended to verify cultural fit, review specific scheduling windows around her school hours, and confirm reliable transportation.*\n\n---\n\n### 5. Authenticity Assessment\n\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** **75.6%**\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answer:** **Response 4 (56%)**\n* **Answers Below 35% Confidence:** **None** (0 responses flagged)\n\n#### Writing-Style & Behavioral Analysis\n* **Typing Metrics & Behavioral Signals:** Typing speeds remained within a natural, organic range (10â€“42 WPM) with realistic durations and keystroke volumes matching the output text lengths. One single paste attempt was recorded on Response 4, and multiple tab switches occurred across several prompts (averaging 5â€“17 switches). \n* **Writing Style Evaluation:** **Agrees with authentic human authorship.** The text contains frequent organic typos, colloquial punctuation, and natural grammatical patterns consistent with an unassisted applicant typing on a mobile device or browser (e.g., *\"intrested\"*, *\"exepeicne\"*, *\"weather\"*, *\"hsve\"*). The frequent tab switches appear to reflect normal phone distractions or casual drafting rather than external AI generation or script copying. No indicators of automated assistance were detected.","id":"4f39b93a-53f9-4efa-8eb4-7a1e1966c638","date":"2026-08-23T21:34:21.680Z","secondInterviewGuide":{"interviewerTips":["Guiar a la candidata hacia ejemplos especÃ­ficos de su vida escolar, proyectos o tareas en casa con mÃ©tricas y resultados concretos.","No intimidar sobre la falta de experiencia; enfocarse en evaluar actitud de aprendizaje rÃ¡pido, honestidad y dinamismo corporal.","Simular escenarios reales de presiÃ³n en cabina drive-thru para observar su lenguaje no verbal y receptividad a correcciones en vivo."],"decision":{"hire":"AprobaciÃ³n de todos los bloques con mustPass: true (puntaje >= 3.8/5.0), disponibilidad vespertina y de fin de semana 100% confirmada, transporte seguro a Lehigh Acres, y demostraciÃ³n de actitud enÃ©rgica, coachable y honesta.","decline":"CalificaciÃ³n menor a 3.0 en cualquier bloque mustPass, incompatibilidad horaria con los turnos vespertinos/fines de semana, resistencia o mala actitud ante el feedback correctivo, o inconsistencias graves de honestidad.","thirdConversation":"Dudas menores en la logÃ­stica de transporte o ajuste exacto de los horarios escolares que requieran confirmaciÃ³n de horarios con la escuela o autorizaciÃ³n de turno por parte del Store Manager."},"blocks":[{"id":"block_transicion_madurez","title":"TransiciÃ³n al Trabajo y Sentido de Responsabilidad","goal":"Verificar hÃ¡bitos de autodisciplina, organizaciÃ³n personal y madurez para asumir su primer rol laboral formal.","minutes":10,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q1","q2"]},{"id":"block_operaciones_presion","title":"Ritmo Operativo, Multitarea y Receptividad al Feedback","goal":"Evaluar la capacidad de trabajar en un espacio fÃ­sico estrecho de 800 sq ft bajo presiÃ³n y con correcciÃ³n inmediata.","minutes":15,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q3","q4","q5"]},{"id":"block_ingles_servicio","title":"Customer Service & Drive-Thru Interaction","goal":"Evaluar fluidez oral en inglÃ©s, rapidez verbal y calidez de atenciÃ³n al cliente en ventanilla.","minutes":10,"mustPass":false,"questionIds":["q6","q7"]},{"id":"block_disponibilidad_cierre","title":"Disponibilidad Horaria, LogÃ­stica y Honestidad","goal":"Confirmar la viabilidad de horarios escolares, transporte puntual y autenticidad del proceso de postulaciÃ³n.","minutes":10,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q8","q9"]}],"generatedAt":"2026-08-23T21:59:50.390Z","questions":[{"id":"q1","block":"block_transicion_madurez","text":"En tu entrevista virtual mencionaste: 'Since i havenâ€™t had the chance to get a job i use the exepeicne from every day life'. Al ser este tu primer empleo formal, Â¿cÃ³mo te estÃ¡s preparando para asumir la responsabilidad de un horario estricto, rendir cuentas a un supervisor y no fallarle a tu equipo en dÃ­as difÃ­ciles?","language":"es","purpose":"Evaluar el grado de conciencia y compromiso ante las exigencias de un primer entorno laboral.","listenFor":["Reconocimiento claro de la diferencia entre responsabilidades escolares y un empleo formal.","MenciÃ³n de puntualidad, respeto a normas internas y deseo activo de superaciÃ³n.","Actitud humilde y proactiva para dejarse guiar por los lÃ­deres de turno."],"redFlags":["Minimizar la responsabilidad laboral tratÃ¡ndola como un pasatiempo casual.","Falta de claridad sobre cÃ³mo responderÃ¡ ante figuras de autoridad o reglamentos.","Justificaciones anticipadas ante posibles ausencias o retrasos."]},{"id":"q2","block":"block_transicion_madurez","text":"Escribiste que mantienes la organizaciÃ³n personal usando una agenda: 'I stay consistently organized by having a planner... a good day starts with an organized life'. CuÃ©ntame un caso real en la escuela o en tu hogar donde tuviste una semana saturada de entregas y compromisos; Â¿cÃ³mo planificaste tus horas y cuÃ¡l fue el resultado?","language":"es","purpose":"Comprobar con hechos reales si cuenta con mÃ©todos probados de gestiÃ³n de tiempo.","listenFor":["Detalle secuencial de priorizaciÃ³n entre tareas urgentes y no urgentes.","Cumplimiento efectivo de todas las responsabilidades sin descuidar compromisos.","Manejo ordenado y autÃ³nomo de su tiempo libre y obligaciones."],"redFlags":["Incapacidad para dar un ejemplo especÃ­fico a pesar de haberlo afirmado por escrito.","Dependencia total de recordatorios de padres o terceros para cumplir sus deberes.","Respuestas abstractas o evasivas sin resultados tangibles."]},{"id":"q3","block":"block_operaciones_presion","text":"En el escenario del drive-thru resolviste muy bien la urgencia diciendo: 'Id quickly give the customer a napkin... then go right back to the drink order... if needed help with grits asked my team'. Imagina que durante un rush de 5 autos, se te cae un jarabe, el piso se vuelve resbaladizo y tu Shift Leader te dice en tono directo y enÃ©rgico: 'Â¡Maylin, limpia eso de inmediato y vuelve a la barra!'. Â¿QuÃ© pasa por tu mente y cÃ³mo respondes verbal y fÃ­sicamente en ese segundo dentro de un espacio de solo 800 sq ft?","language":"es","purpose":"Medir tolerancia al estrÃ©s, rapidez de reacciÃ³n y asimilaciÃ³n de feedback directo sin tomarlo como ataque personal.","listenFor":["Respuesta orientada a la seguridad del equipo y la continuidad del flujo operativo.","AceptaciÃ³n madura del tono directo por tratarse de un momento crÃ­tico de velocidad.","Capacidad de actuar rÃ¡pido sin bloquearse ni mostrar lenguaje corporal defensivo."],"redFlags":["Resentimiento, susceptibilidad emocional o tomar la retroalimentaciÃ³n como una ofensa.","ParÃ¡lisis o indecisiÃ³n ante la orden enÃ©rgica del supervisor.","Ignorar el protocolo de seguridad/limpieza por querer apresurar bebidas."]},{"id":"q4","block":"block_operaciones_presion","text":"Mencionaste que para aprender aplicas repeticiÃ³n continua: 'I try to memorize by practicing and repeating it until it sticks'. En Ellianos deberÃ¡s memorizar mÃ¡s de 30 recetas, medidas exactas de pumps y temperaturas en tu primera semana. DescrÃ­beme tu tÃ©cnica exacta para aprenderte esa cantidad de informaciÃ³n tÃ©cnica en pocos dÃ­as.","language":"es","purpose":"Verificar la metodologÃ­a de aprendizaje rÃ¡pido y retenciÃ³n cognitiva bajo estÃ¡ndares de calidad precisos.","listenFor":["TÃ©cnicas concretas de estudio (fichas, repeticiÃ³n activa, esquemas, prÃ¡ctica visual).","DisposiciÃ³n para repasar materiales en casa durante la fase de entrenamiento inicial.","ComprensiÃ³n de que las medidas y recetas de cafÃ© deben ser exactas y consistentes."],"redFlags":["Confiar Ãºnicamente en la memoria a corto plazo sin mÃ©todo estructurado.","Falta de interÃ©s por capacitarse fuera de los minutos de turno.","Actitud pasiva esperando que los compaÃ±eros hagan el trabajo por ella."]},{"id":"q5","block":"block_operaciones_presion","text":"El trabajo en cabina implica 6 a 8 horas de pie en movimiento constante, levantando cajas de leche de 30 lbs en espacios angostos. Â¿QuÃ© actividades fÃ­sicas o rutinas has realizado antes que demuestren que mantendrÃ¡s el ritmo y la energÃ­a alta sin agotarte a mitad de turno?","language":"es","purpose":"Confirmar resistencia fÃ­sica real y disposiciÃ³n hacia las tareas mÃ¡s demandantes del kiosco.","listenFor":["Experiencia en deportes, actividades fÃ­sicas intensas o tareas pesadas en casa.","EnergÃ­a fÃ­sica visible y postura corporal activa durante la entrevista.","Compromiso hacia las labores de carga, descarga y limpieza pesada."],"redFlags":["Indicios de fatiga prematura o quejas sobre estar de pie por perÃ­odos prolongados.","Rechazo encubierto hacia las labores de reposiciÃ³n pesada o limpieza profunda.","Lenguaje corporal letÃ¡rgico o desganado."]},{"id":"q6","block":"block_ingles_servicio","text":"In your written interview you mentioned that you love making people's day brighter. Let's do a quick roleplay in English: I am a customer pulling up to Window A at 4:00 PM looking tired. Greet me, ask for my order with high energy, and upsell our signature Lotus Energy drink.","language":"en","purpose":"Evaluar dinamismo, espontaneidad, calidez y soltura comunicativa en inglÃ©s en el punto de venta.","listenFor":["EntonaciÃ³n alegre, contacto visual inmediato y bienvenida genuina.","Fluidez natural en inglÃ©s para formular preguntas y sugerir productos.","Capacidad de romper el hielo y transmitir hospitalidad en menos de 10 segundos."],"redFlags":["Inseguridad extrema, timidez excesiva o silencio prolongado.","InglÃ©s incomprensible o incapacidad de hilar frases bÃ¡sicas de servicio.","Tono plano, robÃ³tico o desinteresado."]},{"id":"q7","block":"block_ingles_servicio","text":"Imagine a guest at the drive-thru window is upset because their drink is taking a minute longer than usual. In English, what exact words would you use to acknowledge their frustration, keep them calm, and ensure they leave happy?","language":"en","purpose":"Comprobar habilidades de resoluciÃ³n bÃ¡sica de quejas y empatÃ­a en inglÃ©s en ventanilla rÃ¡pida.","listenFor":["Disculpas sinceras y explicaciones breves sin culpar a sus compaÃ±eros.","Uso de frases asertivas y corteses (e.g., 'Thank you for your patience', 'We're crafting it fresh for you').","Mantenimiento de la compostura bajo la mirada del cliente impaciente."],"redFlags":["Ponerse a la defensiva o discutir con el cliente.","Quedarse callada o cerrar la ventanilla para evadir la situaciÃ³n.","Falta de vocabulario en inglÃ©s para manejar situaciones tensas comunes."]},{"id":"q8","block":"block_disponibilidad_cierre","text":"Mencionaste que por la escuela estÃ¡s disponible en las tardes entre semana y tiempo completo en fines de semana y feriados. Â¿A quÃ© hora exacta terminas clases de lunes a viernes, cuÃ¡nto tardas en llegar al local de Lehigh Acres y cuÃ¡l es tu plan de transporte seguro para no tener retrasos?","language":"es","purpose":"Asegurar que los horarios escolares sean 100% compatibles con la operaciÃ³n y el transporte sea confiable.","listenFor":["Horario escolar definido con hora exacta de salida y margen holgado de traslado.","Medio de transporte propio o plan familiar firme y garantizado hacia Lehigh Acres.","Disponibilidad total confirmada para fines de semana, aperturas de sÃ¡bado/domingo y feriados."],"redFlags":["Horarios que chocan con los turnos de la tarde o cambios imprevistos de horario escolar.","Dependencia de transporte pÃºblico inestable o personas sin compromiso fijo de traslado.","Dudas o restricciones sorpresivas para laborar fines de semana completos."]},{"id":"q9","block":"block_disponibilidad_cierre","text":"Durante la primera fase virtual vimos que algunas de tus respuestas tuvieron tiempos de pausa o ajustes de texto. Queremos asegurarnos de tu estilo de trabajo: Â¿te apoyaste en traductores, notas preparadas o ayuda de alguien mÃ¡s para formular tus respuestas escritas? Valoramos mucho la honestidad directa.","language":"es","purpose":"Evaluar la honestidad, transparencia y coherencia frente a la telemetrÃ­a registrada en la primera etapa.","listenFor":["Respuesta honesta y transparente sobre el uso de borradores, autocorrector o apoyo.","Coherencia entre su forma de expresarse en persona y el estilo escrito.","Actitud abierta que refuerza la confianza en su integridad personal."],"redFlags":["Mentir o mostrar incomodidad evidente cuando se le pregunta de forma neutral.","Contradicciones notorias entre su nivel de razonamiento en vivo y el texto previo.","Falta de transparencia en aspectos bÃ¡sicos de su postulaciÃ³n."]}],"focusPoints":["Evaluar la madurez y transiciÃ³n de un perfil sin experiencia laboral previa a la exigencia de un empleo formal de alto ritmo.","Verificar la compatibilidad y exactitud de sus horarios escolares con los turnos vespertinos, fines de semana y festivos en Lehigh Acres.","Comprobar su capacidad de asimilar feedback correctivo inmediato y mantener la calma en el espacio reducido (800 sq ft) del kiosco.","Validar su energÃ­a comunicativa y servicio al cliente en inglÃ©s fluido durante la interacciÃ³n directa en ventanilla."]},"candidateInfo":{"phone":"2398399941","name":"maylin perez","email":"maylinperez2008@icloud.com"}},{"emailSent":true,"status":"Completed","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Nylah! Welcome, and thank you for your interest in joining our brand-new Ellianos Coffee team in Lehigh Acres, FL. We're thrilled to chat with you today!\n\nBefore we begin, I'd like to share a few quick details about how this interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of **25 questions**, asked one at a time.\n- You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know right here in the chat whenever you'd like to finish.\n\nPrevious coffee experience isn't requiredâ€”we love teaching enthusiastic people! \n\nTo kick things off with our first question: **What made you interested in applying to be a Barista with Ellianos Coffee?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™m interested in working at Ellianos because I really like the environment of coffee shops and I enjoy serving and helping customers out. Iâ€™m also a very fast learner and work well is fast paced environments. I think this would be a fun place for my first job to especially because iâ€™d be doing something iâ€™m actually interested in."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":150370,"keystrokes":415,"maxInsertChunk":11,"responseDelayMs":54937,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":24,"pasteAttempts":1,"humanConfidence":64}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That's wonderful to hear, Nylah! Starting your first job in a place you're genuinely excited about is a great way to begin.\n\nAt Ellianos, our tagline is \"Italian Quality at America's Pace,\" but our warm customer service is what truly keeps people coming back. \n\nSince this would be your first job, can you share an example from school, a group project, volunteering, or daily life where you went out of your way to help someone or make them feel welcomed?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"In my culinary class, we would have to work together to prepare food it to teachers. I made sure to help my classmates when they were confused or running behind and I always tried to make everyone feel comfortable and included. My class helped me learn how important team work is especially is a busy environment"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":152983,"keystrokes":403,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":29986,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":22,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":84}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Culinary class is fantastic preparation for a coffee shop! You already understand kitchen teamwork, hygiene, and the rush of preparing orders for people.\n\nOur Ellianos building is a unique double drive-thru setup that is only about 800 square feet. That means our team of baristas works closely side-by-side in a tight, high-energy space, often on your feet for an entire 4-to-8-hour shift, moving quickly and lifting items like milk crates or ice bags (up to 30 lbs).\n\nHow do you feel about working in a compact, physically active environment where you're constantly on the move?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™m completely good with that! I actually like staying busy and having tasks to do."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":57499,"keystrokes":107,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":25909,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":16,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That energetic mindset is exactly what thrives in our drive-thrus!\n\nBecause of our compact 800 sq ft size, we run with very lean staffingâ€”often just a few baristas per shift. If one person is late or misses a shift, it creates an immediate challenge for the entire team and impacts our drive-thru times.\n\nDo you have reliable transportation to the Lehigh Acres location, and what systems or habits do you use to ensure you are consistently on time for your commitments?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes i have reliable transportation. To make sure iâ€™m consistently on time would be setting reminders, alarms, and leaving early just incase of any traffic or anything unexpected."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":65666,"keystrokes":204,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":26136,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":26,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Leaving early is definitely the best way to stay ahead of traffic!\n\nIn our fast-paced double drive-thru, you'll often have to listen to new incoming orders through your headset while simultaneously measuring syrups, steaming milk, or preparing drinks for the window. \n\nHow do you handle taking in multiple pieces of information at once, and can you give me a specific example of a time you had to juggle several tasks at the same time without losing track?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™m good at handling many things at once. In my culinary class there was times when we did a competition alone and I had to make sure food was prepped, area was clean, and i had time to work. I made it work by doing the most important things first"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":128128,"keystrokes":291,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":35466,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":23,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Prioritizing the most crucial steps first is a great strategy for staying organized under pressure!\n\nSpeed is essential in a drive-thru, but precision is just as importantâ€”for example, if a customer requests oat milk due to a dairy allergy, getting that detail right matters immensely. \n\nIf you're in the middle of a rush and realize you just made a drink with regular whole milk instead of oat milk, or a teammate catches your mistake, how would you handle that situation in the moment?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"If I was in that situation I would definitely just take the time to remake it. Mistakes happen and you never know if a customer has an allergy/dietary restrictions."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":87505,"keystrokes":288,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":11404,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":20,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Spot on, Nylah. Customer safety and getting the order right are always worth those extra few seconds!\n\nNow, let's step up the pressure a bit. Sometimes during peak morning rush hours, lines can back up, and a customer might pull up to the window visibly frustrated or complaining about the wait time. \n\nHow would you respond to an upset customer at the window to turn their experience around while still keeping the line moving quickly?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would make sure to stay calm, listen to the issue, and make sure they feel heard. I would make sure to apologize for the inconvenience and do what i can to fix the issue or get the manager involved if needed so I could get things moving."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":88827,"keystrokes":257,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":24657,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":32,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Staying calm and making people feel heard is the best way to diffuse tension quickly.\n\nNow, let's put your multitasking and prioritization skills to the ultimate test with a real-time rush scenario we often face at Ellianos:\n\n**You are operating window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you honks asking for napkins. Walk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks.**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™d prioritize the one that could be the fastest, which in my opinion it would be the napkins, then quickly finish the espresso from window A. After iâ€™m done iâ€™d communicate with my team to see if anyone could help me make the Lotus Edge energy drinks to get them done faster and more efficiently."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":116906,"keystrokes":323,"maxInsertChunk":11,"responseDelayMs":58874,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":28,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Excellent breakdown! Handing over the napkins takes two seconds and resolves an immediate issue, finishing your active espresso drink keeps Window A moving, and calling out to your team for Window B prevents bottlenecks. That shows great drive-thru instincts!\n\nAs we prepare to open our new Lehigh Acres branch, flexibility is a big help. What does your weekly availability look like (e.g., mornings, afternoons, weekends), and how many hours per week are you ideally hoping to work?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"My schedule is pretty much completely open. I have full availability on weekends, and on tuesday, thursday, and friday i can start at 9. But monday and wednesdays i can come in at 2:30 due to my dual enrollment classes. I was hoping for atleast 30 hours!"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":146243,"keystrokes":301,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":13177,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":19,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That schedule offers great flexibility, Nylah, and balancing dual enrollment with work shows great dedication and time management!\n\nSince this would be your first official job, learning the ropes at a high-speed coffee shop will involve lots of on-the-spot coaching and feedback from shift leaders as you memorize recipes and speed techniques.\n\nHow do you prefer to receive feedback or corrections when you are learning a new skill?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I prefer very direct feedback, if iâ€™m doing something wrong iâ€™d rather get told so i can fix it. Also, iâ€™m definitely a visual learner so if iâ€™m given a demonstration iâ€™m more likely to pick up that way. I do think iâ€™m a very fast learner"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":82898,"keystrokes":226,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":33226,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":34,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That direct, open attitude is fantastic. In a fast-paced drive-thru, quick and clear communication is key, and our trainers love working with visual learners who want to improve every day!\n\nWe have covered all the major topics I needed to go over today. \n\nDo you have any questions for me about the Barista position, the new Lehigh Acres store, or what it's like to be part of the Ellianos Coffee team? (Or is there anything else youâ€™d like to share before submitting your application?)"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"When is it officially open?"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":6745,"keystrokes":22,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":23359,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":44,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"The Lehigh Acres store is slated to open in the coming weeks! Once our core team is finalized, we will be holding comprehensive, hands-on training sessions right before our official Grand Opening so everyone feels confident, prepared, and ready to serve our customers from day one.\n\nYou did a fantastic job today, Nylah. If you have any other questions, feel free to ask. If you're all set, you can go ahead and click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen to finalize your application with us!"}]}],"candidateInfo":{"phone":"5513132634","name":"Nylah Mansour","email":"nylahmansour@gmail.com"},"id":"d07b1817-c501-41ee-ae75-6ce301d25fea","evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation Report\n\n**Candidate Name:** Nylah Mansour  \n**Position Applied For:** Barista (Lehigh Acres Location)  \n**Email:** nylahmansour@gmail.com | **Phone:** 551-313-2634  \n\n---\n\n### Final Score: **92 / 100**\nNylah demonstrates an ideal profile for an entry-level barista. She displays strong operational logic under pressure, high coachability, natural customer-service empathy, and relevant foundation skills from her culinary coursework.\n\n---\n\n### Strengths\n* **Operational Logic & Multitasking:** Demonstrated exceptional real-time problem-solving during the rush scenario by identifying quick wins (handing out napkins), maintaining flow on active orders (finishing Window A espresso), and communicating/delegating with teammates on larger orders.\n* **Customer Care & Food Safety Awareness:** Recognizes the critical importance of food safety and allergens without hesitation, prioritizing customer well-being over speed when remaking drinks.\n* **Relevant Foundational Experience:** Her culinary class background has prepared her well for kitchen cleanliness, working in tight spaces, team communication, and fast-paced order prep.\n* **Coachability & Attitude:** Expressed a strong desire for direct feedback and self-identified as a visual learner, making her very easy to train during store opening.\n* **Solid Availability & Reliability:** Clear transportation and punctuality plans, with strong availability (open weekends, ~30 hours/week) while managing dual-enrollment coursework.\n\n---\n\n### Weaknesses & Areas for Development\n* **First-Time Work Experience:** As this will be her first official job, she will need standard onboarding support regarding formal workplace policies, POS systems, and commercial coffee workflow.\n* **Minor Schedule Constraints:** Dual-enrollment classes limit availability on Monday and Wednesday mornings until 2:30 PM (though she offers broad availability across all other days and full weekends).\n\n---\n\n### Authenticity Assessment\n\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** **90.2%**\n* **Lowest-Confidence Response:** **Response 2 (64%)** (1 paste attempt / 2 tab switches during initial introductory response).\n* **Responses Below 35%:** **None.**\n* **Writing Style & Metric Alignment:** **Agrees strongly.** The typing metrics reflect completely organic writing behaviorâ€”steady typing speeds (16â€“44 WPM), realistic durations (up to 150s), and proportionate keystroke counts with natural revisions. The conversational tone, natural phrasing, and consistent personal voice across all answers fully corroborate human authorship.\n\n---\n\n### Final Recommendation: **HIRE**\nNylah is an enthusiastic, fast-learning, and level-headed candidate who is well-suited for the dynamic, fast-paced environment of an Ellianos double drive-thru. She is highly recommended for the opening team at the Lehigh Acres location.","date":"2026-08-22T04:21:25.964Z","position":"Barista"},{"messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Store Manager position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Madison! Welcome, and thank you for your interest in the Store Manager position for our brand-new Ellianos Coffee location in Lehigh Acres, Florida. Weâ€™re excited to speak with you today.\n\nBefore we get started, I want to go over a few quick details about how this interview works:\n- You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know right here in the chat if you wish to wrap up early.\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of 25 questions, which we will take one at a time at your pace.\n\nTo kick things off with a simple icebreaker: **What caught your interest about Ellianos Coffee, and what excites you most about the opportunity to lead the team at our new Lehigh Acres location?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I have 6 years total of experience in a coffee business. I came across a video asking for managers. I personally loved working in a coffee shop"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":75602,"keystrokes":157,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":40812,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":21,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Having six years of coffee industry experience is fantastic, Madison! That background gives you a great foundational understanding of the day-to-day rhythm of a shop.\n\nGiven your time in the industry, **how would you describe your personal leadership style, and how do you motivate a team during high-energy morning rushes?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I keep my thoughts and opinions positive, I am very good at keeping others motivated while doing a great job"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":86625,"keystrokes":147,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":17966,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":14,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"A positive mindset can truly set the tone for the entire floor, especially during those intense peak hours. \n\nCould you share a **specific example** from your previous experience where morale was dipping or a rush was getting chaotic, and describe the exact steps you took to keep your team motivated and performing at their best?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I finish what Iâ€™m doing and immediately ask who needs help to help with the speed time as well as helping my coworkers with learning how to pick up the pace so I can then move on to the next person who need help"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":60983,"keystrokes":210,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":41023,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":43,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That hands-on, supportive approach is essential on the floor. \n\nAt Ellianos, our model is unique: we operate out of an 800-square-foot double drive-thru. Itâ€™s an extremely fast-paced, high-volume environment with very tight physical space and multiple team members moving around each other constantly.\n\n**How do you maintain efficient station flow, clear communication, and safety when managing a team in such a compact, high-speed workspace?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Very importantly I remain calm, things can get very chaotic if everyone is hectic and not on track, I help the drive thru first because thereâ€™s a drive time goal that needs to be reached, I then switch spots with the coworker struggling more to reach that goal, until the rush is over I then fulfill any online orders and help around the store until the next rush"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":129080,"keystrokes":376,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":17014,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":32,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Prioritizing drive times and stepping into bottleneck positions is a smart tactical move on the floor.\n\nBecause our footprint is lean and efficient, staffing is also very leanâ€”often just a few team members per shift. A single absence or late arrival can seriously disrupt operations.\n\nAs Store Manager, **how do you ensure strict punctuality and schedule adherence across your team, and what is your strategy for handling unexpected call-outs without burning out yourself or your remaining crew?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Anyone that chooses to call out MUST write it on the calendar I have provided in the office, I then can approve the call outs. If itâ€™s an emergency call out I have them find someone to cover their shift BEFORE calling out of their shifts, other times I will cover if need be"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":81515,"keystrokes":314,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":21174,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":40,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Having clear accountability for time-off requests and having a plan to step in yourself when emergencies happen shows true dedication. As Store Manager, you'll also be responsible for the financial health of the Lehigh Acres store. \n\nLet's talk a bit about business acumen: **How do you approach managing inventory, reducing product waste, and monitoring labor percentages to ensure the store stays profitable without sacrificing quality or customer service?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"A big thing to cut waste is to have EVERYTHING rang in, no freebies. I double check my inventory before submitting the truck for the next day, I am very big on breaks and overtime hours,Your breaks are the main reason for bad labor, as long as everyone goes as told to labor remains great."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":190994,"keystrokes":422,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":38102,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":17,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Ringing in every item accurately and managing break schedules strictly are both vital practices for protecting the bottom line and controlling labor costs.\n\nBuilding on that, opening a brand-new location in Lehigh Acres means you will be hiring and training a brand-new crew from the ground up to uphold Ellianosâ€™ standard of \"Italian Quality at America's Pace.\"\n\n**What is your approach to onboarding and training new baristas, and how do you handle a team member who is struggling to meet speed or recipe consistency standards despite repeated training?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"When training and hiring I always have an idea where I need everyone at and I know my current teams strengths I hire ONLY if needed I donâ€™t over hire because my original crew loses hours. I train exactly what Iâ€™m hiring them for and then once they have a good head on it, I then train them on other positions"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":130061,"keystrokes":335,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":57070,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":28,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Protecting your team's hours while cross-training systematically is a great way to maintain consistency and build team loyalty.\n\nAs the Store Manager for our new Lehigh Acres store, you will need to oversee opening, mid, and closing shifts, as well as handle emergencies on-site. \n\n**Do you have reliable personal transportation, and do you have fully open, flexible availability to meet the demands of opening and managing this new store?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes full open availability as well as my own vehicle"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":12346,"keystrokes":41,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":8859,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":49,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is great to hearâ€”having reliable transportation and open availability is crucial for launching a new store smoothly.\n\nNow, Iâ€™d like to put you in a realistic, high-pressure scenario on the floor to see your prioritization skills in action:\n\n**You are operating window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you honks asking for napkins. Walk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks.**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I tell whoever close to the window to politely hand out the napkins as I quickly finish the espresso station I then go help make the complex drinks and replace spots with whomever is in that window and send them to window A."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":105160,"keystrokes":265,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":50038,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":25,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you for walking me through that scenario, Madison. Clear delegation and prioritizing the customer right in front of you while managing ticket flow is key in our double drive-thru setup.\n\nAs we look toward opening this brand-new location, community connection is everything for establishing long-term customer loyalty.\n\n**What steps would you take in your first 30 to 60 days as Store Manager to build strong relationships with the Lehigh Acres community and ensure a successful grand opening?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Make the store homey comfortable build clientele and grabbing Lehigh attention to the well kept maintenance of inside and outside the store, my crew will enjoy work which makes the customers enjoy being there and able to relax maybe even read. Iâ€™m aiming for a very calm cozy environment"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":94615,"keystrokes":267,"maxInsertChunk":11,"responseDelayMs":12874,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":31,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Creating that welcoming, positive atmosphere will definitely leave a lasting impression on our guests! \n\nBecause the Ellianos model is strictly a double drive-thru kiosk with no indoor lobby seating for customers, every touchpoint happens right at the vehicle window in a matter of seconds.\n\n**How do you and your team deliver that warm, personal, and memorable customer connection strictly through quick 45-to-60-second drive-thru window interactions?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Respect is a very big thing as a drive thru employee, if you answer your headset positive and cheerful then the chances of the customer ordering more product which benefits us, I then as well reward and take care of my crew so they enjoy coming to work to make work enjoyable for they team and the customers"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":134639,"keystrokes":323,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":17815,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":26,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Setting the tone right from that very first headset greeting makes a world of difference in the drive-thru experience.\n\nInevitably, there will be times when an order is delayed or a customer is unhappy with their drink and expresses their frustration directly at the window. \n\n**Can you share your philosophy on handling customer complaints and de-escalating tense situations, and how do you use those moments as coaching opportunities for your team?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I always go by â€œLARPâ€ Listen,Apologize,Reassure, Provide"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":47583,"keystrokes":59,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":16113,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":9,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"The \"LARP\" method is a classic, structured framework for service recoveryâ€”listening actively and providing a clear solution turns a negative experience right around.\n\nAs a Store Manager, youâ€™ll also be conducting performance reviews and giving daily constructive feedback. \n\n**How do you approach having a difficult or corrective conversation with a team member who isn't meeting Ellianos' standards, and how do you follow up to ensure positive, long-term behavior change?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"If a team member isnâ€™t meeting standards I then have a conversation with them about what needs more attention, if then they still arenâ€™t meeting the standards I prepare for termination, while interviewing people for that position. Responsibilities is part of work, respect is part of work, if you donâ€™t have them then this job wonâ€™t work"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":105747,"keystrokes":301,"maxInsertChunk":12,"responseDelayMs":13390,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":32,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Maintaining high standards and holding team members accountable is essential for running a tight ship.\n\nIn a coffee drive-thru, product consistency hinges on equipment performanceâ€”like proper espresso machine calibration, grinder dial-ins, and strict food safety protocols (refrigeration temps, sanitation).\n\n**What is your routine for managing daily food safety checklists, cleanliness standards, and preventative equipment maintenance to ensure high quality and pass health inspections with flying colors?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I treat the store like home, there will be chores every shift to make sure maintenance is kept up with as well as cleaning. Having a unkept business thrives. To be able to assure the customers there health is important they would have to see for themselves"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":83211,"keystrokes":249,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":22904,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":34,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Treating the store with that level of pride and care sets a great example for your entire crew.\n\nTo keep a store performing at peak levels, Store Managers often track key performance indicators (KPIs)â€”such as average drive-thru window times, ticket averages, and daily sales targets. \n\n**How do you share performance goals and metrics with your team on a daily or weekly basis to keep them focused, engaged, and motivated to hit those targets?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"We will have monthly mandatory work meetings to talk about anything that may be bothering them or maybe things they need help with. If someone comes to me privately I speak with them afterwards privately. I make sure my team is in the correct head space and comfortable with their job"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":100814,"keystrokes":277,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":16531,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":30,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Open communication and monthly check-ins are great ways to keep the team aligned and supported.\n\nAs Store Manager, youâ€™ll also be the primary bridge between your team and the franchise owners/corporate leadership. You'll be responsible for reporting on weekly sales trends, labor performance, and store-level challenges while strictly upholding the Ellianos brand standards.\n\n**How do you approach regular communication and reporting with franchise owners, and how do you ensure your store consistently adheres to corporate standard operating procedures (SOPs)?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Every day before I leave my store I check EVERYTHING, days Iâ€™m supposed to have off I come in and suprise check how my crew is doing"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":44771,"keystrokes":140,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":20527,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":36,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Having that strong personal oversight and accountability definitely helps maintain high standards. \n\nBecause you can't be at the store 24/7, developing strong Shift Leaders and Assistant Managers is essential so the store runs at the exact same high standard even on your days off.\n\n**How do you train, empower, and delegate responsibility to your shift supervisors so that operations, speed, and customer service remain flawless when you aren't physically in the building?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I train them exactly how I was taught, it can go 2 ways, you can catch on or you canâ€™t. Iâ€™m looking for the strongest to be able to keep up with the hours and the speed of productivity, also has to know inventory very well as they will be trusted to keep up with truck"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":102384,"keystrokes":292,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":13799,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":33,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"In the fast-paced drive-thru and coffee industry, turnover can often be a major challenge for store managers. \n\n**What specific strategies do you use to keep team morale consistently high, build long-term loyalty, and retain great baristas so you aren't constantly in a cycle of hiring and retraining?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I take care of my team I make sure they are comfortable, I am running a safe space, everyone is going to understand every position therefor I can have a team member help with training"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":55668,"keystrokes":189,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":20315,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":38,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Cross-training your entire team to support each other and assist with onboarding certainly builds a collaborative culture.\n\nIn a fast-paced drive-thru, unexpected operational hiccups can happen at the worst timesâ€”such as an espresso machine malfunctioning or the POS system going offline during a peak morning rush.\n\n**How would you lead your team through an equipment or technical emergency like that to keep the drive-thru moving safely, minimize lost sales, and maintain a calm atmosphere for both your crew and waiting customers?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I tell them to please assure everyone we need their patience while we are experiencing a system malfunction I will offer alternative options"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":221140,"keystrokes":197,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":19188,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":6,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Clear communication and offering quick alternative solutions are key to keeping guests happy and orders flowing during tech issues.\n\nLooking ahead to the big picture: **What does a successful first year look like to you as the Store Manager of our new Lehigh Acres branchâ€”both for the store's business performance and for the culture of your team?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"A successful first year would be being able to tell a stranger I am the manager of the shop and the response I receive is â€œI love that placeâ€ being able to run a business people really enjoy. I want my crew to be proud of there employment"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":276089,"keystrokes":243,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":97776,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":10,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a wonderful vision, Madison. Having the community genuinely love the shop and having a team that takes true pride in their work is what the Ellianos brand is all about.\n\nWe have covered a lot of ground today regarding your leadership style, operations, and vision for Lehigh Acres. \n\nTo wrap up our interview today: **Why are you the ideal leader to launch this brand-new Ellianos location, and do you have any questions for us about the role, the store launch, or working with Ellianos Coffee?**"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I am very positive and excited to experience this I will make this a major achievement"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":110665,"keystrokes":63,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":90678,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":9,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you so much for your time, enthusiasm, and thoughtful responses today, Madison! Your positive energy, hands-on coffee background, and dedication to building a strong team culture really came through during our conversation.\n\nOur hiring team will be reviewing your interview responses as we finalize leadership selections for the new Lehigh Acres location. If your qualifications match our needs, we will reach out to you directly regarding the next steps in the process.\n\nTo officially finish and transmit your application, please go ahead and click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen now. \n\nWe appreciate your interest in Ellianos Coffee and wish you the very best! Have a wonderful day!"}]}],"secondInterviewScores":{"notes":{},"scores":{},"updatedAt":"2026-08-28T14:10:50.228Z"},"id":"1eed378e-d37f-4b20-a45f-cc751565b47b","position":"Store Manager","status":"Completed","emailSent":true,"evaluation":"### Final Evaluation: Madison Jurado â€“ Store Manager (Ellianos Coffee, Lehigh Acres)\n\n---\n\n### 1. Final Score: **82 / 100**\n\n---\n\n### 2. Summary of Strengths\n* **Industry Experience:** Brings six years of hands-on coffee industry experience, providing a solid foundational understanding of shop rhythms and barista expectations.\n* **Floor Leadership & Tactical Execution:** Demonstrates a willingness to jump into the trenches, prioritize drive-thru speed, and step into bottleneck positions during peak rushes.\n* **Service Recovery:** Accurately utilized the \"LARP\" (Listen, Apologize, Reassure, Provide) framework, showing a strong grasp of structured de-escalation.\n* **Positive Culture & Vision:** Expresses a clear desire to foster a welcoming, cozy environment and wants her crew to feel genuine pride in their workplace.\n* **Accountability:** Places a high value on operational compliance, checking details thoroughly and keeping strict standards regarding call-outs and waste management.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Summary of Weaknesses & Areas of Concern\n* **Misunderstanding of Physical Footprint:** In Response 10, the candidate suggested having team members \"maybe even read\" in a \"calm cozy environment.\" However, Ellianos is strictly an 800-square-foot double drive-thru kiosk with **no indoor lobby seating**, indicating a slight gap in understanding the specific physical model.\n* **Rigid Management Philosophy:** When discussing training and leadership development (Responses 13 and 21), the candidate stated, *\"I train them exactly how I was taught, it can go 2 ways, you can catch on or you canâ€™t.\"* This indicates a potentially rigid \"sink-or-swim\" coaching style rather than adapting to diverse learning needs.\n* **Labor & Break Management:** While strict adherence to breaks is important for labor, attributing bad labor *solely* to breaks oversimplifies labor percentage forecasting and scheduling efficiency.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Final Recommendation\n* **Recommendation:** **Second Interview**\n* **Reasoning:** Madison has great baseline coffee experience, high energy, and a strong work ethic. However, because this is a brand-new double drive-thru kiosk location in Lehigh Acres, a second interview should be used to clarify her understanding of the drive-thru-only format (addressing the lobby/reading misconception) and to evaluate her coaching flexibility (moving away from a \"sink-or-swim\" mentality).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Authenticity Assessment\n* **Average Confidence:** 98.6%\n* **Lowest-Confidence Answers:** \n  * Response 20 (92%)\n  * Response 21 (92%)\n  * Response 22 (92%)\n  *(Note: No answers fell below the 35% threshold.)*\n* **Writing-Style Analysis Agreement:** The writing-style analysis **agrees** with the confidence metrics. The candidate's typing metrics show natural human pacing, realistic response delays, and varied typing speeds without paste attempts or suspicious text insertions. The slightly lower confidence percentages on the final three questions correspond with longer response durations and tab switches (reflective of a candidate carefully pondering their final thoughts), but the linguistic register remains entirely consistent throughout the transcript.","candidateInfo":{"phone":"2399408254","name":"Madison jurado","email":"madisonroselynn04@gmail.com"},"date":"2026-08-21T20:16:17.536Z"},{"candidateInfo":{"phone":"2396747373","name":"Accounting Galiano's","email":"galianos.accntng@gmail.com"},"id":"71c9b923-3a35-4f10-ae30-8921b131e4ef","position":"Store Manager","date":"2026-08-20T20:04:02.433Z","status":"Incomplete","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Store Manager position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello, Accounting Galiano's! Welcome to your interview for the Store Manager position at our brand-new Ellianos Coffee location in Lehigh Acres, Florida. We are excited to learn more about you today.\n\nBefore we get started, I want to share a couple of quick details about how this interview works:\n* The full interview consists of a maximum of **25 questions**, asked one at a time.\n* You are in complete control of your pace. You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen, or you can simply tell me in the chat whenever you would like to wrap up.\n\nLetâ€™s start with an easy opening question:\n\n**What sparked your interest in joining the Ellianos Coffee team as our Store Manager in Lehigh Acres?**"}]}]},{"candidateInfo":{"phone":"2397859533","name":"Tacarra Thomas","email":"tacarra.thomas0530@gmail.com"},"emailSent":true,"status":"Completed","secondInterviewGuide":{"interviewerTips":["Exigir mÃ©tricas y procedimientos exactos; no aceptar respuestas genÃ©ricas como 'seguir las polÃ­ticas' o 'crear un checklist'.","Mantener un tono conversacional y no acusatorio al indagar sobre la ayuda externa o herramientas usadas durante la entrevista virtual.","Evaluar el dinamismo verbal, aplomo bajo presiÃ³n y agilidad mental necesarios para un modelo de alta velocidad ('Italian Quality at America's Pace')."],"decision":{"hire":"CalificaciÃ³n >= 4.0/5.0 en los Bloques 1, 2 y 3 (mustPass: true), demostrando dominio numÃ©rico en P&L/COGS, tÃ©cnicas de mediaciÃ³n de equipo, conocimientos tÃ©cnicos de espresso y fluidez en inglÃ©s >= 3.5 en la pregunta q8.","decline":"CalificaciÃ³n <= 2.0 en cualquiera de los bloques must-pass, incapacidad para explicar procedimientos reales de inventario/mantenimiento, inconsistencias Ã©ticas o falta de disponibilidad horaria para aperturas a las 4:30 AM.","thirdConversation":"DesempeÃ±o destacado en liderazgo cultural y servicio al cliente (Bloques 2 y 4 >= 4.0), pero con dudas intermedias en experiencia financiera o tÃ©cnica de equipos (Bloques 1 o 3 entre 2.5 y 3.5). Requiere entrevista tÃ©cnica adicional con el District Manager o Franchise Owner."},"blocks":[{"id":"block_1","title":"Experiencia Real y Control Financiero/Operativo","goal":"Verificar la experiencia real administrando costos, mermas de inventario y estado de resultados (P&L).","minutes":15,"mustPass":true,"questionIds":["q1","q2","q3"]},{"id":"block_2","title":"ResoluciÃ³n de Conflictos y Liderazgo de Equipo","goal":"Evaluar la madurez gerencial en mediaciÃ³n interpersonal y retenciÃ³n de talento antes de recurrir a