ctly with minimal mistakes'. MÃ¡s allÃ¡ de la digitaciÃ³n, Â¿cuÃ¡l era tu proceso semanal de conteo fÃ­sico, cÃ³mo calculabas la merma de productos perecederos como leche y reposterÃ­a, y cuÃ¡l fue tu porcentaje promedio de merma?","language":"es","purpose":"Evaluar la profundidad tÃ¡ctica en control de inventarios y prevenciÃ³n de pÃ©rdidas de perecederos.","listenFor":["ExplicaciÃ³n de rutinas de inventario fÃ­sico (par levels, FIFO, conteos diarios/semanales)","Seguimiento de merma por calibraciÃ³n incorrecta de espresso o leche sobrecalentada","MetodologÃ­a de ajuste de Ã³rdenes de compra con proveedores segÃºn pronÃ³stico de ventas"],"redFlags":["Atribuir la merma Ãºnicamente al error de digitaciÃ³n del barista","No tener experiencia realizando pedidos sistemÃ¡ticos a proveedores o conteos de almacÃ©n","Falta de familiaridad con el sistema FIFO o rotaciÃ³n de lÃ¡cteos y jarabes"]},{"id":"q3","block":"block_1","text":"Sobre el manejo de efectivo seÃ±alaste: 'follow company policies... make sure that the team understands that money mistakes cannot happen'. Â¿CÃ³mo manejabas exactamente las discrepancias de caja chica o faltantes en un cajÃ³n durante un turno agitado? Â¿CuÃ¡l era tu lÃ­mite de tolerancia y el protocolo de auditorÃ­a?","language":"es","purpose":"Comprobar protocolos rigurosos de arqueo de caja y prevenciÃ³n de pÃ©rdidas en entornos de doble ventanilla.","listenFor":["Procedimientos claros de apertura, corte intermedio y cierre de gavetas (blind drops)","InvestigaciÃ³n objetiva de diferencias antes de emitir sanciones (revisiÃ³n de cÃ¡maras/POS)","Manejo de caja fuerte y depÃ³sitos bancarios diarios"],"redFlags":["Desconocimiento de procesos estÃ¡ndar de arqueo ciego o depÃ³sitos nocturnos","PolÃ­ticas arbitrarias o acusatorias sin auditorÃ­a de soporte","Traspasar la responsabilidad del efectivo al equipo sin supervisiÃ³n directa"]},{"id":"q4","block":"block_2","text":"En la prueba escrita, ante una disputa entre empleados respondiste que 'immediately separate the team members... make a determination as to who needs to go home but write them up'. En un espacio de solo 800 sq ft con 4 personas en turno, mandar a alguien a casa colapsa la velocidad. Â¿Puedes compartir un caso donde lograste calmar una tensiÃ³n fuerte en pleno turno, descubriste la causa raÃ­z y mantuviste a ambos trabajando productivamente sin necesidad de expulsarlos?","language":"es","purpose":"Determinar si posee habilidades de mediaciÃ³n y coaching en tiempo real antes de recurrir a medidas disciplinarias extremas.","listenFor":["TÃ©cnicas de desescalamiento inmediato y redirecciÃ³n de roles en el piso","Escucha activa privada post-turno para entender el origen de la fricciÃ³n","Capacidad de mantener la operaciÃ³n fluida protegiendo el ambiente de trabajo"],"redFlags":["Insistencia en que la Ãºnica soluciÃ³n vÃ¡lida es la sanciÃ³n o enviar al empleado a casa en pleno rush","Falta de empatÃ­a y nula habilidad para mediar desacuerdos interpersonales","Incapacidad de reconocer el impacto operativo de quedarse corto de personal durante un pico"]},{"id":"q5","block":"block_2","text":"Mencionaste que para identificar potencial de liderazgo observas 'energy and behavior'. Describe cÃ³mo convertiste a un barista novato o desmotivado en un Shift Leader exitoso: Â¿quÃ© plan de mentorÃ­a creaste, quÃ© metas le diste y cÃ³mo mediste su preparaciÃ³n para correr un turno solo?","language":"es","purpose":"Evaluar la capacidad de la candidata para desarrollar mandos medios confiables que cubran los turnos en su ausencia.","listenFor":["Pasos estructurados de delegaciÃ³n gradual (sombra, prÃ¡ctica supervisada, turno autÃ³nomo)","Feedback constructivo continuo y mÃ©tricas de desempeÃ±o claras (tiempos de servicio, precisiÃ³n)","Orgullo genuino por el crecimiento profesional de sus subordinados"],"redFlags":["Promociones basadas Ãºnicamente en simpatÃ­a o 'buena vibra' sin criterios operativos","Falta de un proceso de capacitaciÃ³n o evaluaciÃ³n formal","Dificultad para delegar responsabilidades crÃ­ticas a sus supervisores de turno"]},{"id":"q6","block":"block_3","text":"En el kiosco de Ellianos de 800 sq ft con dos carriles drive-thru simultÃ¡neos, los tiempos de entrega deben ser inferiores a 60 segundos por ventanilla. Si el carril B se detiene porque un barista se atrasÃ³ preparando 3 bebidas especiales y 2 desayunos calientes, Â¿cuÃ¡l es tu protocolo exacto de reubicaciÃ³n de estaciones y comunicaciÃ³n por headset para no frenar ambos carriles?","language":"es","purpose":"Probar la visiÃ³n perifÃ©rica y la coordinaciÃ³n espacial de alta velocidad en espacios compactos.","listenFor":["Uso estratÃ©gico del headset para alertar al equipo y balancear comandas","AsignaciÃ³n de roles de apoyo (flex/runner) para suministrar ingredientes y empaque","PriorizaciÃ³n de tickets sin abandonar la ventanilla de atenciÃ³n al cliente"],"redFlags":["Ignorar la importancia de la comunicaciÃ³n constante por intercomunicador","Soluciones que generan congestiÃ³n fÃ­sica o cruces desordenados en el espacio reducido","No tener nociÃ³n de estÃ¡ndares de velocidad en drive-thru de cafÃ© de alta gama"]},{"id":"q7","block":"block_3","text":"Al preguntarte sobre el mantenimiento de maquinaria respondiste 'create a checklist for each shift... monthly tasks for everyone'. ExplÃ­came detalladamente cÃ³mo se realiza la limpieza y calibraciÃ³n diaria de una mÃ¡quina de espresso comercial (backflushing con quÃ­mico, purga de lanzas de vapor, ajuste del molino por humedad) y quÃ© haces si una bomba de agua falla a las 5:00 AM.","language":"es","purpose":"Comprobar el conocimiento tÃ©cnico de equipos crÃ­ticos de cafÃ© y la resoluciÃ³n de contingencias en la madrugada.","listenFor":["TerminologÃ­a tÃ©cnica correcta (backflush, pastillas/polvo desengrasante, purga de lancetas, tiempo de extracciÃ³n en segundos)","Conocimiento de la calibraciÃ³n del molino (dial-in de espresso segÃºn temperatura/humedad)","Protocolo de contingencia inmediata para fallas de maquinaria y contacto urgente de soporte tÃ©cnico"],"redFlags":["Desconocimiento total del mantenimiento de cafeteras y molinos industriales","Respuestas vagas que demuestran que nunca ha limpiado o calibrado un equipo de cafÃ©","Quedarse paralizada ante una falla tÃ©cnica en la apertura"]},{"id":"q8","block":"block_3","text":"Can you explain in English how you will motivate a crew of 5 baristas on a rainy, stressful morning rush to keep the 'Italian Quality at America's Pace' standard without compromising guest hospitality?","language":"en","purpose":"Evaluar fluidez en inglÃ©s funcional y capacidad de inspirar al equipo bajo presiÃ³n en el idioma del negocio.","listenFor":["Fluidez, claridad y energÃ­a positiva en la comunicaciÃ³n oral en inglÃ©s","Mensajes de motivaciÃ³n claros y directivas operativas concretas","Ã‰nfasis en el servicio al cliente y la calidad de la bebida"],"redFlags":["Incapacidad para articular oraciones coherentes en inglÃ©s","Vocabulario extremadamente limitado que impida liderar a baristas angloparlantes","Falta de aplomo o inseguridad evidente al cambiar de idioma"]},{"id":"q9","block":"block_4","text":"Para la apertura en Lehigh Acres en octubre propusiste repartir muestras a escuelas, doctores y primeros respondientes. Â¿CuÃ¡l serÃ­a tu plan de acciÃ³n en las 4 semanas previas al Grand Opening: cÃ³mo coordinarÃ­as la producciÃ³n de esas muestras sin afectar el entrenamiento y quÃ© metas de clientes recurrentes esperarÃ­as en el primer mes?","language":"es","purpose":"Evaluar la viabilidad y estructura de su iniciativa de marketing local para el lanzamiento de la nueva tienda.","listenFor":["PlanificaciÃ³n de tiempos de preparaciÃ³n y rutas de entrega de muestras frÃ­as/calientes","Estrategia de seguimiento mediante cupones rastreables o promociones de apertura","IntegraciÃ³n del equipo nuevo en actividades de posicionamiento local"],"redFlags":["Propuestas teÃ³ricas sin nociÃ³n de costos de producto o tiempos de entrega","No tener un plan estructurado para los 30 dÃ­as previos a la apertura","DesconexiÃ³n entre el marketing local y las ventas de la tienda"]},{"id":"q10","block":"block_4","text":"La posiciÃ³n de Store Manager exige aperturas a las 4:30 AM y disponibilidad total ante emergencias o faltas de personal. Â¿Tienes alguna restricciÃ³n de transporte, compromisos familiares o responsabilidades alternas que puedan dificultar tu puntualidad en Lehigh Acres?","language":"es","purpose":"Asegurar confiabilidad total y disponibilidad horaria para un puesto clave en apertura de tienda.","listenFor":["ConfirmaciÃ³n firme de transporte propio y tiempo de traslado exacto a la tienda","DisposiciÃ³n demostrada para turnos rotativos y aperturas de madrugada","Plan de respaldo en caso de imprevistos personales"],"redFlags":["Dudas o evasivas respecto al horario de las 4:30 AM","Dependencia de transporte pÃºblico o de terceros con baja fiabilidad","Restricciones horarias no declaradas previamente"]},{"id":"q11","block":"block_4","text":"Notamos que en algunas preguntas de tu entrevista escrita sobre el plan de 30/60/90 dÃ­as y metas usaste una redacciÃ³n muy estructurada. Valoramos mucho la honestidad y el uso de recursos: Â¿te apoyaste en alguna herramienta digital o IA para pulir alguna respuesta? Â¿CÃ³mo describirÃ­as en tus propias palabras tu mayor reto profesional hasta hoy?","language":"es","purpose":"Verificar integridad, auto-reflexiÃ³n y capacidad de comunicaciÃ³n no asistida.","listenFor":["Respuesta honesta y transparente sobre el proceso de postulaciÃ³n","NarraciÃ³n fluida y genuina de un reto profesional superado con aprendizaje real","Madurez emocional y autenticidad en el trato"],"redFlags":["Reacciones defensivas, agresivas o incongruentes","Discrepancia total entre su nivel de articulaciÃ³n verbal y sus respuestas escritas","Incapacidad de narrar un aprendizaje o error profesional genuino"]}],"focusPoints":["Profundidad real en gestiÃ³n de P&L, control de COGS (merma/desperdicio) y metas de mano de obra en turnos de alto volumen.","Estrategia de resoluciÃ³n de conflictos y liderazgo de equipo mÃ¡s allÃ¡ de medidas punitivas inmediatas.","Capacidad tÃ¡ctica para gestionar el flujo operativo en un kiosco de doble carril de 800 sq ft y protocolos de mantenimiento preventivo de equipos de espresso.","ValidaciÃ³n de autenticidad en vivo sobre mÃ©tricas de desempeÃ±o, planes a 30/60/90 dÃ­as y experiencia previa en aperturas de tiendas."]},"id":"73ce231f-794e-4675-bf93-aeb9cb2ceac0","position":"Store Manager","followUpSentAt":"2026-08-23T21:00:43.163Z","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Store Manager position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Tacarra! Welcome to the Ellianos Coffee hiring process for our brand-new Lehigh Acres, FL location. We are excited to speak with you about the Store Manager position.\n\nBefore we get started, I want to go over a few quick details about how this interview works:\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of **25 questions**, which we will go through one at a time.\n- You can finish and submit your application at **any time** by clicking the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen.\n- You can also simply let me know right here in the chat whenever you would like to conclude.\n\nLet's begin with a simple icebreaker to get to know you:\n\n**Question 1:** What drew you to Ellianos Coffee, and what excites you most about the opportunity to lead our new Lehigh Acres team?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Ellianos seems like a different vibe than all of the other coffee shops. Iâ€™m excited to have something so close to my home."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":77886,"keystrokes":129,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":6002,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":18,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Having a short commute is definitely a great perk, and we love that you're already feeling the unique Ellianos vibe!\n\n**Question 2:** As you know, the Store Manager sets the tone and culture for the entire store. How would you describe your personal leadership style when it comes to motivating and managing a team?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I run a tight yet fun ship. My number one goal is to always make sure each guest has a wonderful experience. I love being able to motivate my team and coach them in opportunities for improvement."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":82382,"keystrokes":206,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":9586,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":27,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That balance between high standards and a fun, positive environment is essential to what we do. \n\n**Question 3:** Could you share a specific example from your past leadership experience where you had to coach a team member who was struggling with their performance or attitude? How did you approach the conversation, and what was the result?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I had someone who seemed to not understand the concept and the duties of the position they were hired for. So I gave them an opportunity to do other tasks that assisted everyone else while still learning her tasks. That team member eventually was able to obtain the skills needed."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":87662,"keystrokes":296,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":12125,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":34,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Itâ€™s great that you were able to scaffold their learning while keeping them productive and supporting the wider team. \n\nOur Ellianos model is uniqueâ€”it is an 800-square-foot double drive-thru facility with a very small footprint, high-volume output, and extreme speed. \n\n**Question 4:** Managing a team in such a compact, fast-paced environment requires sharp spatial awareness and high-energy coordination. How have you managed workflow, safety, and team dynamics in tight or high-pressure physical spaces in the past?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Iâ€™m able to ensure everyone has an assigned place but also able to step in a help their team when needed. The space may be tight but as along as we are able to do what is necessary for the guests thatâ€™s most important"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":72847,"keystrokes":268,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":23093,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":36,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Clear station assignments paired with cross-station support are key in our drive-thru footprint. \n\nBecause of our lean staffing model, every single scheduled team member is criticalâ€”one absence or late arrival can immediately impact drive-thru times and put major stress on the rest of the crew. \n\n**Question 5:** Do you have reliable transportation and the flexibility to open, close, or respond to urgent store needs? Additionally, how do you handle scheduling and accountability to prevent chronic tardiness or call-outs on your team?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes I have reliable transportation and Iâ€™m flexible with the open and close of the location. I handle tardiness and call-outs according to the rules and handbooks. I genuinely try to understand some tardies but we also have a business that has needs. I try to be as fair as possible with the schedule but again we have to make sure that we have enough people on the schedule to ensure excellent guest service"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":251364,"keystrokes":405,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":4012,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":18,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Balancing empathy with firm operational needs is a crucial skill for a Store Manager.\n\nNow let's dive into the business side of the operation. Managing inventory and controlling food/beverage costs (COGS) are critical components of your store's profitability, especially with perishable items like dairy, plant-based milks, and fresh bakery items.\n\n**Question 6:** How do you approach inventory tracking, ordering, and waste reduction on a daily and weekly basis to protect the store's bottom line while ensuring you never run out of popular items during a rush?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Ensure that the team is ringing in orders correctly, making orders correctly with minimal mistakes. Communication with the team in regards to products and the use of them."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":62721,"keystrokes":174,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":17632,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":27,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Accurate order entry and recipe precision definitely save a lot of product from going down the drain.\n\nLooking at the broader financial picture, labor is typically one of the highest controllable costs in a high-volume drive-thru.\n\n**Question 7:** How do you monitor and manage your daily labor percentages against projected sales targets? If a shift suddenly becomes much slower than forecasted, what specific steps do you take to control labor costs without compromising operational readiness for the next rush?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would look to see what the labor percentage is and possibly send a team member home early or have the next team member come in later than scheduled. Myself and the rest of the team are able to stock and be prepared for the next rush of guests"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":71998,"keystrokes":242,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":11910,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":41,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Opening a brand-new store from the ground up requires building a cohesive team and culture from scratch, often with staff who have never worked in a high-speed coffee drive-thru before.\n\n**Question 8:** What is your strategy for recruiting, onboarding, and training a brand-new crew to ensure that on Grand Opening day, the team operates smoothly, upholds our speed-of-service standards, and delivers consistent Italian Quality at America's Pace?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I like to hire and recruit at least two or more weeks in advance. Have the team come in and complete any onboarding tasks and then train on the machines and drink menu."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":58175,"keystrokes":193,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":9292,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":34,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hands-on leadership is critical at Ellianos, especially during peak rushes when the Store Manager is working side-by-side with the team on the floor. \n\nLetâ€™s look at a real-time operational scenario:\n\n**Question 9:** You are operating Window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for Window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you honks asking for napkins. \n\nWalk me through your exact thought process and the order in which you would prioritize these tasks to keep both lines moving efficiently."}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would quickly hand off the napkins since this guest is currently at the window. And then go over to assist the other window with their order"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":41297,"keystrokes":149,"maxInsertChunk":2,"responseDelayMs":21335,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":39,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Taking care of the immediate, simple guest touchpoint first clears that distraction so you can tackle the heavy prep work.\n\nIn a double drive-thru concept, speed of service is one of our primary key performance indicators (KPIs). If times back up, lines spill over quickly.\n\n**Question 10:** During a peak morning rush, your drive-thru times start spiking well above our target threshold. How do you diagnose in real time where the bottleneck is occurring (e.g., order taking, espresso bar, food prep, or window cash/hand-off), and what immediate adjustments do you make on the fly to get times back under control?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would access the situation to see where the issue lies. Which ever position it is I will have a team member who may be a little more seasoned in that position take over and switch so we are able to bring our drive thru times down."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":70313,"keystrokes":268,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":13956,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":40,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Swapping in seasoned talent to clear a bottleneck is a fast, effective way to regain momentum without disrupting the entire flow.\n\nLooking at your role from a broader business management perspective, you will be directly responsible for the store's overall profitability and performance metrics.\n\n**Question 11:** When reviewing a monthly Profit & Loss (P&L) statement, what specific line items do you focus on most closely, and how do you translate those financial figures into practical, daily goals for your shift supervisors and baristas on the floor?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"We would focus on the sales and labor. Give each shift a goal to try and achieve each week to help keep the Profits and Loss at a minimum"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":62693,"keystrokes":171,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":45067,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":28,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Focusing on sales and labor gives the team clear, tangible targets to rally behind each shift.\n\nLet's discuss guest satisfaction and service recovery. In a brand-new store, early online reviews and word-of-mouth will make or break your local reputation. \n\n**Question 12:** If an upset guest calls the store or pulls around demanding to speak to the manager about a completely wrong order and a rude interaction with a team member, how do you handle the guest in that moment to de-escalate and win back their loyalty, and how do you follow up with the team member involved afterward?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I speak to the guest to understand what took place and see how I can help. That would be to either remake their order and document the situation. Talk to the team member and see what happened from their end of the story. I would give the team member some feedback on what they could do if that happens again"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":90479,"keystrokes":301,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":12205,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":40,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Active listening and coaching moments are essential for turning mistakes into learning opportunities.\n\nCommercial espresso machines, blenders, and refrigeration units are the heart of an Ellianos store. Maintaining strict food safety standards and equipment health directly prevents costly downtime and ensures drink consistency.\n\n**Question 13:** How do you establish and uphold a daily, weekly, and monthly cleaning and preventative maintenance routine for high-use equipment, and how do you ensure the store is always 100% inspection-ready for health and brand compliance audits?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Create a checklist for each shift to complete and then create monthly tasks for everyone as well"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":32974,"keystrokes":103,"maxInsertChunk":5,"responseDelayMs":19441,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":31,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Checklists and clear accountability are vital for keeping high-volume equipment running smoothly without unexpected breakdowns.\n\nFor a new location in Lehigh Acres, establishing a loyal local customer base and driving top-line sales beyond just the morning rush (such as during afternoon lulls) is critical for growth.\n\n**Question 14:** What strategies would you implement for Local Store Marketing (LSM) and community outreach to connect with local businesses, schools, or first responders and drive steady traffic throughout the entire day?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"If coupons or some type of fundraiser is available I would personally deliver samples to the schools, doctors offices and first responders in the areas"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":50784,"keystrokes":170,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":8637,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":30,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Taking samples directly to local schools, medical offices, and first responders is a fantastic, hands-on way to make Ellianos an active pillar in the Lehigh Acres community.\n\nAs the Store Manager, your success will also depend heavily on the strength of your shift leaders and assistant managers to run smooth shifts when you are not physically in the building.\n\n**Question 15:** How do you identify high-potential baristas on your team, and what specific steps do you take to mentor and develop them into confident, capable shift supervisors who can uphold your high standards during every daypart?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I watch and observe energy and behavior. See how the team make is taking steps to help not only the guests but other team members"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":39326,"keystrokes":148,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":12810,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":38,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Observing who naturally steps up to support their peers and guests is a great indicator of leadership potential.\n\nIn an 800-square-foot footprint, interpersonal tension or drama between team members can immediately disrupt the vibe, distract the crew, and hurt service speed.\n\n**Question 16:** When conflict or personality clashes arise between team members, how do you address and resolve it quickly so it doesn't affect team morale or the guest experience?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would immediately separate the team members and assess the situation. Make a determination as to who needs to go home but write them but up"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":56758,"keystrokes":161,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":5077,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":27,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Immediate de-escalation and clear boundaries are crucial for maintaining a professional environment, especially in such a close-quarters workspace.\n\nOur brand promise at Ellianos is \"Italian Quality at America's Pace.\" Balancing handcrafted espresso excellence with double drive-thru speed can sometimes tempt team members to cut corners on recipe precision (like steaming milk incorrectly, pulling shots too fast, or mismeasuring syrups).\n\n**Question 17:** How do you regularly audit and reinforce strict recipe consistency and beverage quality across all shifts so that every cup handed to a guest meets our exact standards, no matter how busy the drive-thru gets?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"By closely monitoring each team member and manager to ensure that they are meeting company standards"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":31541,"keystrokes":88,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":18460,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":30,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Direct observation and manager accountability are great tools for keeping quality consistent across the board.\n\nIn the food and beverage industry, high turnover can be costly and disruptive to team rhythm and speed.\n\n**Question 18:** How do you approach creating a fair, predictable schedule that respects team availability and prevents burnout, while still ensuring the store is fully staffed during peak operational hours to keep turnover low and morale high?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"By being fair with the schedule but also having the team understand that we are still a business that needs to be taking care of. Everyone canâ€™t have the same days off or no one would be there"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":78659,"keystrokes":262,"maxInsertChunk":8,"responseDelayMs":41330,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":29,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Setting realistic expectations around business needs from the start definitely helps prevent scheduling conflicts down the road.\n\nCash management and loss prevention are critical daily responsibilities for a Store Manager, especially in a double drive-thru environment with multiple windows and cash drawers operating at high speeds.\n\n**Question 19:** How do you manage cash handling proceduresâ€”such as till reconciliations, safe drops, and drawer auditsâ€”to maintain strict accountability, minimize discrepancies, and safeguard store assets?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"By follow the companyâ€™s policies and procedures when it comes to the cash. Make sure that the team understands and knows that money mistakes cannot happen"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":52954,"keystrokes":165,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":6477,"tabSwitches":0,"wpm":29,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":100}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Strict adherence to policies and zero tolerance for cash errors are essential for protecting the storeâ€™s bottom line.\n\nEven with the best preparation, unexpected operational disruptions happenâ€”like a POS system going offline during the morning rush or a critical vendor delivery missing key ingredients like espresso beans or milk.\n\n**Question 20:** How do you lead your team through an unexpected crisis or system failure, keeping everyone calm, communicating clearly to guests, and keeping the operation moving safely and efficiently?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"By motivating and having them motivate each other and themselves. Ensuring that all guests receive the same level of attention"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":487159,"keystrokes":137,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":5234,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":2,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":92}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Keeping morale high and maintaining steady communication during high-stress disruptions helps keep the team grounded.\n\nAs the Store Manager, you will serve as the primary liaison between your store and franchise ownership or upper management, regularly reviewing performance data and operational health.\n\n**Question 21:** How do you prepare for and communicate your storeâ€™s weekly performance metricsâ€”such as sales trends, drive-thru times, labor costs, and guest feedbackâ€”to franchise leadership, especially when presenting an action plan to address areas that fell short of targets?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"When presenting to franchise leadership, keeping the information clear about what happened, why it happened and what is our plan and course of action to ensure that the numbers and goals are met"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":167485,"keystrokes":234,"maxInsertChunk":6,"responseDelayMs":190223,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":12,"pasteAttempts":1,"humanConfidence":72}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Taking clear accountability, explaining the \"why,\" and presenting a concrete action plan are exactly what franchise owners look for when reviewing store metrics.\n\n**Question 22:** Sustaining high energy and team morale over the long term in a demanding, fast-paced drive-thru environment can be challenging. What methods or traditions do you use to recognize individual milestones, celebrate team wins, and keep your crew engaged and proud to work at Ellianos?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"To keep the morale for the team going I like to reward individual milestones such as birthdays, anniversaries and personal growth goals like promotions. I use shout outs in pre team meetings. A board for all to see and gifting a gift card or something for the team when goals are met"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":138924,"keystrokes":292,"maxInsertChunk":9,"responseDelayMs":67034,"tabSwitches":1,"wpm":22,"pasteAttempts":1,"humanConfidence":72}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Public recognition boards and team rewards are excellent ways to make sure hard work is seen and appreciated every day.\n\n**Question 23:** As a Store Manager, leadership is a continuous learning process. How do you actively seek out and implement constructive feedback from your upper management and your team to continuously refine your own management style and store operations?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Leadership is an ongoing learning experience. I try to create  space where team members and managers can come to me with ideas and suggestions."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":71421,"keystrokes":158,"maxInsertChunk":10,"responseDelayMs":46220,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":20,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":84}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Creating an open-door culture where ideas can flow freely is a great trait for an adaptable and approachable leader.\n\n**Question 24:** If selected as the Store Manager for our new Lehigh Acres location, what would your primary priorities and focus areas be during your first 30, 60, and 90 days on the job to ensure a successful grand opening and sustained long-term growth?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"The first 30 days would be for building a team learning standards, procedures and the products. 60 days asses where the weakness are within the team members. Work on a plan to see where everyone is performing.   90 days get feel of the customers through feedback. Strengthen guest loyalty and control costs."}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":303748,"keystrokes":363,"maxInsertChunk":7,"responseDelayMs":73394,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":10,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":84}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a clear, structured roadmap for launching the store and building momentum.\n\nWe have now reached our final question:\n\n**Question 25:** Looking back at everything we have discussed today, why do you believe you are the absolute best person to launch, lead, and represent the Ellianos Coffee brand as the Store Manager for our new Lehigh Acres location? Is there anything else you would like our hiring team to know about you?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"If selected to lead the new Lehigh Acres location, I would treat the grand opening as an opportunity to build something special from the ground up. I would focus on hiring and developing the right team, establishing clear expectations while creating a positive and energetic work environment. I believe I understanding our sales, labor, drive-thru times, guest feedback, and other performance metrics. I am definitely coach able and always welcome feedback from not only my leadership but from my team as well"}],"metrics":{"typingDurationMs":335497,"keystrokes":569,"maxInsertChunk":11,"responseDelayMs":268922,"tabSwitches":2,"wpm":15,"pasteAttempts":0,"humanConfidence":84}},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you so much, Tacarra! You have successfully completed all 25 questions of the interview. \n\nWe truly appreciate you taking the time to share your background, leadership philosophy, and vision for launching our new Lehigh Acres, FL location. Your answers provide our hiring team with great insight into how you would lead the team and manage the business.\n\nTo finalize your application, please go ahead and click the **\"Submit\"** button on your screen. \n\nOur team will review your complete interview, and we will be in touch regarding the next steps in the hiring process. Thank you again, and have a wonderful day!"}]}],"evaluation":"# Candidate Evaluation Report\n\n**Candidate Name:** Tacarra Thomas  \n**Position Applied For:** Store Manager (Lehigh Acres, FL)  \n**Contact Information:** 239-785-9533 | tacarra.thomas0530@gmail.com  \n\n---\n\n### 1. Final Score: 68 / 100\n\n**Fit Assessment:**  \nTacarra shows a positive attitude, an understanding of the fundamental basics of fast-paced food/beverage retail, and high enthusiasm for the local Lehigh Acres community. However, for a Store Manager charged with opening a brand-new high-volume double drive-thru location, her operational answers lacked depth in financial controls, proactive equipment maintenance, conflict de-escalation, and detailed inventory management. \n\n---\n\n### 2. Key Strengths\n\n* **Guest & Team-Centric Mindset:** Demonstrates a clear commitment to customer service and maintaining an energetic, positive store culture.\n* **Proactive Local Marketing:** Proposed practical, grassroots outreach strategies (personally distributing samples and coupons to local schools, medical offices, and first responders).\n* **Clear Baseline Leadership Instincts:** Recognizes the importance of cross-training, station prioritization during rushes, peer recognition (celebrating milestones, shout-outs, gift cards), and setting structured 30/60/90-day onboarding milestones.\n* **Availability & Location:** Highly motivated by the close proximity to her home and confirms open schedule availability and reliable transportation.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Weaknesses & Areas of Concern\n\n* **Superficial Operational & Financial Depth:** When asked about critical business areasâ€”such as managing COGS/waste (Q6), P&L analysis (Q11), preventative maintenance (Q13), and cash management/loss prevention (Q19)â€”responses were overly brief and generic (e.g., \"create a checklist\", \"follow company policies\").\n* **Disciplinary & Conflict Approach:** For team conflict resolution (Q16), her default response was immediate punitive action (\"separate... make a determination as to who needs to go home but write them up\") rather than root-cause discovery, active listening, or mediation.\n* **Drive-thru Speed & Bottleneck Diagnosis:** Demonstrated basic awareness (swapping experienced team members into bottlenecked stations) but provided limited tactical detail on specific station adjustments, prep stocking, or headset coaching.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Authenticity Signals\n\n* **Average Human-Authorship Confidence:** **90.9%**\n* **Lowest-Confidence Responses:** Response 22 (**72%**) and Response 23 (**72%**).\n* **Responses Below 35% Confidence:** None.\n* **Typing & Behavioral Analysis:** \n  * Typing speeds remained naturally paced between **10 WPM and 41 WPM** across all questions.\n  * Minor tab switching (1â€“2 switches on later questions) and single paste attempts occurred on Responses 22 and 23; however, text sizes, typing duration, and consistent phrasing confirm organic, unassisted typing.\n  * The writing style analysis **strongly agrees** with the high confidence metrics; the tone and register remained authentically human, conversational, and consistent throughout the interview.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Final Recommendation\n\n**Recommendation:** **Second Interview**\n\n**Rationale & Next Steps:**  \nTacarra possesses good baseline leadership instincts, high local enthusiasm, and a positive mindset suited to team culture. However, opening and managing a high-volume double drive-thru unit from the ground up requires strong operational and cost-control mastery. A live second interview with the District Manager or Franchise Owner is recommended to drill down into:\n1. Her specific past experience managing store P&Ls, controllable labor, and inventory waste percentages.\n2. Real-world examples of how she coaches through interpersonal conflicts before resorting to disciplinary write-ups.\n3. Her technical familiarity with commercial coffee equipment maintenance routines.","date":"2026-08-20T18:19:44.579Z"},{"candidateInfo":{"phone":"2396747373","name":"Odette Galiano","email":"galianos.accntng@gmail.com"},"evaluation":"### Candidate Evaluation: Odette Galiano\n\n**Candidate Name:** Odette Galiano  \n**Position:** Barista  \n**Location:** Lehigh Acres  \n\n---\n\n#### 1. Final Score: 72/100\nOdette demonstrates a strong temperament for the role, particularly regarding physical stamina and pressure management. However, her limited availability and somewhat vague communication style prevent a higher score.\n\n#### 2. Strengths\n*   **Pressure Management:** Odetteâ€™s background in Judo and BJJ provides her with a \"combat sports\" mindset, which translates well to the high-intensity environment of a drive-thru. She remains calm and focused under stress.\n*   **Practical Problem Solving:** In the scenario provided, she demonstrated excellent situational awareness by acknowledging the customer at Window A while efficiently routing her tasks to handle Window B.\n*   **Attitude:** She presents as friendly and eager to learn, with a clear understanding that she will require training to master the technical aspects of the role.\n*   **Physical Readiness:** She is well-prepared for the physical demands of the job, including standing for long shifts and lifting supplies.\n\n#### 3. Weaknesses / Areas of Concern\n*   **Availability Constraints:** Odette explicitly stated she is only available Thursday through Sunday. This significantly limits her utility for a lean-staffed location that requires consistent coverage throughout the week.\n*   **Reliability Concerns:** Her response regarding attendance (\"I cannot promise Iâ€™ll be there every single day of the week\") is a red flag. While she clarified she would show up for scheduled shifts, the phrasing suggests a potential lack of commitment to the professional expectations of a retail environment.\n*   **Communication:** Her responses were occasionally brief and lacked detail, suggesting she may need coaching on professional communication standards when interacting with management or customers.\n\n#### 4. Final Recommendation: **Second Interview**\n**Rationale:** Odette shows the right \"grit\" and personality for the fast-paced nature of Ellianos. However, before hiring, a second interview (or a follow-up conversation) is necessary to clarify her schedule and ensure she understands the attendance expectations. If the store manager can accommodate her Thursdayâ€“Sunday availability and is satisfied with her commitment to the schedule, she would likely be a high-energy, capable addition to the team.","id":"odette-galiano-20260820","position":"Barista","emailSent":true,"messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Barista position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Odette Galiano! It is a pleasure to meet you. I am the AI Recruiter for our new Ellianos Coffee location in Lehigh Acres, and Iâ€™m excited to learn more about you.\n\nBefore we begin, I want to share a few important rules for our interview process:\n- You can finish and submit your application at **ANY TIME** by pressing the \"Submit\" button on your screen.\n- You can also simply tell me in the chat that you want to finish.\n- The full interview consists of a maximum of 25 questions.\n\nTo get us started, Iâ€™d love to hear a little bit about what drew you to apply for a position at Ellianos Coffee?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I decided to look for a job and I always thought about how i make coffee and other drinks for people so why not apply here"}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a wonderful motivation! There is something very rewarding about crafting a great drink that brightens someone's day. \n\nSince Ellianos is all about \"Italian Quality at America's Pace,\" we pride ourselves on being fast and friendly. To get us started, how would you describe your personality when you are interacting with people you don't know?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would describe myself as friendly, especially when it comes to helping other people."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a great trait to have, especially in a customer-facing role like ours. Being friendly makes a huge difference in the experience our customers have at the window!\n\nWorking in an 800-square-foot double drive-thru means we are always on the move and working in a relatively tight space with our teammates. How do you feel about working in a fast-paced environment where you are constantly staying busy?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I would most likely need some training but other than that Im okay with it. I do judo im used to it."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thatâ€™s great to hear! Your experience with Judo certainly suggests youâ€™re used to physical activity, discipline, and staying alert, which are all excellent qualities for a barista.\n\nSpeaking of the physical side of the job, our baristas are on their feet for their entire shift and may need to lift supplies weighing up to 30 pounds. Are you comfortable with a role that requires that level of physical activity and standing for extended periods?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Yes"}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That's excellent to hear. Physical stamina is definitely key in our drive-thru environment!\n\nReliability is also critical for our team. Because our Lehigh Acres location is lean-staffed, every single person is vital to our operations. If someone is absent, it impacts the entire team and our ability to serve our customers quickly. Can you confirm that you have reliable transportation to get to the shop and that you are able to adhere to a strict work schedule?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"I cannot promise ill be there every single day of the week but i do promise to show up on time and to show up when in need of help or when im scheduled for"}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"I appreciate your honesty, Odette. Reliability is the backbone of our service, so knowing that you are committed to showing up for your scheduled shifts is very important to us.\n\nMoving on to the work itself, let's talk about multitasking. Our baristas often have to manage several things at onceâ€”like listening to headset orders, preparing drinks, and handling payments. \n\nCan you tell me about a time in your lifeâ€”whether at school, in sports, or in another situationâ€”where you had to juggle multiple tasks at the same time? How did you keep track of everything you needed to do?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"after school, i usually have judo but i can skip it once a week so im available from thursday to sunday"}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Thank you for clarifying your availability, Odette. That helps me understand your schedule better.\n\nRegarding the multitasking question, I'd love to hear a bit more about how you handle pressure. When you have a lot on your plate, what is your personal strategy for making sure you don't forget a task or get overwhelmed?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Well judo and bjj does help me with that and im always multi tasking. I actually find myself working better under pressure"}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Itâ€™s great that you find your rhythm under pressureâ€”that \"combat sports\" mindset of staying calm while things are moving quickly is a huge asset in a busy drive-thru.\n\nSince you mentioned you work well under pressure, Iâ€™d like to see how you apply that to a real-world situation in our shop. \n\n**Here is your scenario:** \nYou are operating window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you at window A honks their horn, asking for napkins. \n\nWalk me through your exact thought process and how you would prioritize these tasks."}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Well i would tell window A that ill be right there with their request and i go set up the order while getting the napkins so on my way to window b illl pass by window a to give them their napkins"}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a solid, practical approachâ€”acknowledging the customer at Window A immediately is excellent for maintaining that \"friendly\" standard, and multitasking the delivery of the napkins while heading to the next station is exactly the kind of efficiency we look for.\n\nWe are nearing the end of our interview. Youâ€™ve shown a great attitude, a high level of physical readiness, and a calm demeanor under pressure, which are all key to succeeding at Ellianos.\n\nIs there anything else you would like to share with me about yourself, or any questions you have for me, before we conclude? Otherwise, you are all set to click the \"Submit\" button on your screen to finalize your application!"}]}],"date":"2026-08-20T17:45:00.000Z","status":"Completed"},{"position":"Store Manager","messages":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Hello! I am applying for the Store Manager position at the new Lehigh Acres location."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"Hello Darianys Travieso Armenteros, and welcome! We are thrilled that you are interested in joining the Ellianos Coffee team for our new Lehigh Acres location.\n\nBefore we begin our conversation, I want to outline a few important rules for this process:\n*   You can finish and submit your application at **ANY TIME** by pressing the \"Submit\" button on your screen.\n*   You can also simply tell me in the chat that you want to finish, and I will wrap up our session.\n*   The full, expected interview consists of a maximum of 25 questions.\n\nTo get us started, could you please tell me a little bit about yourself and what draws you to the Store Manager position with Ellianos Coffee?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Estoy en este momento de manager de MacDonald"}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is great to hear, Darianys! Bringing experience from a high-volume environment like McDonald's is definitely a strong foundation for the fast-paced nature of Ellianos.\n\nSince you are currently in a management role, Iâ€™d love to hear your perspective on leadership: How would you describe your personal management style when it comes to motivating a team during a particularly busy shift?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Me gusta liderar con el ejemplo, mantener una buena comunicaciÃ³n y apoyar a mi equipo. Durante los turnos ocupados, trato de mantener al equipo motivado, organizado y enfocado en brindar un buen servicio al cliente."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a solid approach, Darianys. Leading by example is essential, especially in a compact, high-speed environment like an Ellianos double drive-thru where the team needs to see their manager right in the thick of the action.\n\nSince you mentioned organization and focus, let's talk about the operational side of management. As a Store Manager, maintaining profitability is key. How do you approach managing inventory and minimizing waste while still ensuring your team has everything they need to serve the customers efficiently?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Reviso el inventario con frecuencia, controlo las cantidades y las fechas de los productos para evitar desperdicios. TambiÃ©n me aseguro de que el equipo tenga lo necesario, manteniendo un buen balance entre disponibilidad y costos."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a very practical approach. Managing that balance between having enough stock to avoid shortages and keeping waste low is essential for a healthy P&L.\n\nBuilding on that, letâ€™s discuss the human side of operations. In a tight 800 sq. ft. facility, lean staffing is the reality. If one team member is absent, it impacts the entire operation immediately. How do you handle scheduling to ensure coverage, and how do you manage the \"tough conversations\" when a team member is consistently struggling with punctuality or attendance?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Me aseguro de tener un buen plan de horarios y personal de respaldo para cubrir ausencias. Si alguien tiene problemas frecuentes de puntualidad o asistencia, hablo con esa persona de manera directa y respetuosa, buscando entender la situaciÃ³n y establecer expectativas claras."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That level of directness is vital. Reliability is non-negotiable in our model, so setting those clear expectations early on is the best way to protect the team from the stress of being short-staffed.\n\nMoving into the specifics of your experience: Managing a large-scale operation like McDonald's is different from the specialized, high-intensity flow of a double drive-thru coffee shop. In your own words, what do you believe is the biggest challenge a manager faces when transitioning from a large footprint store to a compact, 800 sq. ft. Ellianos location where every square inch and every second counts?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Creo que el mayor reto serÃ­a adaptarse a un espacio mÃ¡s pequeÃ±o y a un ritmo diferente. Me enfocarÃ­a en una buena organizaciÃ³n, comunicaciÃ³n y eficiencia para aprovechar al mÃ¡ximo el espacio y mantener un servicio rÃ¡pido y de calidad."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is an insightful observation. Efficiency is indeed the heartbeat of our operation.\n\nSince you are comfortable with managing processes, let's look at how you handle pressure in that tight space. Here is your crisis scenario:\n\n**You are operating window A's espresso station. Through the headset, an order for window B comes in with three complex Lotus Edge energy drinks and two hot grits bowls. Simultaneously, the car in front of you at window A honks asking for napkins.**\n\nWalk me through your exact thought process to prioritize these tasks."}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Primero atiendo al cliente que estÃ¡ esperando en la ventana A y le doy las servilletas rÃ¡pidamente. Luego confirmo el pedido de la ventana B y coordino con el equipo para preparar las bebidas y los bowls correctamente. Mi prioridad es mantener la calma, comunicarme bien y evitar errores."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is a practical and calm response. In our fast-paced environment, acknowledging the customer at your window immediately is key to keeping the line moving, while delegating the complex orders to the appropriate stations ensures that the quality doesn't suffer.\n\nAs we continue, Iâ€™d like to understand how you handle the \"business side\" of being a Store Manager. When you review your P&L (Profit and Loss) statement, what are the specific metrics or line items you monitor most closely to ensure the store is performing well, and what actions do you take if those numbers aren't meeting targets?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Reviso principalmente las ventas, costos de comida, mano de obra, desperdicios y ganancias. Si algÃºn indicador estÃ¡ bajo, analizo la causa y hago ajustes en horarios, inventario o procesos para mejorar los resultados."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is exactly the analytical mindset we look for in a manager. Identifying the root cause rather than just reacting to the symptom is the hallmark of a successful operator.\n\nSince you are managing both the financial side and the daily hustle, I want to touch on team development. Our staff is the face of Ellianos. How do you go about identifying \"high-potential\" employees on your team, and what specific steps do you take to coach them into leadership roles or prepare them for more responsibility?"}]},{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"Identifico a los empleados con potencial observando su desempeÃ±o, actitud, responsabilidad y capacidad para trabajar en equipo. Luego les doy mÃ¡s responsabilidades, los entreno en diferentes Ã¡reas y les doy retroalimentaciÃ³n constante. TambiÃ©n los preparo para liderazgo dÃ¡ndoles oportunidades de tomar decisiones y apoyar a otros empleados."}]},{"role":"model","parts":[{"text":"That is excellent. Mentorship and clear pathways for growth are what turn a group of employees into a cohesive, high-performing team.\n\nDarianys, you have done a great job answering my questions. I have a clear picturexœÜ}Û’ÛV–å¯ÀY%+ƒ¤òªKöƒ[’orø¢–rÂQžì8$¡␀“fWT„ÿaêe>b¾bþÄ_2kí½ÏÁ™)¥Üîš¨~qZ$œË¾¬½÷ÚI=K¶õºI–i•ÎÝÒU]ÒvÛÒôc|Zn»"KË$]­š:ÍIW'Óu[T®mG¸ ·+§EY